    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-2ba",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "2BA Application of Parts IV and IVA to local government bodies",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-2ba"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.30",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Parts IV and IVA apply in relation to a local government body only\nto the extent that it carries on a business, either directly or by an\nincorporated company in which it has a controlling interest.\n\nPreliminary  Chapter 1\nPreliminary  Part I\n\nSection 2C\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(2) In this section:\nlocal government body means a body established by or under a law\nof a State or Territory for the purposes of local government, other\nthan a body established solely or primarily for the purposes of\nproviding a particular service, such as the supply of electricity or\nwater.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Parts IV and IVA apply in relation to a local government body only\nto the extent that it carries on a business, either directly or by an\nincorporated company in which it has a controlling interest.\n\nPreliminary  Chapter 1\nPreliminary  Part I\n\nSection 2C\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(2) In this section:\nlocal government body means a body established by or under a law\nof a State or Territory for the purposes of local government, other\nthan a body established solely or primarily for the purposes of\nproviding a particular service, such as the supply of electricity or\nwater.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-2ba-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-2ba-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c6e12817745bd8d22ecc2350f13213884800042148a41543f4b4615296df27c8"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-2ba",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "2BA Application of Parts IV and IVA to local government bodies",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 30,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Parts IV and IVA apply in relation to a local government body only\nto the extent that it carries on a business, either directly or by an\nincorporated company in which it has a controlling interest.\n\nPreliminary  Chapter 1\nPreliminary  Part I\n\nSection 2C\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(2) In this section:\nlocal government body means a body established by or under a law\nof a State or Territory for the purposes of local government, other\nthan a body established solely or primarily for the purposes of\nproviding a particular service, such as the supply of electricity or\nwater."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-2ba-ss-1",
