    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 Interpretation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.33",
      "values:originalText": "(1) In this Act, unless the contrary intention appears:\naccountable authority has the same meaning as in the Public\nGovernance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013.\nAccreditation Registrar means:\n\n(a) if a person holds an appointment under\nsubsection 56CK(1)—that person; or\n\n(b) otherwise—the Commission.\naccredited action initiator has the meaning given by\nsection 56AMC.\naccredited data recipient has the meaning given by section 56AK.\naccredited person means a person who holds an accreditation\nunder subsection 56CA(1).\nACMA means the Australian Communications and Media\nAuthority.\nacquire includes:\n\n(a) in relation to goods—acquire by way of purchase, exchange\nor taking on lease, on hire or on hire-purchase; and\n\n(b) in relation to services—accept.\nacquisition determination, in respect of a notification of an\nacquisition, means:\n\n(a) a determination made under subsection 51ABZE(1) in\nrespect of the notification; or\n\nChapter 1  Preliminary",
      "skos:definition": "(1) In this Act, unless the contrary intention appears:\naccountable authority has the same meaning as in the Public\nGovernance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013.\nAccreditation Registrar means:\n\n(a) if a person holds an appointment under\nsubsection 56CK(1)—that person; or\n\n(b) otherwise—the Commission.\naccredited action initiator has the meaning given by\nsection 56AMC.\naccredited data recipient has the meaning given by section 56AK.\naccredited person means a person who holds an accreditation\nunder subsection 56CA(1).\nACMA means the Australian Communications and Media\nAuthority.\nacquire includes:\n\n(a) in relation to goods—acquire by way of purchase, exchange\nor taking on lease, on hire or on hire-purchase; and\n\n(b) in relation to services—accept.\nacquisition determination, in respect of a notification of an\nacquisition, means:\n\n(a) a determination made under subsection 51ABZE(1) in\nrespect of the notification; or\n\nChapter 1  Preliminary",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-4-logic-deontic-1"
        },
