      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:DescriptionLogic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "=",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Definition of Acquire",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::dl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "acquire includes: (a) in relation to goods—acquire by way of purchase, exchange or taking on lease, on hire or on hire-purchase; and (b) in relation to services—accept.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Acquire means to acquire goods through purchase, exchange, or lease, or to accept a service."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-4a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4A Subsidiary, holding and related bodies corporate",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-4a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.57",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Act, a body corporate shall, subject to\nsubsection (3), be deemed to be a subsidiary of another body\ncorporate if:\n\n(a) that other body corporate:\n\n(i) controls the composition of the board of directors of the\nfirst-mentioned body corporate;\n\n(ii) is in a position to cast, or control the casting of, more\nthan one-half of the maximum number of votes that\nmight be cast at a general meeting of the first-mentioned\nbody corporate; or\n\n(iii) holds more than one-half of the allotted share capital of\nthe first-mentioned body corporate (excluding any part\nof that allotted share capital that carries no right to\nparticipate beyond a specified amount in a distribution\nof either profits or capital); or\n\n(b) the first-mentioned body corporate is a subsidiary of any\nbody corporate that is that other body corporate’s subsidiary\n(including any body corporate that is that other body\ncorporate’s subsidiary by another application or other\napplications of this paragraph).\n\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), the composition of a body\ncorporate’s board of directors shall be deemed to be controlled by\n\nChapter 1  Preliminary",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of this Act, a body corporate shall, subject to\nsubsection (3), be deemed to be a subsidiary of another body\ncorporate if:\n\n(a) that other body corporate:\n\n(i) controls the composition of the board of directors of the\nfirst-mentioned body corporate;\n\n(ii) is in a position to cast, or control the casting of, more\nthan one-half of the maximum number of votes that\nmight be cast at a general meeting of the first-mentioned\nbody corporate; or\n\n(iii) holds more than one-half of the allotted share capital of\nthe first-mentioned body corporate (excluding any part\nof that allotted share capital that carries no right to\nparticipate beyond a specified amount in a distribution\nof either profits or capital); or\n\n(b) the first-mentioned body corporate is a subsidiary of any\nbody corporate that is that other body corporate’s subsidiary\n(including any body corporate that is that other body\ncorporate’s subsidiary by another application or other\napplications of this paragraph).\n\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), the composition of a body\ncorporate’s board of directors shall be deemed to be controlled by\n\nChapter 1  Preliminary",
