    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-4b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4B Consumers",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-4b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.60",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Act, unless the contrary intention appears,\na person is taken to have acquired particular goods or services as a\nconsumer if the person would be taken to have acquired the goods\nor services as a consumer under section 3 of the Australian\nConsumer Law.\n\n(2) If it is alleged in:\n\n(a) any proceeding under this Act; or\n\n(b) any other proceeding in respect of a matter arising under this\nAct;\nthat a person was a consumer in relation to particular goods or\nservices, it is presumed, unless the contrary is established, that the\nperson was a consumer in relation to those goods or services.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of this Act, unless the contrary intention appears,\na person is taken to have acquired particular goods or services as a\nconsumer if the person would be taken to have acquired the goods\nor services as a consumer under section 3 of the Australian\nConsumer Law.\n\n(2) If it is alleged in:\n\n(a) any proceeding under this Act; or\n\n(b) any other proceeding in respect of a matter arising under this\nAct;\nthat a person was a consumer in relation to particular goods or\nservices, it is presumed, unless the contrary is established, that the\nperson was a consumer in relation to those goods or services.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-4b-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-4b-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9e4931534dd82192fdd87d4c638e24c52a374fb6ff7026183a86ea81892e5cbd"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-4b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4B Consumers",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 60,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Act, unless the contrary intention appears,\na person is taken to have acquired particular goods or services as a\nconsumer if the person would be taken to have acquired the goods\nor services as a consumer under section 3 of the Australian\nConsumer Law.\n\n(2) If it is alleged in:\n\n(a) any proceeding under this Act; or\n\n(b) any other proceeding in respect of a matter arising under this\nAct;\nthat a person was a consumer in relation to particular goods or\nservices, it is presumed, unless the contrary is established, that the\nperson was a consumer in relation to those goods or services."
    },
