      },
      "cml:premiseText": "If it is alleged in any proceeding under this Act or other proceeding in respect of a matter arising under this Act.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "That the person was a consumer in relation to particular goods or services."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-4c",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4C Acquisition, supply and re-supply",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-4c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.60",
      "values:originalText": "In this Act, unless the contrary intention appears:\n\n(a) a reference to the acquisition of goods includes a reference to\nthe acquisition of property in, or rights in relation to, goods\nin pursuance of a supply of the goods;\n\n(b) a reference to the supply or acquisition of goods or services\nincludes a reference to agreeing to supply or acquire goods or\nservices;\n\n(c) a reference to the supply or acquisition of goods includes a\nreference to the supply or acquisition of goods together with\nother property or services, or both;\n\n(d) a reference to the supply or acquisition of services includes a\nreference to the supply or acquisition of services together\nwith property or other services, or both;\n\n(e) a reference to the re-supply of goods acquired from a person\nincludes a reference to:\n\n(i) a supply of the goods to another person in an altered\nform or condition; and\n\n(ii) a supply to another person of goods in which the\nfirst-mentioned goods have been incorporated;\n\nPreliminary  Chapter 1\nPreliminary  Part I\n\nSection 4E\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(f) a reference to the re-supply of services (the original services)\nacquired from a person (the original supplier) includes a\nreference to:\n\n(i) a supply of the original services to another person in an\naltered form or condition; and\n\n(ii) a supply to another person of other services that are\nsubstantially similar to the original services, and could\nnot have been supplied if the original services had not\nbeen acquired by the person who acquired them from\nthe original supplier.",
      "skos:definition": "In this Act, unless the contrary intention appears:\n\n(a) a reference to the acquisition of goods includes a reference to\nthe acquisition of property in, or rights in relation to, goods\nin pursuance of a supply of the goods;\n\n(b) a reference to the supply or acquisition of goods or services\nincludes a reference to agreeing to supply or acquire goods or\nservices;\n\n(c) a reference to the supply or acquisition of goods includes a\nreference to the supply or acquisition of goods together with\nother property or services, or both;\n\n(d) a reference to the supply or acquisition of services includes a\nreference to the supply or acquisition of services together\nwith property or other services, or both;\n\n(e) a reference to the re-supply of goods acquired from a person\nincludes a reference to:\n\n(i) a supply of the goods to another person in an altered\nform or condition; and\n\n(ii) a supply to another person of goods in which the\nfirst-mentioned goods have been incorporated;\n\nPreliminary  Chapter 1\nPreliminary  Part I\n\nSection 4E\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(f) a reference to the re-supply of services (the original services)\nacquired from a person (the original supplier) includes a\nreference to:\n\n(i) a supply of the original services to another person in an\naltered form or condition; and\n\n(ii) a supply to another person of other services that are\nsubstantially similar to the original services, and could\nnot have been supplied if the original services had not\nbeen acquired by the person who acquired them from\nthe original supplier.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-4c-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-4c-logic-descriptionlogic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-4c-logic-deontic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1dcbc2b660f9c7c5a800d10b3650ae2250e58824f1a6a8a6e0e5550031b6946a",
      "skos:note": "Definitions for acquisition, supply and re-supply of goods and services."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-4c",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4C Acquisition, supply and re-supply",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 60,
      "values:originalText": "In this Act, unless the contrary intention appears:\n\n(a) a reference to the acquisition of goods includes a reference to\nthe acquisition of property in, or rights in relation to, goods\nin pursuance of a supply of the goods;\n\n(b) a reference to the supply or acquisition of goods or services\nincludes a reference to agreeing to supply or acquire goods or\nservices;\n\n(c) a reference to the supply or acquisition of goods includes a\nreference to the supply or acquisition of goods together with\nother property or services, or both;\n\n(d) a reference to the supply or acquisition of services includes a\nreference to the supply or acquisition of services together\nwith property or other services, or both;\n\n(e) a reference to the re-supply of goods acquired from a person\nincludes a reference to:\n\n(i) a supply of the goods to another person in an altered\nform or condition; and\n\n(ii) a supply to another person of goods in which the\nfirst-mentioned goods have been incorporated;\n\nPreliminary  Chapter 1\nPreliminary  Part I\n\nSection 4E\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(f) a reference to the re-supply of services (the original services)\nacquired from a person (the original supplier) includes a\nreference to:\n\n(i) a supply of the original services to another person in an\naltered form or condition; and\n\n(ii) a supply to another person of other services that are\nsubstantially similar to the original services, and could\nnot have been supplied if the original services had not\nbeen acquired by the person who acquired them from\nthe original supplier."
    },
