      "skos:definition": "(5) To avoid doubt, a right to sue is taken not to be personal property\nfor the purposes of subsection (3).\n\nPreliminary  Chapter 1\nThe Australian Competition and Consumer Commission  Part II\n\nSection 7\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-6a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-6a-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-6a-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "de12e91be0c553f50fe7729e2c806527cb365061751ab644a3a30bec87d46d87",
      "skos:note": "Right to sue is not personal property for the purposes of subsection (3)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-6a-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6A(5) Establishment of Commission",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 76,
      "values:originalText": "(5) To avoid doubt, a right to sue is taken not to be personal property\nfor the purposes of subsection (3).\n\nPreliminary  Chapter 1\nThe Australian Competition and Consumer Commission  Part II\n\nSection 7\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026"
    },
