    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-7",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "7 Constitution of Commission",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-7"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.77",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commission shall consist of a Chairperson and such number\nof other members as are from time to time appointed in accordance\nwith this Act.\n\n(2) The members of the Commission shall be appointed by the\nGovernor-General and shall be so appointed as full-time members.\n\n(3) Before the Governor-General appoints a person as a member of the\nCommission or as Chairperson, the Minister must:\n\n(a) be satisfied that the person qualifies for the appointment\nbecause of the person’s knowledge of, or experience in,\nindustry, commerce, economics, law, public administration\nor consumer protection; and\n\n(b) consider whether the person has knowledge of, or experience\nin, small business matters; and\n\n(c) if there is at least one fully-participating jurisdiction—be\nsatisfied that a majority of such jurisdictions support the\nappointment.\n\n(4) At least one of the members of the Commission must be a person\nwho has knowledge of, or experience in, consumer protection.\nNote:\nUnder section 23 of the Public Governance, Performance and\nAccountability Act 2013, the Chairperson may enter into contracts and\nother arrangements on behalf of the Commonwealth.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Commission shall consist of a Chairperson and such number\nof other members as are from time to time appointed in accordance\nwith this Act.\n\n(2) The members of the Commission shall be appointed by the\nGovernor-General and shall be so appointed as full-time members.\n\n(3) Before the Governor-General appoints a person as a member of the\nCommission or as Chairperson, the Minister must:\n\n(a) be satisfied that the person qualifies for the appointment\nbecause of the person’s knowledge of, or experience in,\nindustry, commerce, economics, law, public administration\nor consumer protection; and\n\n(b) consider whether the person has knowledge of, or experience\nin, small business matters; and\n\n(c) if there is at least one fully-participating jurisdiction—be\nsatisfied that a majority of such jurisdictions support the\nappointment.\n\n(4) At least one of the members of the Commission must be a person\nwho has knowledge of, or experience in, consumer protection.\nNote:\nUnder section 23 of the Public Governance, Performance and\nAccountability Act 2013, the Chairperson may enter into contracts and\nother arrangements on behalf of the Commonwealth.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-7-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-7-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-7-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-7-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "afe3ea7217f2a45fd362ba49bfcd8933c42195848bcca76466f091aad9c3d6d0"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-7",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "7 Constitution of Commission",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 77,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commission shall consist of a Chairperson and such number\nof other members as are from time to time appointed in accordance\nwith this Act.\n\n(2) The members of the Commission shall be appointed by the\nGovernor-General and shall be so appointed as full-time members.\n\n(3) Before the Governor-General appoints a person as a member of the\nCommission or as Chairperson, the Minister must:\n\n(a) be satisfied that the person qualifies for the appointment\nbecause of the person’s knowledge of, or experience in,\nindustry, commerce, economics, law, public administration\nor consumer protection; and\n\n(b) consider whether the person has knowledge of, or experience\nin, small business matters; and\n\n(c) if there is at least one fully-participating jurisdiction—be\nsatisfied that a majority of such jurisdictions support the\nappointment.\n\n(4) At least one of the members of the Commission must be a person\nwho has knowledge of, or experience in, consumer protection.\nNote:\nUnder section 23 of the Public Governance, Performance and\nAccountability Act 2013, the Chairperson may enter into contracts and\nother arrangements on behalf of the Commonwealth."
    },
