    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-8ab",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "8AB AER members taken to be associate members",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-8ab"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.79",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Act and the Public Governance,\nPerformance and Accountability Act 2013, an AER member is\ntaken to be an associate member of the Commission during the\nperiod for which he or she is an AER member.\nNote:\nAn AER member who is taken to be an associate member of the\nCommission can still be appointed as an associate member under\nsection 8A.\n\n(2) However, an AER member who is taken to be an associate member\nunder subsection (1), is not taken to be an associate member for the\npurposes of sections 8A, 9, 14 and 15 and for the purposes of\nsection 29 of the Public Governance, Performance and\nAccountability Act 2013.\n\n(3) As an associate member, the AER member holds office on such\nterms and conditions as are specified in the instrument of his or her\nappointment under section 44AM or 44AP.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of this Act and the Public Governance,\nPerformance and Accountability Act 2013, an AER member is\ntaken to be an associate member of the Commission during the\nperiod for which he or she is an AER member.\nNote:\nAn AER member who is taken to be an associate member of the\nCommission can still be appointed as an associate member under\nsection 8A.\n\n(2) However, an AER member who is taken to be an associate member\nunder subsection (1), is not taken to be an associate member for the\npurposes of sections 8A, 9, 14 and 15 and for the purposes of\nsection 29 of the Public Governance, Performance and\nAccountability Act 2013.\n\n(3) As an associate member, the AER member holds office on such\nterms and conditions as are specified in the instrument of his or her\nappointment under section 44AM or 44AP.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-8ab-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-8ab-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-8ab-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0e4120b7e139d68357d6583dea991c0b1b24c788f4d711c6a984b633ca4e2415"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-8ab",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "8AB AER members taken to be associate members",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 79,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Act and the Public Governance,\nPerformance and Accountability Act 2013, an AER member is\ntaken to be an associate member of the Commission during the\nperiod for which he or she is an AER member.\nNote:\nAn AER member who is taken to be an associate member of the\nCommission can still be appointed as an associate member under\nsection 8A.\n\n(2) However, an AER member who is taken to be an associate member\nunder subsection (1), is not taken to be an associate member for the\npurposes of sections 8A, 9, 14 and 15 and for the purposes of\nsection 29 of the Public Governance, Performance and\nAccountability Act 2013.\n\n(3) As an associate member, the AER member holds office on such\nterms and conditions as are specified in the instrument of his or her\nappointment under section 44AM or 44AP."
    },
