    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-17a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "17A Disclosure of certain interests by members of the Commission",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-17a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.83",
      "values:originalText": "when taking part in determinations of matters\n\n(1) If, as a result of rules made for the purposes of section 29 of the\nPublic Governance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013\n(which deals with the duty to disclose interests), the Chairperson\nbecomes aware that:\n\n(a) a member of the Commission is taking part, or is to take part,\nin the determination of a matter; and\n\n(b) the member has a pecuniary interest that could conflict with\nthe proper performance of his or her functions in relation to\nthe determination of the matter;\nthen:\n\nChapter 1  Preliminary",
      "skos:definition": "when taking part in determinations of matters\n\n(1) If, as a result of rules made for the purposes of section 29 of the\nPublic Governance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013\n(which deals with the duty to disclose interests), the Chairperson\nbecomes aware that:\n\n(a) a member of the Commission is taking part, or is to take part,\nin the determination of a matter; and\n\n(b) the member has a pecuniary interest that could conflict with\nthe proper performance of his or her functions in relation to\nthe determination of the matter;\nthen:\n\nChapter 1  Preliminary",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-17a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-17a-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "eae16cceacccf5a5037776e020b2352815804a8865e62c0ac8220ca5cc8cc448",
      "skos:note": "Member of Commission must disclose pecuniary interests when taking part in determinations."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-17a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "17A Disclosure of certain interests by members of the Commission",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 83,
      "values:originalText": "when taking part in determinations of matters\n\n(1) If, as a result of rules made for the purposes of section 29 of the\nPublic Governance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013\n(which deals with the duty to disclose interests), the Chairperson\nbecomes aware that:\n\n(a) a member of the Commission is taking part, or is to take part,\nin the determination of a matter; and\n\n(b) the member has a pecuniary interest that could conflict with\nthe proper performance of his or her functions in relation to\nthe determination of the matter;\nthen:\n\nChapter 1  Preliminary"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-17a-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-17a"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-17a-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Must",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Member must disclose pecuniary interests.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-18",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "18 Meetings of Commission",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-18"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.84",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to this section, the Chairperson shall convene such\nmeetings of the Commission as he or she thinks necessary for the\nefficient performance of the functions of the Commission.\n\n(2) Meetings of the Commission shall be held at such places as the\nChairperson determines.\n\n(3) The Chairperson shall preside at all meetings of the Commission at\nwhich he or she is present.\n\n(4) In the absence of the Chairperson from a meeting of the\nCommission:\n\n(a) if there are 2 Deputy Chairpersons available to preside at the\nmeeting—the Chairperson may nominate 1 of them to\npreside at the meeting; or\n\n(b) if there is only 1 Deputy Chairperson available to preside at\nthe meeting—that Deputy Chairperson is to preside at the\nmeeting.\n\n(5) Subject to this Act and the regulations, the member presiding at a\nmeeting of the Commission may give directions regarding the\nprocedure to be followed at or in connexion with the meeting.\n\n(6) At a meeting of the Commission:\n\nPreliminary  Chapter 1\nThe Australian Competition and Consumer Commission  Part II\n\nSection 19\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(a) three members (including the Chairperson or a Deputy\nChairperson) form a quorum;\n\n(b) all questions shall be decided by a majority of votes of the\nmembers present and voting; and\n\n(c) the member presiding has a deliberative vote and, in the\nevent of an equality of votes, also has a casting vote.\n\n(7) If the Commission so determines, a member or members may\nparticipate in, and form part of a quorum at, a meeting of the\nCommission or a Division of the Commission by means of any of\nthe following methods of communication:\n\n(a) telephone;\n\n(b) closed circuit television;\n\n(c) another method of communication determined by the\nCommission.\n\n(8) A determination made by the Commission under subsection (7)\nmay be made in respect of a particular meeting or meetings of the\nCommission or a Division of the Commission or in respect of all\nmeetings of the Commission or a Division of the Commission.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Subject to this section, the Chairperson shall convene such\nmeetings of the Commission as he or she thinks necessary for the\nefficient performance of the functions of the Commission.\n\n(2) Meetings of the Commission shall be held at such places as the\nChairperson determines.\n\n(3) The Chairperson shall preside at all meetings of the Commission at\nwhich he or she is present.\n\n(4) In the absence of the Chairperson from a meeting of the\nCommission:\n\n(a) if there are 2 Deputy Chairpersons available to preside at the\nmeeting—the Chairperson may nominate 1 of them to\npreside at the meeting; or\n\n(b) if there is only 1 Deputy Chairperson available to preside at\nthe meeting—that Deputy Chairperson is to preside at the\nmeeting.\n\n(5) Subject to this Act and the regulations, the member presiding at a\nmeeting of the Commission may give directions regarding the\nprocedure to be followed at or in connexion with the meeting.\n\n(6) At a meeting of the Commission:\n\nPreliminary  Chapter 1\nThe Australian Competition and Consumer Commission  Part II\n\nSection 19\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(a) three members (including the Chairperson or a Deputy\nChairperson) form a quorum;\n\n(b) all questions shall be decided by a majority of votes of the\nmembers present and voting; and\n\n(c) the member presiding has a deliberative vote and, in the\nevent of an equality of votes, also has a casting vote.\n\n(7) If the Commission so determines, a member or members may\nparticipate in, and form part of a quorum at, a meeting of the\nCommission or a Division of the Commission by means of any of\nthe following methods of communication:\n\n(a) telephone;\n\n(b) closed circuit television;\n\n(c) another method of communication determined by the\nCommission.\n\n(8) A determination made by the Commission under subsection (7)\nmay be made in respect of a particular meeting or meetings of the\nCommission or a Division of the Commission or in respect of all\nmeetings of the Commission or a Divisio",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-18-ss-1"
        },
