    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-26",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "26 Delegation by Commission of certain functions and powers",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-26"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.87",
      "values:originalText": "Delegation to staff members of ASIC\n\n(1) The Commission may, by resolution, delegate:\n\n(a) any of its functions and powers under or in relation to Parts\nVI and XI and the Australian Consumer Law; and\n\n(b) any of its powers under Part XII that relate to those Parts or\nthe Australian Consumer Law;\nto a staff member of ASIC.\n\n(2) The Commission must not delegate a function or power under\nsubsection (1) unless the Chairperson of ASIC has agreed to the\ndelegation in writing.\n\nChapter 1  Preliminary",
      "skos:definition": "Delegation to staff members of ASIC\n\n(1) The Commission may, by resolution, delegate:\n\n(a) any of its functions and powers under or in relation to Parts\nVI and XI and the Australian Consumer Law; and\n\n(b) any of its powers under Part XII that relate to those Parts or\nthe Australian Consumer Law;\nto a staff member of ASIC.\n\n(2) The Commission must not delegate a function or power under\nsubsection (1) unless the Chairperson of ASIC has agreed to the\ndelegation in writing.\n\nChapter 1  Preliminary",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-26-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-26-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "87a85f4e5a41dff16fa1182329ebdf42f4113b7c09bc77eb122c3d2013286e1a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-26",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26 Delegation by Commission of certain functions and powers",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 87,
      "values:originalText": "Delegation to staff members of ASIC\n\n(1) The Commission may, by resolution, delegate:\n\n(a) any of its functions and powers under or in relation to Parts\nVI and XI and the Australian Consumer Law; and\n\n(b) any of its powers under Part XII that relate to those Parts or\nthe Australian Consumer Law;\nto a staff member of ASIC.\n\n(2) The Commission must not delegate a function or power under\nsubsection (1) unless the Chairperson of ASIC has agreed to the\ndelegation in writing.\n\nChapter 1  Preliminary"
    },
