    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-27a-ss-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-27a-ss-2"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:LegalPerson"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: LegalPerson"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-27a-ss-2-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "determined",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Duty to provide terms and conditions",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The Commission has the authority to determine terms and conditions.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Terms and conditions of engagement must be as determined by the Commission."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-27a-ss-2-logic-linearlogic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LinearLogic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "determined",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Implication of determination",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::linear",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "If the Commission determines terms and conditions, then those terms and conditions apply.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "If the Commission determines terms and conditions, then they are binding."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-27a-ss-2-logic-alleninterval-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "determined",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Temporal relationship of determination",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The Commission's determination of terms and conditions occurs at a specific point in time.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The Commission's determination of terms and conditions is a single event."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-27a-ss-2-logic-diffusion-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Diffusion"
      },
      "cml:operator": "determined",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Spread of determination",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::diffusion",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The Commission's determination of terms and conditions spreads to all parties involved.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "All parties must comply with the determined terms and conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-27a-ss-2-logic-cogai-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:CogAI"
      },
      "cml:operator": "determined",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Artificial intelligence application",
      "cml:executionSurface": "sparql_library::parsers::chk_parser",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The Commission's determination of terms and conditions can be applied by artificial intelligence systems.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Artificial intelligence systems must comply with the determined terms and conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-28",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "28 Functions of Commission in relation to dissemination of",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-28"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.89",
      "values:originalText": "information, law reform and research\n\n(1) In addition to any other functions conferred on the Commission,\nthe Commission has the following functions:\n\n(a) to make available to persons engaged in trade or commerce\nand other interested persons general information for their\nguidance with respect to the carrying out of the functions, or\nthe exercise of the powers, of the Commission under this\nAct;\n\n(b) to examine critically, and report to the Minister on, the laws\nin force in Australia relating to the protection of consumers\nin respect of matters referred to the Commission by the\nMinister, being matters with respect to which the Parliament\nhas power to make laws;\n\n(c) to conduct research in relation to matters affecting the\ninterests of consumers, being matters with respect to which\nthe Parliament has power to make laws;\n\n(ca) to conduct research and undertake studies on matters that are\nreferred to the Commission by the Council and that relate to\nthe Commission’s other functions;\n\nChapter 1  Preliminary",
      "skos:definition": "information, law reform and research\n\n(1) In addition to any other functions conferred on the Commission,\nthe Commission has the following functions:\n\n(a) to make available to persons engaged in trade or commerce\nand other interested persons general information for their\nguidance with respect to the carrying out of the functions, or\nthe exercise of the powers, of the Commission under this\nAct;\n\n(b) to examine critically, and report to the Minister on, the laws\nin force in Australia relating to the protection of consumers\nin respect of matters referred to the Commission by the\nMinister, being matters with respect to which the Parliament\nhas power to make laws;\n\n(c) to conduct research in relation to matters affecting the\ninterests of consumers, being matters with respect to which\nthe Parliament has power to make laws;\n\n(ca) to conduct research and undertake studies on matters that are\nreferred to the Commission by the Council and that relate to\nthe Commission’s other functions;\n\nChapter 1  Preliminary",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-28-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-28-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1ac228905dd15842fc380324ed2c334832a45e53072f7244a3b77dce601a7a1d",
      "skos:note": "Commission must provide general information and report on laws related to consumer protection."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-28",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "28 Functions of Commission in relation to dissemination of",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 89,
      "values:originalText": "information, law reform and research\n\n(1) In addition to any other functions conferred on the Commission,\nthe Commission has the following functions:\n\n(a) to make available to persons engaged in trade or commerce\nand other interested persons general information for their\nguidance with respect to the carrying out of the functions, or\nthe exercise of the powers, of the Commission under this\nAct;\n\n(b) to examine critically, and report to the Minister on, the laws\nin force in Australia relating to the protection of consumers\nin respect of matters referred to the Commission by the\nMinister, being matters with respect to which the Parliament\nhas power to make laws;\n\n(c) to conduct research in relation to matters affecting the\ninterests of consumers, being matters with respect to which\nthe Parliament has power to make laws;\n\n(ca) to conduct research and undertake studies on matters that are\nreferred to the Commission by the Council and that relate to\nthe Commission’s other functions;\n\nChapter 1  Preliminary"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-28-norm",
