    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "29B Functions and powers of Council",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-29b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.92",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Council’s functions include:\n\n(a) carrying out research into matters referred to the Council by\nthe Minister; and\n\n(b) providing advice on matters referred to the Council by the\nMinister.\n\n(2) The Council may:\n\n(a) perform any function conferred on it by a law of the\nCommonwealth, or of a State or Territory; and\n\n(b) exercise any power:\n\n(i) conferred by that law to facilitate the performance of\nthat function; or\n\nPreliminary  Chapter 1\nThe National Competition Council  Part IIA\n\nSection 29BA\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(ii) necessary or convenient to permit the performance of\nthat function.\n\n(2A) The Council must not, under subsection (2):\n\n(a) perform a function conferred on it by a law of a State or\nTerritory; or\n\n(b) exercise a power that is so conferred;\nunless the conferral of the function or power is in accordance with\nthe Competition Principles Agreement.\n\n(2B) Subsection (2) does not apply to a State/Territory energy law.\nNote:\nSection 29BA provides that a State/Territory energy law may confer\nfunctions or powers, or impose duties, on the Council.\n\n(3) In performing its functions, the Council may co-operate with a\ndepartment, body or authority of the Commonwealth, of a State or\nof a Territory.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Council’s functions include:\n\n(a) carrying out research into matters referred to the Council by\nthe Minister; and\n\n(b) providing advice on matters referred to the Council by the\nMinister.\n\n(2) The Council may:\n\n(a) perform any function conferred on it by a law of the\nCommonwealth, or of a State or Territory; and\n\n(b) exercise any power:\n\n(i) conferred by that law to facilitate the performance of\nthat function; or\n\nPreliminary  Chapter 1\nThe National Competition Council  Part IIA\n\nSection 29BA\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(ii) necessary or convenient to permit the performance of\nthat function.\n\n(2A) The Council must not, under subsection (2):\n\n(a) perform a function conferred on it by a law of a State or\nTerritory; or\n\n(b) exercise a power that is so conferred;\nunless the conferral of the function or power is in accordance with\nthe Competition Principles Agreement.\n\n(2B) Subsection (2) does not apply to a State/Territory energy law.\nNote:\nSection 29BA provides that a State/Territory energy law may confer\nfunctions or powers, or impose duties, on the Council.\n\n(3) In performing its functions, the Council may co-operate with a\ndepartment, body or authority of the Commonwealth, of a State or\nof a Territory.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29b-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29b-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29b-ss-2a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29b-ss-2b"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29b-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9172cdc2cca1d3c71083cebd1713de668303d189c646d0a0e30d7aedecf766ef"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-29b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "29B Functions and powers of Council",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 92,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Council’s functions include:\n\n(a) carrying out research into matters referred to the Council by\nthe Minister; and\n\n(b) providing advice on matters referred to the Council by the\nMinister.\n\n(2) The Council may:\n\n(a) perform any function conferred on it by a law of the\nCommonwealth, or of a State or Territory; and\n\n(b) exercise any power:\n\n(i) conferred by that law to facilitate the performance of\nthat function; or\n\nPreliminary  Chapter 1\nThe National Competition Council  Part IIA\n\nSection 29BA\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(ii) necessary or convenient to permit the performance of\nthat function.\n\n(2A) The Council must not, under subsection (2):\n\n(a) perform a function conferred on it by a law of a State or\nTerritory; or\n\n(b) exercise a power that is so conferred;\nunless the conferral of the function or power is in accordance with\nthe Competition Principles Agreement.\n\n(2B) Subsection (2) does not apply to a State/Territory energy law.\nNote:\nSection 29BA provides that a State/Territory energy law may confer\nfunctions or powers, or impose duties, on the Council.\n\n(3) In performing its functions, the Council may co-operate with a\ndepartment, body or authority of the Commonwealth, of a State or\nof a Territory."
    },
    {
