      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.92",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The Council may:\n\n(a) perform any function conferred on it by a law of the\nCommonwealth, or of a State or Territory; and\n\n(b) exercise any power:\n\n(i) conferred by that law to facilitate the performance of\nthat function; or\n\nPreliminary  Chapter 1\nThe National Competition Council  Part IIA\n\nSection 29BA\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(ii) necessary or convenient to permit the performance of\nthat function.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The Council may:\n\n(a) perform any function conferred on it by a law of the\nCommonwealth, or of a State or Territory; and\n\n(b) exercise any power:\n\n(i) conferred by that law to facilitate the performance of\nthat function; or\n\nPreliminary  Chapter 1\nThe National Competition Council  Part IIA\n\nSection 29BA\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(ii) necessary or convenient to permit the performance of\nthat function.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29b"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29b-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29b-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "42e8ba00c0025f18e09e242f882a85aee407bd9d25e866d88df4cbfb6de22a66",
      "skos:note": "The Council may perform functions and exercise powers necessary to facilitate performance."
    },
    {
