    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29ba",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "29BA Commonwealth consent to conferral of functions etc. on",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-29ba"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.93",
      "values:originalText": "Council\n\n(1) A State/Territory energy law may confer functions or powers, or\nimpose duties, on the Council for the purposes of that law.\nNote:\nSection 29BC sets out when such a law imposes a duty on the\nCouncil.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not authorise the conferral of a function or\npower, or the imposition of a duty, by a State/Territory energy law\nto the extent to which:\n\n(a) the conferral or imposition, or the authorisation, would\ncontravene any constitutional doctrines restricting the duties\nthat may be imposed on the Council; or\n\n(b) the authorisation would otherwise exceed the legislative\npower of the Commonwealth.\n\n(3) The Council cannot perform a duty or function, or exercise a\npower, under a State/Territory energy law unless the conferral of\nthe function or power, or the imposition of the duty, is in\n\nChapter 1  Preliminary",
      "skos:definition": "Council\n\n(1) A State/Territory energy law may confer functions or powers, or\nimpose duties, on the Council for the purposes of that law.\nNote:\nSection 29BC sets out when such a law imposes a duty on the\nCouncil.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not authorise the conferral of a function or\npower, or the imposition of a duty, by a State/Territory energy law\nto the extent to which:\n\n(a) the conferral or imposition, or the authorisation, would\ncontravene any constitutional doctrines restricting the duties\nthat may be imposed on the Council; or\n\n(b) the authorisation would otherwise exceed the legislative\npower of the Commonwealth.\n\n(3) The Council cannot perform a duty or function, or exercise a\npower, under a State/Territory energy law unless the conferral of\nthe function or power, or the imposition of the duty, is in\n\nChapter 1  Preliminary",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29ba-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29ba-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29ba-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "15b42c09c8a6f64f15078c22ffb69551a48af5540c460d66a8c18851cea82033"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-29ba",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "29BA Commonwealth consent to conferral of functions etc. on",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 93,
      "values:originalText": "Council\n\n(1) A State/Territory energy law may confer functions or powers, or\nimpose duties, on the Council for the purposes of that law.\nNote:\nSection 29BC sets out when such a law imposes a duty on the\nCouncil.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not authorise the conferral of a function or\npower, or the imposition of a duty, by a State/Territory energy law\nto the extent to which:\n\n(a) the conferral or imposition, or the authorisation, would\ncontravene any constitutional doctrines restricting the duties\nthat may be imposed on the Council; or\n\n(b) the authorisation would otherwise exceed the legislative\npower of the Commonwealth.\n\n(3) The Council cannot perform a duty or function, or exercise a\npower, under a State/Territory energy law unless the conferral of\nthe function or power, or the imposition of the duty, is in\n\nChapter 1  Preliminary"
    },
