      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.94",
      "values:originalText": "(4) If, because of subsection (3), this Part is taken to impose the duty,\nit is the intention of the Parliament to rely on all powers available\nto it under the Constitution to support the imposition of the duty by\nthis Part.\n\nPreliminary  Chapter 1\nThe National Competition Council  Part IIA\n\nSection 29BC\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(4) If, because of subsection (3), this Part is taken to impose the duty,\nit is the intention of the Parliament to rely on all powers available\nto it under the Constitution to support the imposition of the duty by\nthis Part.\n\nPreliminary  Chapter 1\nThe National Competition Council  Part IIA\n\nSection 29BC\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29bb"
      },
