    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29bb-ss-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "29BB(6) How duty is imposed",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-29bb-ss-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.94",
      "values:originalText": "(6) Subsections (1) to (5) do not limit section 29BA.\n29BC  When a State/Territory energy law imposes a duty\n\nFor the purposes of sections 29BA and 29BB, a State/Territory\nenergy law imposes a duty on the Council if:\n\n(a) the law confers a function or power on the Council; and\n\n(b) the circumstances in which the function or power is\nconferred give rise to an obligation on the Council to perform\nthe function or to exercise the power.",
      "skos:definition": "(6) Subsections (1) to (5) do not limit section 29BA.\n29BC  When a State/Territory energy law imposes a duty\n\nFor the purposes of sections 29BA and 29BB, a State/Territory\nenergy law imposes a duty on the Council if:\n\n(a) the law confers a function or power on the Council; and\n\n(b) the circumstances in which the function or power is\nconferred give rise to an obligation on the Council to perform\nthe function or to exercise the power.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29bb"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29bb-ss-6-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29bb-ss-6-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29bb-ss-6-logic-alleninterval-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "19ecda15558ee6748e3cf7fa00dc127216f7108d34961efec603bcaa8e2ba6c6",
      "skos:note": "A State/Territory energy law imposes a duty on the Council if it confers a function or power on the Council."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-29bb-ss-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "29BB(6) How duty is imposed",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 94,
      "values:originalText": "(6) Subsections (1) to (5) do not limit section 29BA.\n29BC  When a State/Territory energy law imposes a duty\n\nFor the purposes of sections 29BA and 29BB, a State/Territory\nenergy law imposes a duty on the Council if:\n\n(a) the law confers a function or power on the Council; and\n\n(b) the circumstances in which the function or power is\nconferred give rise to an obligation on the Council to perform\nthe function or to exercise the power."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29bb-ss-6-norm",
