      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "29E Acting Council President",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-29e"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.96",
      "values:originalText": "The Minister may appoint a Councillor to act as the Council\nPresident:\n\n(a) if there is a vacancy in the office of Council President,\nwhether or not an appointment has previously been made to\nthe office; or\n\n(b) during any period, or during all periods, when the Council\nPresident is absent from duty or absent from Australia or is,\nfor any reason, unable to perform the duties of the office.\nNote:\nFor rules that apply to acting appointments, see section 33A of the\nActs Interpretation Act 1901.",
      "skos:definition": "The Minister may appoint a Councillor to act as the Council\nPresident:\n\n(a) if there is a vacancy in the office of Council President,\nwhether or not an appointment has previously been made to\nthe office; or\n\n(b) during any period, or during all periods, when the Council\nPresident is absent from duty or absent from Australia or is,\nfor any reason, unable to perform the duties of the office.\nNote:\nFor rules that apply to acting appointments, see section 33A of the\nActs Interpretation Act 1901.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29e-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29e-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "248d74cd39d2c00b2f91a1181e3441efc8bfe7201f4095e76b4845cabf7a4d55",
      "skos:note": "The Minister may appoint a Councillor to act as the Council President.",
      "dc:references": [
        "sec-33A"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-29e",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "29E Acting Council President",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 96,
      "values:originalText": "The Minister may appoint a Councillor to act as the Council\nPresident:\n\n(a) if there is a vacancy in the office of Council President,\nwhether or not an appointment has previously been made to\nthe office; or\n\n(b) during any period, or during all periods, when the Council\nPresident is absent from duty or absent from Australia or is,\nfor any reason, unable to perform the duties of the office.\nNote:\nFor rules that apply to acting appointments, see section 33A of the\nActs Interpretation Act 1901."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29e-norm",
