      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29f",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "29F Remuneration of Councillors",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-29f"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.96",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A Councillor is to be paid the remuneration that is determined by\nthe Remuneration Tribunal. If no determination of the\nRemuneration Tribunal is in operation, the Councillor is to be paid\nthe remuneration that is prescribed.\n\n(2) A Councillor is to be paid such allowances as are prescribed.\n\n(3) This section has effect subject to the Remuneration Tribunal Act\n1973.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A Councillor is to be paid the remuneration that is determined by\nthe Remuneration Tribunal. If no determination of the\nRemuneration Tribunal is in operation, the Councillor is to be paid\nthe remuneration that is prescribed.\n\n(2) A Councillor is to be paid such allowances as are prescribed.\n\n(3) This section has effect subject to the Remuneration Tribunal Act\n1973.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29f-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29f-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29f-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0cca8fc9ecb22360d84315a97c0ed39975d9a0907038d4e4f250c55ae71f29d3"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-29f",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "29F Remuneration of Councillors",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 96,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A Councillor is to be paid the remuneration that is determined by\nthe Remuneration Tribunal. If no determination of the\nRemuneration Tribunal is in operation, the Councillor is to be paid\nthe remuneration that is prescribed.\n\n(2) A Councillor is to be paid such allowances as are prescribed.\n\n(3) This section has effect subject to the Remuneration Tribunal Act\n1973."
    },
