    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29l",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "29L Council meetings",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-29l"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.98",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Council President must convene the meetings that the Council\nPresident thinks are necessary to perform the Council’s functions\nefficiently.\n\n(2) The meetings must be held in places determined by the Council\nPresident.\n\n(3) The Council President must preside at any meeting that he or she\nattends.\n\n(4) If the Council President is absent from a meeting, a Councillor\nchosen by the Councillors at the meeting must preside.\n\n(5) The Councillor presiding at a meeting may give directions on the\nprocedure to be followed in relation to the meeting.\n\n(6) The quorum for a meeting is 3 Councillors (including the Council\nPresident).\n\n(7) At a meeting, a question must be decided by a majority of votes of\nthe Councillors present and voting. The Councillor presiding has a\ndeliberative vote, and a casting vote if the deliberative votes are\nequally divided.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Council President must convene the meetings that the Council\nPresident thinks are necessary to perform the Council’s functions\nefficiently.\n\n(2) The meetings must be held in places determined by the Council\nPresident.\n\n(3) The Council President must preside at any meeting that he or she\nattends.\n\n(4) If the Council President is absent from a meeting, a Councillor\nchosen by the Councillors at the meeting must preside.\n\n(5) The Councillor presiding at a meeting may give directions on the\nprocedure to be followed in relation to the meeting.\n\n(6) The quorum for a meeting is 3 Councillors (including the Council\nPresident).\n\n(7) At a meeting, a question must be decided by a majority of votes of\nthe Councillors present and voting. The Councillor presiding has a\ndeliberative vote, and a casting vote if the deliberative votes are\nequally divided.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29l-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29l-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29l-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29l-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29l-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29l-ss-6"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29l-ss-7"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9e4226bcb4d583e419f897400614bc708fe5cb3ee10edd3a5762acc43cfed50d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-29l",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "29L Council meetings",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 98,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Council President must convene the meetings that the Council\nPresident thinks are necessary to perform the Council’s functions\nefficiently.\n\n(2) The meetings must be held in places determined by the Council\nPresident.\n\n(3) The Council President must preside at any meeting that he or she\nattends.\n\n(4) If the Council President is absent from a meeting, a Councillor\nchosen by the Councillors at the meeting must preside.\n\n(5) The Councillor presiding at a meeting may give directions on the\nprocedure to be followed in relation to the meeting.\n\n(6) The quorum for a meeting is 3 Councillors (including the Council\nPresident).\n\n(7) At a meeting, a question must be decided by a majority of votes of\nthe Councillors present and voting. The Councillor presiding has a\ndeliberative vote, and a casting vote if the deliberative votes are\nequally divided."
    },
