    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29la",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "29LA Resolutions without meetings",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-29la"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.98",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If all Councillors (other than those that must not sign a document\nbecause of subsection (3)) sign a document containing a statement\nthat they are in favour of a resolution in terms set out in the\ndocument, then a resolution in those terms is taken to have been\npassed at a duly constituted meeting of the Council held on the day\nthe document was signed, or, if the members sign the document on\ndifferent days, on the last of those days.\n\nPreliminary  Chapter 1\nThe National Competition Council  Part IIA\n\nSection 29M\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), 2 or more separate documents\ncontaining statements in identical terms each of which is signed by\none or more Councillors are together taken to constitute one\ndocument containing a statement in those terms signed by those\nCouncillors on the respective days on which they signed the\nseparate documents.\n\n(3) A Councillor must not sign a document containing a statement in\nfavour of a resolution if the resolution concerns a matter in which\nthe Councillor has any pecuniary interest, being an interest that\ncould conflict with the proper performance of the Councillor’s\nfunctions in relation to any matter.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If all Councillors (other than those that must not sign a document\nbecause of subsection (3)) sign a document containing a statement\nthat they are in favour of a resolution in terms set out in the\ndocument, then a resolution in those terms is taken to have been\npassed at a duly constituted meeting of the Council held on the day\nthe document was signed, or, if the members sign the document on\ndifferent days, on the last of those days.\n\nPreliminary  Chapter 1\nThe National Competition Council  Part IIA\n\nSection 29M\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), 2 or more separate documents\ncontaining statements in identical terms each of which is signed by\none or more Councillors are together taken to constitute one\ndocument containing a statement in those terms signed by those\nCouncillors on the respective days on which they signed the\nseparate documents.\n\n(3) A Councillor must not sign a document containing a statement in\nfavour of a resolution if the resolution concerns a matter in which\nthe Councillor has any pecuniary interest, being an interest that\ncould conflict with the proper performance of the Councillor’s\nfunctions in relation to any matter.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29la-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29la-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29la-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "77885d93cac8bb732143e1477a20623679b92e94a27782018b3b502e0c53d1e4"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-29la",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "29LA Resolutions without meetings",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 98,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If all Councillors (other than those that must not sign a document\nbecause of subsection (3)) sign a document containing a statement\nthat they are in favour of a resolution in terms set out in the\ndocument, then a resolution in those terms is taken to have been\npassed at a duly constituted meeting of the Council held on the day\nthe document was signed, or, if the members sign the document on\ndifferent days, on the last of those days.\n\nPreliminary  Chapter 1\nThe National Competition Council  Part IIA\n\nSection 29M\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), 2 or more separate documents\ncontaining statements in identical terms each of which is signed by\none or more Councillors are together taken to constitute one\ndocument containing a statement in those terms signed by those\nCouncillors on the respective days on which they signed the\nseparate documents.\n\n(3) A Councillor must not sign a document containing a statement in\nfavour of a resolution if the resolution concerns a matter in which\nthe Councillor has any pecuniary interest, being an interest that\ncould conflict with the proper performance of the Councillor’s\nfunctions in relation to any matter."
    },
