      "cml:integrityHash": "8bdd3926bba087acfdee247ca66f2047d4f19aa68eb0d6d383ddb429a25505af",
      "skos:note": "All Councillors must sign a document in favour of a resolution."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-29la-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "29LA(1) Resolutions without meetings",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 98,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If all Councillors (other than those that must not sign a document\nbecause of subsection (3)) sign a document containing a statement\nthat they are in favour of a resolution in terms set out in the\ndocument, then a resolution in those terms is taken to have been\npassed at a duly constituted meeting of the Council held on the day\nthe document was signed, or, if the members sign the document on\ndifferent days, on the last of those days.\n\nPreliminary  Chapter 1\nThe National Competition Council  Part IIA\n\nSection 29M\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026"
    },
