      "values:originalText": "(5) Where a person has been appointed under this section to act as a\nmember of the Tribunal during the absence from duty of a member\nof the Tribunal, and that member ceases to hold office without\nhaving resumed duty, the period of appointment of the person so\nappointed shall be deemed to continue until it is terminated by the\nGovernor-General, or until the expiration of 12 months from the\ndate on which the absent member ceases to hold office, whichever\nfirst happens.\n\nChapter 1  Preliminary",
      "skos:definition": "(5) Where a person has been appointed under this section to act as a\nmember of the Tribunal during the absence from duty of a member\nof the Tribunal, and that member ceases to hold office without\nhaving resumed duty, the period of appointment of the person so\nappointed shall be deemed to continue until it is terminated by the\nGovernor-General, or until the expiration of 12 months from the\ndate on which the absent member ceases to hold office, whichever\nfirst happens.\n\nChapter 1  Preliminary",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-34"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-34-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-34-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e695360d146c5ab3ffd4200c3bb050f789228e56d9f8c4c859a6f5c86332576a",
      "skos:note": "Appointment continuation upon member's absence"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-34-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "34(5) Acting appointments",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 102,
      "values:originalText": "(5) Where a person has been appointed under this section to act as a\nmember of the Tribunal during the absence from duty of a member\nof the Tribunal, and that member ceases to hold office without\nhaving resumed duty, the period of appointment of the person so\nappointed shall be deemed to continue until it is terminated by the\nGovernor-General, or until the expiration of 12 months from the\ndate on which the absent member ceases to hold office, whichever\nfirst happens.\n\nChapter 1  Preliminary"
    },
    {
