    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-37",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "37 Constitution of Tribunal for particular matters",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-37"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.105",
      "values:originalText": "For the purpose of hearing and determining proceedings, the\nTribunal must be constituted by a Division of the Tribunal\nconsisting of:\n\n(a) in any case—a presidential member of the Tribunal and 2\nmembers of the Tribunal who are not presidential members;\nor\n\n(b) if the proceedings are proceedings on a review under\nDivision 1A of Part IX—a presidential member of the\nTribunal.",
      "skos:definition": "For the purpose of hearing and determining proceedings, the\nTribunal must be constituted by a Division of the Tribunal\nconsisting of:\n\n(a) in any case—a presidential member of the Tribunal and 2\nmembers of the Tribunal who are not presidential members;\nor\n\n(b) if the proceedings are proceedings on a review under\nDivision 1A of Part IX—a presidential member of the\nTribunal.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-37-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-37-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e9ac39d927102b273258da650606d358be0bd54c2ff5c6c4649cf3c9d10513ed",
      "skos:note": "Presidential member and 2 non-presidential members must constitute the Tribunal for hearing and determining proceedings."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-37",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "37 Constitution of Tribunal for particular matters",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 105,
      "values:originalText": "For the purpose of hearing and determining proceedings, the\nTribunal must be constituted by a Division of the Tribunal\nconsisting of:\n\n(a) in any case—a presidential member of the Tribunal and 2\nmembers of the Tribunal who are not presidential members;\nor\n\n(b) if the proceedings are proceedings on a review under\nDivision 1A of Part IX—a presidential member of the\nTribunal."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-37-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-37"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-37-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Presidential member must be present",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Division of the Tribunal must consist of...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...a presidential member and 2 non-presidential members"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-38",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "38 Validity of determinations",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-38"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.105",
      "values:originalText": "The validity of a determination of the Tribunal shall not be affected\nor called in question by reason of any defect or irregularity in the\nconstitution of the Tribunal.",
      "skos:definition": "The validity of a determination of the Tribunal shall not be affected\nor called in question by reason of any defect or irregularity in the\nconstitution of the Tribunal.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-38-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-38-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-38-logic-deontic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "dc2859db40e099aa1da9aadb3ccd66b6005f7daf2fb74f450dc841a9622c9f02",
      "skos:note": "The validity of a determination is not affected by defects in the Tribunal's constitution."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-38",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "38 Validity of determinations",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 105,
      "values:originalText": "The validity of a determination of the Tribunal shall not be affected\nor called in question by reason of any defect or irregularity in the\nconstitution of the Tribunal."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-38-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-38"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-38-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to uphold validity of determinations",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The Tribunal's constitution is valid.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The determination's validity is not affected."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-38-logic-deontic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Permission",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Permission to disregard defects in the Tribunal's constitution",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "There are no explicit requirements for the Tribunal's constitution.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The defect or irregularity in the constitution does not affect the determination's validity."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-39",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "39 President may give directions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-39"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.105",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The President may give directions as to the arrangement of the\nbusiness of the Tribunal and the constitution of Divisions of the\nTribunal.\n\n(2) The President may give directions to the Deputy Presidents in\nrelation to the exercise by the Deputy Presidents of powers with\nrespect to matters of procedure in proceedings before the Tribunal.\nNote:\nSubsection 103(2) provides that any presidential member may\nexercise powers with respect to matters of procedure in proceedings\nbefore the Tribunal.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The President may give directions as to the arrangement of the\nbusiness of the Tribunal and the constitution of Divisions of the\nTribunal.\n\n(2) The President may give directions to the Deputy Presidents in\nrelation to the exercise by the Deputy Presidents of powers with\nrespect to matters of procedure in proceedings before the Tribunal.\nNote:\nSubsection 103(2) provides that any presidential member may\nexercise powers with respect to matters of procedure in proceedings\nbefore the Tribunal.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-39-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-39-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "920ad5a6f03ea1225949b7d8658934444693e96b20b2ebf444d5f1bd8feb56fa"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-39",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "39 President may give directions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 105,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The President may give directions as to the arrangement of the\nbusiness of the Tribunal and the constitution of Divisions of the\nTribunal.\n\n(2) The President may give directions to the Deputy Presidents in\nrelation to the exercise by the Deputy Presidents of powers with\nrespect to matters of procedure in proceedings before the Tribunal.\nNote:\nSubsection 103(2) provides that any presidential member may\nexercise powers with respect to matters of procedure in proceedings\nbefore the Tribunal."
    },
