      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.105",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The President may give directions to the Deputy Presidents in\nrelation to the exercise by the Deputy Presidents of powers with\nrespect to matters of procedure in proceedings before the Tribunal.\nNote:\nSubsection 103(2) provides that any presidential member may\nexercise powers with respect to matters of procedure in proceedings\nbefore the Tribunal.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The President may give directions to the Deputy Presidents in\nrelation to the exercise by the Deputy Presidents of powers with\nrespect to matters of procedure in proceedings before the Tribunal.\nNote:\nSubsection 103(2) provides that any presidential member may\nexercise powers with respect to matters of procedure in proceedings\nbefore the Tribunal.",
