      "skos:note": "The President may give directions to Deputy Presidents regarding procedure in Tribunal proceedings."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-39-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "39(2) President may give directions",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 105,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The President may give directions to the Deputy Presidents in\nrelation to the exercise by the Deputy Presidents of powers with\nrespect to matters of procedure in proceedings before the Tribunal.\nNote:\nSubsection 103(2) provides that any presidential member may\nexercise powers with respect to matters of procedure in proceedings\nbefore the Tribunal."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-39-ss-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
