    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ai-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44AI(2) Commonwealth consent to conferral of functions etc. on AER",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44ai-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.112",
      "values:originalText": "(2) Subsection (1) does not authorise the conferral of a function or\npower, or the imposition of a duty, by a State/Territory energy law\nor local energy instrument to the extent to which:\n\n(a) the conferral or imposition, or the authorisation, would\ncontravene any constitutional doctrines restricting the duties\nthat may be imposed on the AER; or\n\nPreliminary  Chapter 1\nThe Australian Energy Regulator (AER)  Part IIIAA\nFunctions and powers of the AER  Division 3\n\nSection 44AIA\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(b) the authorisation would otherwise exceed the legislative\npower of the Commonwealth.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) Subsection (1) does not authorise the conferral of a function or\npower, or the imposition of a duty, by a State/Territory energy law\nor local energy instrument to the extent to which:\n\n(a) the conferral or imposition, or the authorisation, would\ncontravene any constitutional doctrines restricting the duties\nthat may be imposed on the AER; or\n\nPreliminary  Chapter 1\nThe Australian Energy Regulator (AER)  Part IIIAA\nFunctions and powers of the AER  Division 3\n\nSection 44AIA\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(b) the authorisation would otherwise exceed the legislative\npower of the Commonwealth.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ai"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ai-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ai-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ai-ss-2-logic-alleninterval-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "49a81f51d91f2ae4e6fdf779dea98cba2a200394193f9bd3ff302378489411a2",
      "skos:note": "No conferral of function or power by State/Territory energy law or local energy instrument to certain extent."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44ai-ss-2",
