    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ai-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44AI(3) Commonwealth consent to conferral of functions etc. on AER",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44ai-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.112",
      "values:originalText": "(3) The AER cannot perform a duty or function, or exercise a power,\nunder a State/Territory energy law or local energy instrument\nunless the conferral of the function or power, or the imposition of\nthe duty, is in accordance with the Australian Energy Market\nAgreement, or any other relevant agreement between the\nCommonwealth and the State or Territory concerned.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) The AER cannot perform a duty or function, or exercise a power,\nunder a State/Territory energy law or local energy instrument\nunless the conferral of the function or power, or the imposition of\nthe duty, is in accordance with the Australian Energy Market\nAgreement, or any other relevant agreement between the\nCommonwealth and the State or Territory concerned.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ai"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ai-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ai-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "fc0465312b9968d6e56b716763cd37b880d36756b05208d99a633eaa2b409fc0",
      "skos:note": "Commonwealth consent required for conferral of functions on AER"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44ai-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44AI(3) Commonwealth consent to conferral of functions etc. on AER",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 112,
      "values:originalText": "(3) The AER cannot perform a duty or function, or exercise a power,\nunder a State/Territory energy law or local energy instrument\nunless the conferral of the function or power, or the imposition of\nthe duty, is in accordance with the Australian Energy Market\nAgreement, or any other relevant agreement between the\nCommonwealth and the State or Territory concerned."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ai-ss-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ai-ss-3"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ai-ss-3-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "requires",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Requires Commonwealth consent",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Conferral of function without consent is not allowed",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Commonwealth consent is required"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ai-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44AI(4) Commonwealth consent to conferral of functions etc. on AER",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44ai-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.112",
      "values:originalText": "(4) A local energy instrument may confer functions or powers, or\nimpose duties, on the AER only if the instrument is designated for\nthe purposes of this subsection under the Australian Energy Market\nAgreement, or any other relevant agreement between the\nCommonwealth and the State or Territory that made the\ninstrument.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) A local energy instrument may confer functions or powers, or\nimpose duties, on the AER only if the instrument is designated for\nthe purposes of this subsection under the Australian Energy Market\nAgreement, or any other relevant agreement between the\nCommonwealth and the State or Territory that made the\ninstrument.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ai"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ai-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ai-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ai-ss-4-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ai-ss-4-logic-ltl-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b18d0bc9b49ced57339b105c270ec42abcc3edb97380463befceb3553b775803",
      "skos:note": "A local energy instrument must be designated for the purposes of this subsection under a relevant agreement before conferring functions or powers on the AER."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44ai-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44AI(4) Commonwealth consent to conferral of functions etc. on AER",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 112,
      "values:originalText": "(4) A local energy instrument may confer functions or powers, or\nimpose duties, on the AER only if the instrument is designated for\nthe purposes of this subsection under the Australian Energy Market\nAgreement, or any other relevant agreement between the\nCommonwealth and the State or Territory that made the\ninstrument."
    },
