    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ai-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44AI(5) Commonwealth consent to conferral of functions etc. on AER",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44ai-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.112",
      "values:originalText": "(5) To avoid doubt, if a State/Territory energy law is also a local\nenergy instrument, subsection (4) applies to the law.\n44AIA  No merits review of AER decisions\n\nA decision of the AER under a State/Territory energy law or local\nenergy instrument is not to be subject to merits review (however\ndescribed) by a body established under a law of a State or\nTerritory.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) To avoid doubt, if a State/Territory energy law is also a local\nenergy instrument, subsection (4) applies to the law.\n44AIA  No merits review of AER decisions\n\nA decision of the AER under a State/Territory energy law or local\nenergy instrument is not to be subject to merits review (however\ndescribed) by a body established under a law of a State or\nTerritory.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ai"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ai-ss-5-norm"
        },
