      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(5) To avoid doubt, if a State/Territory energy law is also a local\nenergy instrument, subsection (4) applies to the law.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "A decision of the AER under a State/Territory energy law or local\nenergy instrument is not to be subject to merits review..."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44aj",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44AJ How duty is imposed",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44aj"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.113",
      "values:originalText": "Application\n\n(1) This section applies if a State/Territory energy law or local energy\ninstrument purports to impose a duty on the AER.\nNote 1:\nSection 44AK sets out when such a law or instrument imposes a duty\non the AER.\nNote 2:\nSection 320 of the South Australian Energy Retail Legislation, as it\napplies as a law of a State or Territory, deals with the case where a\nduty purportedly imposed on a Commonwealth body under that\n\nChapter 1  Preliminary\nPart IIIAA  The Australian Energy Regulator (AER)",
      "skos:definition": "Application\n\n(1) This section applies if a State/Territory energy law or local energy\ninstrument purports to impose a duty on the AER.\nNote 1:\nSection 44AK sets out when such a law or instrument imposes a duty\non the AER.\nNote 2:\nSection 320 of the South Australian Energy Retail Legislation, as it\napplies as a law of a State or Territory, deals with the case where a\nduty purportedly imposed on a Commonwealth body under that\n\nChapter 1  Preliminary\nPart IIIAA  The Australian Energy Regulator (AER)",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44aj-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44aj-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e20c23db1d3355beb209295026c1d65853f8fb96f9dc8596af9a9baa81ff3428",
      "skos:note": "Duty imposed on AER by State/Territory energy law or local energy instrument"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44aj",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44AJ How duty is imposed",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 113,
      "values:originalText": "Application\n\n(1) This section applies if a State/Territory energy law or local energy\ninstrument purports to impose a duty on the AER.\nNote 1:\nSection 44AK sets out when such a law or instrument imposes a duty\non the AER.\nNote 2:\nSection 320 of the South Australian Energy Retail Legislation, as it\napplies as a law of a State or Territory, deals with the case where a\nduty purportedly imposed on a Commonwealth body under that\n\nChapter 1  Preliminary\nPart IIIAA  The Australian Energy Regulator (AER)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44aj-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44aj"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44aj-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "imposes",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Imposes duty on AER",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "State/Territory energy law or local energy instrument",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Obligation on AER"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44al",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44AL Powers of the AER",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44al"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.115",
      "values:originalText": "The AER has power to do all things necessary or convenient to be\ndone for or in connection with the performance of its functions.\nNote:\nState and Territory laws or instruments may also confer powers on the\nAER in respect of its functions under those laws or instruments: see\nsection 44AI.\n\nChapter 1  Preliminary\nPart IIIAA  The Australian Energy Regulator (AER)",
      "skos:definition": "The AER has power to do all things necessary or convenient to be\ndone for or in connection with the performance of its functions.\nNote:\nState and Territory laws or instruments may also confer powers on the\nAER in respect of its functions under those laws or instruments: see\nsection 44AI.\n\nChapter 1  Preliminary\nPart IIIAA  The Australian Energy Regulator (AER)",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44al-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44al-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "001eda03f57c870d0c932770f4f9ead38d99259e03b678742e758176d0fa4d8c",
      "skos:note": "The AER has power to do all things necessary or convenient."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44al",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44AL Powers of the AER",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 115,
      "values:originalText": "The AER has power to do all things necessary or convenient to be\ndone for or in connection with the performance of its functions.\nNote:\nState and Territory laws or instruments may also confer powers on the\nAER in respect of its functions under those laws or instruments: see\nsection 44AI.\n\nChapter 1  Preliminary\nPart IIIAA  The Australian Energy Regulator (AER)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44al-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44al"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44al-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "hasPower",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The AER has power.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44am",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44AM Appointment of Commonwealth AER members",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44am"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.116",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A Commonwealth AER member is to be appointed by the\nGovernor-General by written instrument, on either a full-time or\npart-time basis.\nNote:\nA Commonwealth AER member is also taken to be an associate\nmember of the Commission: see section 8AB.\n\n(2) A Commonwealth AER member holds office for the period\nspecified in the instrument of appointment. The period must not\nexceed 5 years.\n\n(3) A person is not eligible for appointment as a Commonwealth AER\nmember unless the person has knowledge of, or experience in,\nindustry, commerce, economics, law, consumer protection or\npublic administration.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A Commonwealth AER member is to be appointed by the\nGovernor-General by written instrument, on either a full-time or\npart-time basis.\nNote:\nA Commonwealth AER member is also taken to be an associate\nmember of the Commission: see section 8AB.\n\n(2) A Commonwealth AER member holds office for the period\nspecified in the instrument of appointment. The period must not\nexceed 5 years.\n\n(3) A person is not eligible for appointment as a Commonwealth AER\nmember unless the person has knowledge of, or experience in,\nindustry, commerce, economics, law, consumer protection or\npublic administration.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44am-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44am-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44am-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "35b73ecd6554f5c52b56851b75ac3250c8462a097830b5b8677bcf11c8f9b84c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44am",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44AM Appointment of Commonwealth AER members",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 116,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A Commonwealth AER member is to be appointed by the\nGovernor-General by written instrument, on either a full-time or\npart-time basis.\nNote:\nA Commonwealth AER member is also taken to be an associate\nmember of the Commission: see section 8AB.\n\n(2) A Commonwealth AER member holds office for the period\nspecified in the instrument of appointment. The period must not\nexceed 5 years.\n\n(3) A person is not eligible for appointment as a Commonwealth AER\nmember unless the person has knowledge of, or experience in,\nindustry, commerce, economics, law, consumer protection or\npublic administration."
    },
