    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ao",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44AO Acting appointment of Commonwealth AER member",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44ao"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.116",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by written instrument, appoint a person to act as\na Commonwealth AER member:\n\n(a) during a vacancy in the office of Commonwealth AER\nmember, whether or not an appointment has previously been\nmade to the office; or\n\n(b) during any period, or during all periods, when the\nCommonwealth AER member:\n\n(i) is absent from duty or from Australia; or\n\n(ii) is, for any reason, unable to perform the duties of the\noffice.\nNote:\nFor rules that apply to acting appointments, see sections 33AB and\n33A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\n\nPreliminary  Chapter 1\nThe Australian Energy Regulator (AER)  Part IIIAA\nAdministrative provisions relating to the AER  Division 4\n\nSection 44AP\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(2) A person is not eligible for appointment to act as a Commonwealth\nAER member unless the person has knowledge of, or experience\nin, industry, commerce, economics, law, consumer protection or\npublic administration.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may, by written instrument, appoint a person to act as\na Commonwealth AER member:\n\n(a) during a vacancy in the office of Commonwealth AER\nmember, whether or not an appointment has previously been\nmade to the office; or\n\n(b) during any period, or during all periods, when the\nCommonwealth AER member:\n\n(i) is absent from duty or from Australia; or\n\n(ii) is, for any reason, unable to perform the duties of the\noffice.\nNote:\nFor rules that apply to acting appointments, see sections 33AB and\n33A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\n\nPreliminary  Chapter 1\nThe Australian Energy Regulator (AER)  Part IIIAA\nAdministrative provisions relating to the AER  Division 4\n\nSection 44AP\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(2) A person is not eligible for appointment to act as a Commonwealth\nAER member unless the person has knowledge of, or experience\nin, industry, commerce, economics, law, consumer protection or\npublic administration.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ao-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ao-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "582cc66bbb3f71f0e5a28c630fa68290c5146b5ae959df933bb3be17c4e374f4"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44ao",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44AO Acting appointment of Commonwealth AER member",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 116,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by written instrument, appoint a person to act as\na Commonwealth AER member:\n\n(a) during a vacancy in the office of Commonwealth AER\nmember, whether or not an appointment has previously been\nmade to the office; or\n\n(b) during any period, or during all periods, when the\nCommonwealth AER member:\n\n(i) is absent from duty or from Australia; or\n\n(ii) is, for any reason, unable to perform the duties of the\noffice.\nNote:\nFor rules that apply to acting appointments, see sections 33AB and\n33A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\n\nPreliminary  Chapter 1\nThe Australian Energy Regulator (AER)  Part IIIAA\nAdministrative provisions relating to the AER  Division 4\n\nSection 44AP\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(2) A person is not eligible for appointment to act as a Commonwealth\nAER member unless the person has knowledge of, or experience\nin, industry, commerce, economics, law, consumer protection or\npublic administration."
    },
