    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44aq",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44AQ Acting appointment of State/Territory AER member",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44aq"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.117",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by written instrument, appoint a person to act as\na State/Territory AER member:\n\n(a) during a vacancy in the office of State/Territory AER\nmember, whether or not an appointment has previously been\nmade to the office; or\n\n(b) during any period, or during all periods, when the\nState/Territory AER member:\n\n(i) is absent from duty or from Australia; or\n\n(ii) is, for any reason, unable to perform the duties of the\noffice.\nNote:\nFor rules that apply to acting appointments, see sections 33AB and\n33A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\n\nChapter 1  Preliminary\nPart IIIAA  The Australian Energy Regulator (AER)",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may, by written instrument, appoint a person to act as\na State/Territory AER member:\n\n(a) during a vacancy in the office of State/Territory AER\nmember, whether or not an appointment has previously been\nmade to the office; or\n\n(b) during any period, or during all periods, when the\nState/Territory AER member:\n\n(i) is absent from duty or from Australia; or\n\n(ii) is, for any reason, unable to perform the duties of the\noffice.\nNote:\nFor rules that apply to acting appointments, see sections 33AB and\n33A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\n\nChapter 1  Preliminary\nPart IIIAA  The Australian Energy Regulator (AER)",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44aq-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44aq-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7ae08ff9f13fbaaa5718a01c2b4a1ebf0fc11eb8839861aae634f4b4b1f257f9",
      "skos:note": "The Minister may appoint a person to act as State/Territory AER member."
    },
