    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44as",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44AS Acting AER Deputy Chair",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44as"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.119",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by written instrument, appoint an AER member\nto act as the AER Deputy Chair:\n\n(a) during a vacancy in the office of the AER Deputy Chair,\nwhether or not an appointment has previously been made to\nthe office; or\n\n(b) during any period, or during all periods, when the AER\nDeputy Chair:\n\n(i) is absent from duty or from Australia; or\n\n(ii) is, for any reason, unable to perform the duties of the\noffice.\nNote:\nFor rules that apply to acting appointments, see sections 33AB and\n33A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\n\n(2) If a person acting as the AER Deputy Chair ceases to be an AER\nmember, then the appointment to act as the AER Deputy Chair also\nceases.\n\nChapter 1  Preliminary\nPart IIIAA  The Australian Energy Regulator (AER)",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may, by written instrument, appoint an AER member\nto act as the AER Deputy Chair:\n\n(a) during a vacancy in the office of the AER Deputy Chair,\nwhether or not an appointment has previously been made to\nthe office; or\n\n(b) during any period, or during all periods, when the AER\nDeputy Chair:\n\n(i) is absent from duty or from Australia; or\n\n(ii) is, for any reason, unable to perform the duties of the\noffice.\nNote:\nFor rules that apply to acting appointments, see sections 33AB and\n33A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\n\n(2) If a person acting as the AER Deputy Chair ceases to be an AER\nmember, then the appointment to act as the AER Deputy Chair also\nceases.\n\nChapter 1  Preliminary\nPart IIIAA  The Australian Energy Regulator (AER)",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44as-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44as-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "67bb385740b6e677625ebcbe7fb985c4bce550b0bb1f0597cc65e9058623a1b4"
    },
