    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44az-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44AZ(2) Resignation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44az-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.122",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The Governor-General may terminate the appointment of a\nfull-time AER member if:\n\n(a) the member is absent, except on leave of absence, for\n14 consecutive days or for 28 days in any 12 months; or\n\nPreliminary  Chapter 1\nThe Australian Energy Regulator (AER)  Part IIIAA\nAdministrative provisions relating to the AER  Division 4\n\nSection 44AAC\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(b) the member engages, except with the Minister’s consent, in\npaid employment outside the duties of his or her office.\nAdditional grounds: part-time AER members",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The Governor-General may terminate the appointment of a\nfull-time AER member if:\n\n(a) the member is absent, except on leave of absence, for\n14 consecutive days or for 28 days in any 12 months; or\n\nPreliminary  Chapter 1\nThe Australian Energy Regulator (AER)  Part IIIAA\nAdministrative provisions relating to the AER  Division 4\n\nSection 44AAC\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(b) the member engages, except with the Minister’s consent, in\npaid employment outside the duties of his or her office.\nAdditional grounds: part-time AER members",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44az"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44az-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44az-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44az-ss-2-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44az-ss-2-logic-linearlogic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44az-ss-2-logic-alleninterval-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4c33066b6689391ce0bbdf608c17fbb261c9a2ee3afd7475fea69e4b0a217049",
      "skos:note": "The AER Chair must provide a written resignation to the Governor-General. Determination of meeting places by the AER Chair Governor-General may terminate appointment of AER member under certain conditions.",
      "dc:description": "written resignation"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44az-ss-2",
