    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44B Definitions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.139",
      "values:originalText": "In this Part, unless the contrary intention appears:\naccess code means a code referred to in section 44ZZAA.\naccess code application means:\n\n(a) an access code given to the Commission; or\n\n(b) a request made to the Commission for the withdrawal or\nvariation of an access code; or\n\n(c) an application under subsection 44ZZBB(4) for an extension\nof the period for which an access code is in operation.\naccess code decision means:\n\n(a) a decision under section 44ZZAA to accept or reject an\naccess code; or\n\n(b) a decision under section 44ZZAA to consent or refuse to\nconsent to the withdrawal or variation of an access code; or\n\n(c) a decision under section 44ZZBB to extend or refuse to\nextend the period for which an access code is in operation.\n\nChapter 2  Access to services",
      "skos:definition": "In this Part, unless the contrary intention appears:\naccess code means a code referred to in section 44ZZAA.\naccess code application means:\n\n(a) an access code given to the Commission; or\n\n(b) a request made to the Commission for the withdrawal or\nvariation of an access code; or\n\n(c) an application under subsection 44ZZBB(4) for an extension\nof the period for which an access code is in operation.\naccess code decision means:\n\n(a) a decision under section 44ZZAA to accept or reject an\naccess code; or\n\n(b) a decision under section 44ZZAA to consent or refuse to\nconsent to the withdrawal or variation of an access code; or\n\n(c) a decision under section 44ZZBB to extend or refuse to\nextend the period for which an access code is in operation.\n\nChapter 2  Access to services",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44b-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44b-logic-descriptionlogic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "aae3b76ac0254a6414b82148244a5ff381b3e8ad05d168acfb6900f1d28d893d",
      "skos:note": "Definitions for access code and related terms."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44B Definitions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 139,
      "values:originalText": "In this Part, unless the contrary intention appears:\naccess code means a code referred to in section 44ZZAA.\naccess code application means:\n\n(a) an access code given to the Commission; or\n\n(b) a request made to the Commission for the withdrawal or\nvariation of an access code; or\n\n(c) an application under subsection 44ZZBB(4) for an extension\nof the period for which an access code is in operation.\naccess code decision means:\n\n(a) a decision under section 44ZZAA to accept or reject an\naccess code; or\n\n(b) a decision under section 44ZZAA to consent or refuse to\nconsent to the withdrawal or variation of an access code; or\n\n(c) a decision under section 44ZZBB to extend or refuse to\nextend the period for which an access code is in operation.\n\nChapter 2  Access to services"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44b-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44b"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44b-logic-descriptionlogic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:DescriptionLogic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "has definition",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Defines key terms.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::dl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44c",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44C How this Part applies to partnerships and joint ventures",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.143",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if the provider of a service is a partnership or\njoint venture that consists of 2 or more corporations. Those\ncorporations are referred to in this section as the participants.\n\n(2) If this Part requires or permits something to be done by the\nprovider, the thing may be done by one or more of the participants\non behalf of the provider.\n\n(3) If a provision of this Part refers to the provider bearing any costs,\nthe provision applies as if the provision referred to any of the\nparticipants bearing any costs.\n\nChapter 2  Access to services",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies if the provider of a service is a partnership or\njoint venture that consists of 2 or more corporations. Those\ncorporations are referred to in this section as the participants.\n\n(2) If this Part requires or permits something to be done by the\nprovider, the thing may be done by one or more of the participants\non behalf of the provider.\n\n(3) If a provision of this Part refers to the provider bearing any costs,\nthe provision applies as if the provision referred to any of the\nparticipants bearing any costs.\n\nChapter 2  Access to services",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44c-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44c-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44c-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "55dcddfaea9a30ca0cffbdf68937339446bf6e36c3a08e78596c1af8e00715ea"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44c",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44C How this Part applies to partnerships and joint ventures",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 143,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if the provider of a service is a partnership or\njoint venture that consists of 2 or more corporations. Those\ncorporations are referred to in this section as the participants.\n\n(2) If this Part requires or permits something to be done by the\nprovider, the thing may be done by one or more of the participants\non behalf of the provider.\n\n(3) If a provision of this Part refers to the provider bearing any costs,\nthe provision applies as if the provision referred to any of the\nparticipants bearing any costs.\n\nChapter 2  Access to services"
    },
