      "cml:premiseText": "(2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(b):"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ca-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44CA(3) Meaning of declaration criteria",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44ca-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.144",
      "values:originalText": "(3) Without limiting the matters to which the Council may have regard\nfor the purposes of section 44G, or the designated Minister may\nhave regard for the purposes of section 44H, in considering\nwhether paragraph (1)(d) of this section applies the Council or\ndesignated Minister must have regard to:\n\n(a) the effect that declaring the service would have on\ninvestment in:\n\n(i) infrastructure services; and\n\n(ii) markets that depend on access to the service; and\n\n(b) the administrative and compliance costs that would be\nincurred by the provider of the service if the service is\ndeclared.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) Without limiting the matters to which the Council may have regard\nfor the purposes of section 44G, or the designated Minister may\nhave regard for the purposes of section 44H, in considering\nwhether paragraph (1)(d) of this section applies the Council or\ndesignated Minister must have regard to:\n\n(a) the effect that declaring the service would have on\ninvestment in:\n\n(i) infrastructure services; and\n\n(ii) markets that depend on access to the service; and\n\n(b) the administrative and compliance costs that would be\nincurred by the provider of the service if the service is\ndeclared.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ca"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ca-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ca-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ca-ss-3-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ca-ss-3-logic-argumentation-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ca-ss-3-logic-diffusion-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ca-ss-3-logic-cogai-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "688cc72cca4815cbc8c3d7cb0df814fec8b25a66dc57e8a5d8b94fd093dcc4f6",
      "skos:note": "Council must have regard to certain factors when considering whether a service should be declared."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44ca-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44CA(3) Meaning of declaration criteria",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 144,
      "values:originalText": "(3) Without limiting the matters to which the Council may have regard\nfor the purposes of section 44G, or the designated Minister may\nhave regard for the purposes of section 44H, in considering\nwhether paragraph (1)(d) of this section applies the Council or\ndesignated Minister must have regard to:\n\n(a) the effect that declaring the service would have on\ninvestment in:\n\n(i) infrastructure services; and\n\n(ii) markets that depend on access to the service; and\n\n(b) the administrative and compliance costs that would be\nincurred by the provider of the service if the service is\ndeclared."
    },
