    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44f-ss-1a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44F(1A) Person may request recommendation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44f-ss-1a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.148",
      "values:originalText": "(1A) If the Council decides that one or more of paragraphs (1)(a) to (e)\napply for a service mentioned in a person’s purported application\nunder that subsection, the Council must give the person written\nnotice explaining:\n\nAccess to services  Chapter 2\nAccess to services  Part IIIA\nDeclared services  Division 2\n\nSection 44F\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(a) why those paragraphs apply; and\n\n(b) that such an application cannot be made for the service.",
      "skos:definition": "(1A) If the Council decides that one or more of paragraphs (1)(a) to (e)\napply for a service mentioned in a person’s purported application\nunder that subsection, the Council must give the person written\nnotice explaining:\n\nAccess to services  Chapter 2\nAccess to services  Part IIIA\nDeclared services  Division 2\n\nSection 44F\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(a) why those paragraphs apply; and\n\n(b) that such an application cannot be made for the service.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44f"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44f-ss-1a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44f-ss-1a-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "506af36e691f987672e902cfd5aab2d1ecc0bfc64484f3575d93775553bfd5cf",
      "skos:note": "Council must give written notice explaining why certain paragraphs apply and that an application cannot be made for a service.",
      "dc:description": "written notice"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44f-ss-1a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44F(1A) Person may request recommendation",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 148,
      "values:originalText": "(1A) If the Council decides that one or more of paragraphs (1)(a) to (e)\napply for a service mentioned in a person’s purported application\nunder that subsection, the Council must give the person written\nnotice explaining:\n\nAccess to services  Chapter 2\nAccess to services  Part IIIA\nDeclared services  Division 2\n\nSection 44F\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(a) why those paragraphs apply; and\n\n(b) that such an application cannot be made for the service."
    },
