    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44fa",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44FA Council may request information",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44fa"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.150",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Council may give a person a written notice requesting the\nperson give to the Council, within a specified period, information\nof the kind specified in the notice that the Council considers may\nbe relevant to deciding what recommendation to make on an\napplication under section 44F.\n\n(2) The Council must:\n\n(a) give a copy of the notice to:\n\n(i) if the person is not the applicant—the applicant; and\n\n(ii) if the person is not the provider of the service—the\nprovider; and\n\n(b) publish, by electronic or other means, the notice.\n\n(3) In deciding what recommendation to make on the application, the\nCouncil:\n\n(a) must have regard to any information given in compliance\nwith a notice under subsection (1) within the specified\nperiod; and\n\n(b) may disregard any information of the kind specified in the\nnotice that is given after the specified period has ended.\n\n(4) Subsections 44GB(4) to (6) apply to information given in response\nto a notice under this section (whether given in compliance with\nthe notice or not) in a corresponding way to the way those\nsubsections apply to a submission made in response to a notice\nunder subsection 44GB(1).\n\nAccess to services  Chapter 2\nAccess to services  Part IIIA\nDeclared services  Division 2\n\nSection 44G\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nNote:\nThis allows the Council to make the information publicly available,\nsubject to any confidentiality concerns.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Council may give a person a written notice requesting the\nperson give to the Council, within a specified period, information\nof the kind specified in the notice that the Council considers may\nbe relevant to deciding what recommendation to make on an\napplication under section 44F.\n\n(2) The Council must:\n\n(a) give a copy of the notice to:\n\n(i) if the person is not the applicant—the applicant; and\n\n(ii) if the person is not the provider of the service—the\nprovider; and\n\n(b) publish, by electronic or other means, the notice.\n\n(3) In deciding what recommendation to make on the application, the\nCouncil:\n\n(a) must have regard to any information given in compliance\nwith a notice under subsection (1) within the specified\nperiod; and\n\n(b) may disregard any information of the kind specified in the\nnotice that is given after the specified period has ended.\n\n(4) Subsections 44GB(4) to (6) apply to information given in response\nto a notice under this section (whether given in compliance with\nthe notice or not) in a corresponding way to the way those\nsubsections apply to a submission made in response to a notice\nunder subsection 44GB(1).\n\nAccess to services  Chapter 2\nAccess to services  Part IIIA\nDeclared services  Division 2\n\nSection 44G\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nNote:\nThis allows the Council to make the information publicly available,\nsubject to any confidentiality concerns.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44fa-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44fa-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44fa-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44fa-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3829e708fbfbd906692e82ef9ad5b8ec06212c55497fc9d72ded1826c1474a99"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44fa",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44FA Council may request information",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 150,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Council may give a person a written notice requesting the\nperson give to the Council, within a specified period, information\nof the kind specified in the notice that the Council considers may\nbe relevant to deciding what recommendation to make on an\napplication under section 44F.\n\n(2) The Council must:\n\n(a) give a copy of the notice to:\n\n(i) if the person is not the applicant—the applicant; and\n\n(ii) if the person is not the provider of the service—the\nprovider; and\n\n(b) publish, by electronic or other means, the notice.\n\n(3) In deciding what recommendation to make on the application, the\nCouncil:\n\n(a) must have regard to any information given in compliance\nwith a notice under subsection (1) within the specified\nperiod; and\n\n(b) may disregard any information of the kind specified in the\nnotice that is given after the specified period has ended.\n\n(4) Subsections 44GB(4) to (6) apply to information given in response\nto a notice under this section (whether given in compliance with\nthe notice or not) in a corresponding way to the way those\nsubsections apply to a submission made in response to a notice\nunder subsection 44GB(1).\n\nAccess to services  Chapter 2\nAccess to services  Part IIIA\nDeclared services  Division 2\n\nSection 44G\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nNote:\nThis allows the Council to make the information publicly available,\nsubject to any confidentiality concerns."
    },
