    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44gc-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44GC(4) Council must publish its recommendation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44gc-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.155",
      "values:originalText": "(4) Before publishing under subsection (1), the Council may give any\none or more of the following persons:\n\n(a) the applicant under section 44F;\n\n(b) if the applicant is not the provider of the service—the\nprovider;\n\n(c) any other person the Council considers appropriate;\na notice in writing:\n\n(d) specifying what the Council is proposing to publish; and\n\n(e) inviting the person to make a written submission to the\nCouncil within 14 days after the notice is given identifying\nany information the person considers should not be published\nbecause of its confidential commercial nature.\n\nChapter 2  Access to services",
      "skos:definition": "(4) Before publishing under subsection (1), the Council may give any\none or more of the following persons:\n\n(a) the applicant under section 44F;\n\n(b) if the applicant is not the provider of the service—the\nprovider;\n\n(c) any other person the Council considers appropriate;\na notice in writing:\n\n(d) specifying what the Council is proposing to publish; and\n\n(e) inviting the person to make a written submission to the\nCouncil within 14 days after the notice is given identifying\nany information the person considers should not be published\nbecause of its confidential commercial nature.\n\nChapter 2  Access to services",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44gc"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44gc-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44gc-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "64abaaff14feaa411fe3cb18d0c4a7ad4c8db0de6a4d1a6a011ed30da9245c7c",
      "skos:note": "The Council may give notice to the applicant and provider before publishing its recommendation."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44gc-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44GC(4) Council must publish its recommendation",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 155,
      "values:originalText": "(4) Before publishing under subsection (1), the Council may give any\none or more of the following persons:\n\n(a) the applicant under section 44F;\n\n(b) if the applicant is not the provider of the service—the\nprovider;\n\n(c) any other person the Council considers appropriate;\na notice in writing:\n\n(d) specifying what the Council is proposing to publish; and\n\n(e) inviting the person to make a written submission to the\nCouncil within 14 days after the notice is given identifying\nany information the person considers should not be published\nbecause of its confidential commercial nature.\n\nChapter 2  Access to services"
    },
