    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44h-ss-9",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44H(9) Designated Minister may declare a service",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44h-ss-9"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.156",
      "values:originalText": "(9) If the designated Minister does not publish under section 44HA his\nor her decision on the declaration recommendation within 60 days\nafter receiving the declaration recommendation, the designated\nMinister is taken, at the end of that 60-day period:\n\n(a) to have made a decision under this section in accordance with\nthe declaration recommendation; and\n\n(b) to have published that decision under section 44HA.",
      "skos:definition": "(9) If the designated Minister does not publish under section 44HA his\nor her decision on the declaration recommendation within 60 days\nafter receiving the declaration recommendation, the designated\nMinister is taken, at the end of that 60-day period:\n\n(a) to have made a decision under this section in accordance with\nthe declaration recommendation; and\n\n(b) to have published that decision under section 44HA.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44h"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44h-ss-9-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44h-ss-9-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44h-ss-9-logic-alleninterval-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "90817e260cb7a0d77c31c507c44b1f2a9ada2777c0597dde67518169c3467886",
      "skos:note": "Designated Minister must publish decision within 60 days or be deemed to have made a decision in accordance with the declaration recommendation."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44h-ss-9",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44H(9) Designated Minister may declare a service",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 156,
      "values:originalText": "(9) If the designated Minister does not publish under section 44HA his\nor her decision on the declaration recommendation within 60 days\nafter receiving the declaration recommendation, the designated\nMinister is taken, at the end of that 60-day period:\n\n(a) to have made a decision under this section in accordance with\nthe declaration recommendation; and\n\n(b) to have published that decision under section 44HA."
    },
