    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ha",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44HA Designated Minister must publish his or her decision",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44ha"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.156",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The designated Minister must publish, by electronic or other\nmeans, his or her decision on a declaration recommendation and\nhis or her reasons for the decision.\n\n(2) The designated Minister must give a copy of the publication to:\n\n(a) the applicant under section 44F; and\n\nAccess to services  Chapter 2\nAccess to services  Part IIIA\nDeclared services  Division 2\n\nSection 44I\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(b) if the applicant is not the provider of the service—the\nprovider.\nConsultation\n\n(3) Before publishing under subsection (1), the designated Minister\nmay give any one or more of the following persons:\n\n(a) the applicant under section 44F;\n\n(b) if the applicant is not the provider of the service—the\nprovider;\n\n(c) any other person the designated Minister considers\nappropriate;\na notice in writing:\n\n(d) specifying what the designated Minister is proposing to\npublish; and\n\n(e) inviting the person to make a written submission to the\ndesignated Minister within 14 days after the notice is given\nidentifying any information the person considers should not\nbe published because of its confidential commercial nature.\n\n(4) The designated Minister must have regard to any submission so\nmade in deciding what to publish. He or she may have regard to\nany other matter he or she considers relevant.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The designated Minister must publish, by electronic or other\nmeans, his or her decision on a declaration recommendation and\nhis or her reasons for the decision.\n\n(2) The designated Minister must give a copy of the publication to:\n\n(a) the applicant under section 44F; and\n\nAccess to services  Chapter 2\nAccess to services  Part IIIA\nDeclared services  Division 2\n\nSection 44I\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(b) if the applicant is not the provider of the service—the\nprovider.\nConsultation\n\n(3) Before publishing under subsection (1), the designated Minister\nmay give any one or more of the following persons:\n\n(a) the applicant under section 44F;\n\n(b) if the applicant is not the provider of the service—the\nprovider;\n\n(c) any other person the designated Minister considers\nappropriate;\na notice in writing:\n\n(d) specifying what the designated Minister is proposing to\npublish; and\n\n(e) inviting the person to make a written submission to the\ndesignated Minister within 14 days after the notice is given\nidentifying any information the person considers should not\nbe published because of its confidential commercial nature.\n\n(4) The designated Minister must have regard to any submission so\nmade in deciding what to publish. He or she may have regard to\nany other matter he or she considers relevant.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ha-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ha-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ha-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ha-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8ab50593b86be469cf865bc52c7b5c16d40a83a2fcb35edfbeb18ae59cf6436e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44ha",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44HA Designated Minister must publish his or her decision",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 156,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The designated Minister must publish, by electronic or other\nmeans, his or her decision on a declaration recommendation and\nhis or her reasons for the decision.\n\n(2) The designated Minister must give a copy of the publication to:\n\n(a) the applicant under section 44F; and\n\nAccess to services  Chapter 2\nAccess to services  Part IIIA\nDeclared services  Division 2\n\nSection 44I\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(b) if the applicant is not the provider of the service—the\nprovider.\nConsultation\n\n(3) Before publishing under subsection (1), the designated Minister\nmay give any one or more of the following persons:\n\n(a) the applicant under section 44F;\n\n(b) if the applicant is not the provider of the service—the\nprovider;\n\n(c) any other person the designated Minister considers\nappropriate;\na notice in writing:\n\n(d) specifying what the designated Minister is proposing to\npublish; and\n\n(e) inviting the person to make a written submission to the\ndesignated Minister within 14 days after the notice is given\nidentifying any information the person considers should not\nbe published because of its confidential commercial nature.\n\n(4) The designated Minister must have regard to any submission so\nmade in deciding what to publish. He or she may have regard to\nany other matter he or she considers relevant."
    },
