    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44j-ss-7",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44J(7) Revocation of declaration",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44j-ss-7"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.158",
      "values:originalText": "(7) If the designated Minister does not publish under subsection (4) his\nor her decision on the revocation recommendation within the\nperiod starting at the start of the day the recommendation is\nreceived and ending at the end of 60 days after that day, the\ndesignated Minister is taken, immediately after the end of that\n60-day period:\n\n(a) to have made a decision that the declaration be revoked; and\n\n(b) to have published that decision in accordance with this\nsection.",
      "skos:definition": "(7) If the designated Minister does not publish under subsection (4) his\nor her decision on the revocation recommendation within the\nperiod starting at the start of the day the recommendation is\nreceived and ending at the end of 60 days after that day, the\ndesignated Minister is taken, immediately after the end of that\n60-day period:\n\n(a) to have made a decision that the declaration be revoked; and\n\n(b) to have published that decision in accordance with this\nsection.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44j"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44j-ss-7-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44j-ss-7-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44j-ss-7-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44j-ss-7-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44j-ss-7-logic-deontic-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0431364543b267fd9fcfe1e9824ffe726919f7b33c8766c12cc7729ce0e4cc94",
      "skos:note": "Failure to publish decision within 60 days results in automatic revocation of declaration."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44j-ss-7",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44J(7) Revocation of declaration",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 158,
      "values:originalText": "(7) If the designated Minister does not publish under subsection (4) his\nor her decision on the revocation recommendation within the\nperiod starting at the start of the day the recommendation is\nreceived and ending at the end of 60 days after that day, the\ndesignated Minister is taken, immediately after the end of that\n60-day period:\n\n(a) to have made a decision that the declaration be revoked; and\n\n(b) to have published that decision in accordance with this\nsection."
    },
