    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44k",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44K Review of declaration",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44k"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.159",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the designated Minister declares a service, the provider may\napply in writing to the Tribunal for review of the declaration.\n\n(2) If the designated Minister decides not to declare a service, an\napplication in writing for review of the designated Minister’s\ndecision may be made by the person who applied for the\ndeclaration recommendation.\n\n(3) An application for review must be made within 21 days after\npublication of the designated Minister’s decision.\n\n(4) The review by the Tribunal is a re-consideration of the matter\nbased on the information, reports and things referred to in\nsection 44ZZOAA.\nNote:\nThere are limits on the information to which the Tribunal may have\nregard (see section 44ZZOAA) and time limits that apply to the\nTribunal’s decision on the review (see section 44ZZOA).\n\n(5) For the purposes of the review, the Tribunal has the same powers\nas the designated Minister.\n\nChapter 2  Access to services",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If the designated Minister declares a service, the provider may\napply in writing to the Tribunal for review of the declaration.\n\n(2) If the designated Minister decides not to declare a service, an\napplication in writing for review of the designated Minister’s\ndecision may be made by the person who applied for the\ndeclaration recommendation.\n\n(3) An application for review must be made within 21 days after\npublication of the designated Minister’s decision.\n\n(4) The review by the Tribunal is a re-consideration of the matter\nbased on the information, reports and things referred to in\nsection 44ZZOAA.\nNote:\nThere are limits on the information to which the Tribunal may have\nregard (see section 44ZZOAA) and time limits that apply to the\nTribunal’s decision on the review (see section 44ZZOA).\n\n(5) For the purposes of the review, the Tribunal has the same powers\nas the designated Minister.\n\nChapter 2  Access to services",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44k-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44k-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44k-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44k-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44k-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6c85b25add714999d9ad0e966b12bedea782c4c2d588c742f627dbdfd651e94e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44k",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44K Review of declaration",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 159,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the designated Minister declares a service, the provider may\napply in writing to the Tribunal for review of the declaration.\n\n(2) If the designated Minister decides not to declare a service, an\napplication in writing for review of the designated Minister’s\ndecision may be made by the person who applied for the\ndeclaration recommendation.\n\n(3) An application for review must be made within 21 days after\npublication of the designated Minister’s decision.\n\n(4) The review by the Tribunal is a re-consideration of the matter\nbased on the information, reports and things referred to in\nsection 44ZZOAA.\nNote:\nThere are limits on the information to which the Tribunal may have\nregard (see section 44ZZOAA) and time limits that apply to the\nTribunal’s decision on the review (see section 44ZZOA).\n\n(5) For the purposes of the review, the Tribunal has the same powers\nas the designated Minister.\n\nChapter 2  Access to services"
    },
