      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.162",
      "values:originalText": "(2) However, the Tribunal must not make an order requiring the\ndesignated Minister to pay some or all of the costs of another party\nto proceedings unless the Tribunal considers that the designated\nMinister’s conduct in the proceedings was engaged in without due\nregard to:\n\nAccess to services  Chapter 2\nAccess to services  Part IIIA\nDeclared services  Division 2\n\nSection 44L\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(a) the costs that would be incurred by the other party to the\nproceedings as a result of that conduct; or\n\n(b) the time required by the Tribunal to make a decision on the\nreview as a result of that conduct; or\n\n(c) the time required by the other party to prepare their case for\nthe purposes of the review as a result of that conduct; or\n\n(d) the submissions or arguments made during the proceedings to\nthe Tribunal by the other party or parties to the proceedings\nor by the Council.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) However, the Tribunal must not make an order requiring the\ndesignated Minister to pay some or all of the costs of another party\nto proceedings unless the Tribunal considers that the designated\nMinister’s conduct in the proceedings was engaged in without due\nregard to:\n\nAccess to services  Chapter 2\nAccess to services  Part IIIA\nDeclared services  Division 2\n\nSection 44L\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(a) the costs that would be incurred by the other party to the\nproceedings as a result of that conduct; or\n\n(b) the time required by the Tribunal to make a decision on the\nreview as a result of that conduct; or\n\n(c) the time required by the other party to prepare their case for\nthe purposes of the review as a result of that conduct; or\n\n(d) the submissions or arguments made during the proceedings to\nthe Tribunal by the other party or parties to the proceedings\nor by the Council.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44kb"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44kb-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44kb-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f7add5bda7f8bf75aa9dee4ea956c132ceaa050c62dda01f7b8bb8367bfaf672",
      "skos:note": "The Tribunal must consider the costs incurred by another party before ordering the designated Minister to pay some or all of those costs."
