    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44l",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44L Review of decision not to revoke a declaration",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44l"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.163",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the designated Minister decides not to revoke a declaration, the\nprovider may apply in writing to the Tribunal for review of the\ndecision.\n\n(2) An application for review must be made within 21 days after\npublication of the designated Minister’s decision.\n\n(3) The review by the Tribunal is a re-consideration of the matter\nbased on the information, reports and things referred to in\nsection 44ZZOAA.\nNote:\nThere are limits on the information to which the Tribunal may have\nregard (see section 44ZZOAA) and time limits that apply to the\nTribunal’s decision on the review (see section 44ZZOA).\n\nChapter 2  Access to services",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If the designated Minister decides not to revoke a declaration, the\nprovider may apply in writing to the Tribunal for review of the\ndecision.\n\n(2) An application for review must be made within 21 days after\npublication of the designated Minister’s decision.\n\n(3) The review by the Tribunal is a re-consideration of the matter\nbased on the information, reports and things referred to in\nsection 44ZZOAA.\nNote:\nThere are limits on the information to which the Tribunal may have\nregard (see section 44ZZOAA) and time limits that apply to the\nTribunal’s decision on the review (see section 44ZZOA).\n\nChapter 2  Access to services",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44l-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44l-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44l-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "07f7fe3f1d37d717ed0b4848f20876352449f6bfe37ca627302c24e062c4ef13"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44l",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44L Review of decision not to revoke a declaration",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 163,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the designated Minister decides not to revoke a declaration, the\nprovider may apply in writing to the Tribunal for review of the\ndecision.\n\n(2) An application for review must be made within 21 days after\npublication of the designated Minister’s decision.\n\n(3) The review by the Tribunal is a re-consideration of the matter\nbased on the information, reports and things referred to in\nsection 44ZZOAA.\nNote:\nThere are limits on the information to which the Tribunal may have\nregard (see section 44ZZOAA) and time limits that apply to the\nTribunal’s decision on the review (see section 44ZZOA).\n\nChapter 2  Access to services"
    },
