        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e4c74eac6d148d71095257671337efcac26f159db39248e2ccc50d4e44942312",
      "skos:note": "Recommendation of ineligibility for a declared service"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44lb-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44LB(2) Ineligibility recommendation",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 165,
      "values:originalText": "(2) After receiving the application, the Council must, after having\nregard to the objects of this Part:\n\n(a) recommend to the designated Minister:\n\n(i) that he or she decide that the service is ineligible to be a\ndeclared service; and\n\n(ii) the period for which the decision should be in force\n(which must be at least 20 years); or\n\nChapter 2  Access to services"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44lb-ss-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
