    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44lg-ss-5-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Must",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The designated Minister must be satisfied of certain matters.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(5) The designated Minister must not decide that the service is\nineligible to be a declared service unless he or she is satisfied of\nboth of the following matters:"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44lg-ss-5-logic-deontic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Must",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The designated Minister must be satisfied of at least one declaration criterion.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(5) The designated Minister must not decide that the service is\nineligible to be a declared service unless he or she is satisfied of\nboth of the following matters:\n\n(a) that the service is to be provided by means of the proposed\nfacility when constructed;\n\n(b) that he or she is not satisfied of at least one of the declaration\ncriteria for the service to be provided by means of the\nproposed facility."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44lg-ss-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44LG(6) Designated Minister’s decision on ineligibility",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44lg-ss-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.172",
      "values:originalText": "(6) If the designated Minister does not publish under section 44LH his\nor her decision on the ineligibility recommendation within the\nperiod starting at the start of the day the recommendation is\nreceived and ending at the end of 60 days after that day:\n\n(a) the designated Minister is taken, immediately after the end of\nthat 60-day period, to have made a decision under\nsubsection (1) in accordance with the ineligibility\nrecommendation and to have published that decision under\nsection 44LH; and\n\n(b) if the Council recommended that the designated Minister\ndecide that the service be ineligible to be a declared\nservice—the period for which the decision is in force is taken\nto be the period recommended by the Council.\n\nChapter 2  Access to services",
      "skos:definition": "(6) If the designated Minister does not publish under section 44LH his\nor her decision on the ineligibility recommendation within the\nperiod starting at the start of the day the recommendation is\nreceived and ending at the end of 60 days after that day:\n\n(a) the designated Minister is taken, immediately after the end of\nthat 60-day period, to have made a decision under\nsubsection (1) in accordance with the ineligibility\nrecommendation and to have published that decision under\nsection 44LH; and\n\n(b) if the Council recommended that the designated Minister\ndecide that the service be ineligible to be a declared\nservice—the period for which the decision is in force is taken\nto be the period recommended by the Council.\n\nChapter 2  Access to services",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44lg"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44lg-ss-6-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44lg-ss-6-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e7265d7a9662630255c645710babc3624d842de16bbc2803a4c5d97132ecd026",
      "skos:note": "Designated Minister must publish decision on ineligibility within 60 days."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44lg-ss-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44LG(6) Designated Minister’s decision on ineligibility",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 172,
      "values:originalText": "(6) If the designated Minister does not publish under section 44LH his\nor her decision on the ineligibility recommendation within the\nperiod starting at the start of the day the recommendation is\nreceived and ending at the end of 60 days after that day:\n\n(a) the designated Minister is taken, immediately after the end of\nthat 60-day period, to have made a decision under\nsubsection (1) in accordance with the ineligibility\nrecommendation and to have published that decision under\nsection 44LH; and\n\n(b) if the Council recommended that the designated Minister\ndecide that the service be ineligible to be a declared\nservice—the period for which the decision is in force is taken\nto be the period recommended by the Council.\n\nChapter 2  Access to services"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44lg-ss-6-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44lg-ss-6"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
