      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Must publish decision",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44lh",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44LH Designated Minister must publish his or her decision",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44lh"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.174",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The designated Minister must publish, by electronic or other\nmeans, his or her decision on an ineligibility recommendation and\nhis or her reasons for the decision.\n\n(2) The designated Minister must give a copy of the publication to the\nperson who made the application under section 44LB.\nConsultation\n\n(3) Before publishing under subsection (1), the designated Minister\nmay give any one or more of the following persons:\n\n(a) the person who made the application under section 44LB;\n\n(b) any other person the designated Minister considers\nappropriate;\na notice in writing:\n\n(c) specifying what the designated Minister is proposing to\npublish; and\n\n(d) inviting the person to make a written submission to the\ndesignated Minister within 14 days after the day the notice is\ngiven identifying any information the person considers\nshould not be published because of its confidential\ncommercial nature.\n\n(4) The designated Minister must have regard to any submission so\nmade in deciding what to publish. He or she may have regard to\nany other matter he or she considers relevant.\nSubdivision D—Revocation of ineligibility decision",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The designated Minister must publish, by electronic or other\nmeans, his or her decision on an ineligibility recommendation and\nhis or her reasons for the decision.\n\n(2) The designated Minister must give a copy of the publication to the\nperson who made the application under section 44LB.\nConsultation\n\n(3) Before publishing under subsection (1), the designated Minister\nmay give any one or more of the following persons:\n\n(a) the person who made the application under section 44LB;\n\n(b) any other person the designated Minister considers\nappropriate;\na notice in writing:\n\n(c) specifying what the designated Minister is proposing to\npublish; and\n\n(d) inviting the person to make a written submission to the\ndesignated Minister within 14 days after the day the notice is\ngiven identifying any information the person considers\nshould not be published because of its confidential\ncommercial nature.\n\n(4) The designated Minister must have regard to any submission so\nmade in deciding what to publish. He or she may have regard to\nany other matter he or she considers relevant.\nSubdivision D—Revocation of ineligibility decision",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44lh-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44lh-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44lh-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44lh-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "af4b9db69c0ce8775f6adc5228ee69c1f515a0eed28fb23cc438a70c7f30db3f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44lh",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44LH Designated Minister must publish his or her decision",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 174,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The designated Minister must publish, by electronic or other\nmeans, his or her decision on an ineligibility recommendation and\nhis or her reasons for the decision.\n\n(2) The designated Minister must give a copy of the publication to the\nperson who made the application under section 44LB.\nConsultation\n\n(3) Before publishing under subsection (1), the designated Minister\nmay give any one or more of the following persons:\n\n(a) the person who made the application under section 44LB;\n\n(b) any other person the designated Minister considers\nappropriate;\na notice in writing:\n\n(c) specifying what the designated Minister is proposing to\npublish; and\n\n(d) inviting the person to make a written submission to the\ndesignated Minister within 14 days after the day the notice is\ngiven identifying any information the person considers\nshould not be published because of its confidential\ncommercial nature.\n\n(4) The designated Minister must have regard to any submission so\nmade in deciding what to publish. He or she may have regard to\nany other matter he or she considers relevant.\nSubdivision D—Revocation of ineligibility decision"
    },
