        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44lh-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "de2853585befdea1084a8343843861175b222f4b0c153877e1785a796629896a",
      "skos:note": "Designated Minister may give notice to persons before publishing decision."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44lh-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44LH(3) Designated Minister must publish his or her decision",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 174,
      "values:originalText": "(3) Before publishing under subsection (1), the designated Minister\nmay give any one or more of the following persons:\n\n(a) the person who made the application under section 44LB;\n\n(b) any other person the designated Minister considers\nappropriate;\na notice in writing:\n\n(c) specifying what the designated Minister is proposing to\npublish; and\n\n(d) inviting the person to make a written submission to the\ndesignated Minister within 14 days after the day the notice is\ngiven identifying any information the person considers\nshould not be published because of its confidential\ncommercial nature."
    },
