      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.174",
      "values:originalText": "(6) If the designated Minister decides not to revoke the ineligibility\ndecision, the designated Minister must give reasons for the\ndecision to the person who is, or expects to be, the provider of the\nservice concerned when the designated Minister publishes the\ndecision.\n\nChapter 2  Access to services",
      "skos:definition": "(6) If the designated Minister decides not to revoke the ineligibility\ndecision, the designated Minister must give reasons for the\ndecision to the person who is, or expects to be, the provider of the\nservice concerned when the designated Minister publishes the\ndecision.\n\nChapter 2  Access to services",
