    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44lk-ss-8",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44LK(8) Review of decision to revoke or not revoke an ineligibility",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44lk-ss-8"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.178",
      "values:originalText": "(8) If the designated Minister decided to revoke his or her decision\n(the ineligibility decision) that the service is ineligible to be a\ndeclared service, the Tribunal may either:\n\n(a) affirm the designated Minister’s decision; or\n\n(b) set aside the designated Minister’s decision to revoke the\nineligibility decision.",
      "skos:definition": "(8) If the designated Minister decided to revoke his or her decision\n(the ineligibility decision) that the service is ineligible to be a\ndeclared service, the Tribunal may either:\n\n(a) affirm the designated Minister’s decision; or\n\n(b) set aside the designated Minister’s decision to revoke the\nineligibility decision.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44lk"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44lk-ss-8-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44lk-ss-8-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "53d8d9ea2e802baf000d8ae37864e1e224569ad9209eceaf8d874652421c16c0",
      "skos:note": "Tribunal may affirm or set aside designated Minister's decision to revoke ineligibility"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44lk-ss-8",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44LK(8) Review of decision to revoke or not revoke an ineligibility",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 178,
      "values:originalText": "(8) If the designated Minister decided to revoke his or her decision\n(the ineligibility decision) that the service is ineligible to be a\ndeclared service, the Tribunal may either:\n\n(a) affirm the designated Minister’s decision; or\n\n(b) set aside the designated Minister’s decision to revoke the\nineligibility decision."
    },
