      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.178",
      "values:originalText": "(9) If the designated Minister decided not to revoke his or her\nineligibility decision, the Tribunal may either:\n\n(a) affirm the designated Minister’s decision; or\n\n(b) set aside the designated Minister’s decision and revoke the\nineligibility decision.\n\nChapter 2  Access to services",
      "skos:definition": "(9) If the designated Minister decided not to revoke his or her\nineligibility decision, the Tribunal may either:\n\n(a) affirm the designated Minister’s decision; or\n\n(b) set aside the designated Minister’s decision and revoke the\nineligibility decision.\n\nChapter 2  Access to services",
      "values:partOf": {
