    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44na-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44NA(5) Recommendation by Council",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44na-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.184",
      "values:originalText": "(5) If the Council is satisfied that it is an effective access regime, the\nCouncil must, in writing, recommend to the Commonwealth\nMinister that he or she extend the period for which the decision\nunder section 44N is in force. The Council must also recommend\nan extension period.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) If the Council is satisfied that it is an effective access regime, the\nCouncil must, in writing, recommend to the Commonwealth\nMinister that he or she extend the period for which the decision\nunder section 44N is in force. The Council must also recommend\nan extension period.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44na"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44na-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44na-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "364aa21daf990317d4c9b47a1e840cb53bdf3142b63685ce96b1779798425502",
      "skos:note": "Council must recommend extension period to Commonwealth Minister"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44na-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44NA(5) Recommendation by Council",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 184,
      "values:originalText": "(5) If the Council is satisfied that it is an effective access regime, the\nCouncil must, in writing, recommend to the Commonwealth\nMinister that he or she extend the period for which the decision\nunder section 44N is in force. The Council must also recommend\nan extension period."
    },
    {
