    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44na-ss-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44NA(6) Recommendation by Council",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44na-ss-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.184",
      "values:originalText": "(6) If the Council is satisfied that it is not an effective access regime,\nthe Council must, in writing, recommend to the Commonwealth\nMinister that he or she not extend the period for which the decision\nunder section 44N is in force.\n\nAccess to services  Chapter 2\nAccess to services  Part IIIA\nEffective access regimes  Division 2A\n\nSection 44NAA\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nNote 1:\nThere are time limits that apply to the Council’s recommendation: see\nsection 44NC.\nNote 2:\nThe Council may request information and invite public submissions\non the application: see sections 44NAA and 44NE.\nNote 3:\nThe Council must publish its recommendation: see section 44NF.\n44NAA  Council may request information",
      "skos:definition": "(6) If the Council is satisfied that it is not an effective access regime,\nthe Council must, in writing, recommend to the Commonwealth\nMinister that he or she not extend the period for which the decision\nunder section 44N is in force.\n\nAccess to services  Chapter 2\nAccess to services  Part IIIA\nEffective access regimes  Division 2A\n\nSection 44NAA\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nNote 1:\nThere are time limits that apply to the Council’s recommendation: see\nsection 44NC.\nNote 2:\nThe Council may request information and invite public submissions\non the application: see sections 44NAA and 44NE.\nNote 3:\nThe Council must publish its recommendation: see section 44NF.\n44NAA  Council may request information",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44na"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44na-ss-6-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44na-ss-6-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "47ac1092637ce8bf358f0a66fc9f328a5735d2dab18620560f1531f2964fe633",
      "skos:note": "Council must recommend not extending period for decision under section 44N if it is not an effective access regime."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44na-ss-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44NA(6) Recommendation by Council",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 184,
      "values:originalText": "(6) If the Council is satisfied that it is not an effective access regime,\nthe Council must, in writing, recommend to the Commonwealth\nMinister that he or she not extend the period for which the decision\nunder section 44N is in force.\n\nAccess to services  Chapter 2\nAccess to services  Part IIIA\nEffective access regimes  Division 2A\n\nSection 44NAA\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nNote 1:\nThere are time limits that apply to the Council’s recommendation: see\nsection 44NC.\nNote 2:\nThe Council may request information and invite public submissions\non the application: see sections 44NAA and 44NE.\nNote 3:\nThe Council must publish its recommendation: see section 44NF.\n44NAA  Council may request information"
    },
