      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ng-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44NG(3) Publication—Commonwealth Minister",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44ng-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.195",
      "values:originalText": "(3) Before publishing under subsection (1), the Commonwealth\nMinister may give any one or more of the following persons:\n\n(a) the applicant under section 44M or 44NA, or under\nsection 44NBA (unless the recommendation relates to a\nconsideration by the Council under that section on its own\ninitiative);\n\n(b) the provider of the service;\n\n(c) any other person the Minister considers appropriate;\na notice in writing:\n\n(d) specifying what the Minister is proposing to publish; and\n\n(e) inviting the person to make a written submission to the\nMinister within 14 days after the notice is given identifying\nany information the person considers should not be published\nbecause of its confidential commercial nature.\n\nChapter 2  Access to services",
      "skos:definition": "(3) Before publishing under subsection (1), the Commonwealth\nMinister may give any one or more of the following persons:\n\n(a) the applicant under section 44M or 44NA, or under\nsection 44NBA (unless the recommendation relates to a\nconsideration by the Council under that section on its own\ninitiative);\n\n(b) the provider of the service;\n\n(c) any other person the Minister considers appropriate;\na notice in writing:\n\n(d) specifying what the Minister is proposing to publish; and\n\n(e) inviting the person to make a written submission to the\nMinister within 14 days after the notice is given identifying\nany information the person considers should not be published\nbecause of its confidential commercial nature.\n\nChapter 2  Access to services",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ng"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ng-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ng-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ng-ss-3-logic-deontic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2ebd7b1bc53a2dc03051569b512d248f916b9bb9c506ce51ea628ae2f1343458",
      "skos:note": "Notice must be given to persons before publishing under subsection (1)",
      "dc:description": "(a) the applicant under section 44M or 44NA, or under section 44NBA; (b) the provider of the service; (c) any other person the Minister considers appropriate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44ng-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44NG(3) Publication—Commonwealth Minister",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 195,
      "values:originalText": "(3) Before publishing under subsection (1), the Commonwealth\nMinister may give any one or more of the following persons:\n\n(a) the applicant under section 44M or 44NA, or under\nsection 44NBA (unless the recommendation relates to a\nconsideration by the Council under that section on its own\ninitiative);\n\n(b) the provider of the service;\n\n(c) any other person the Minister considers appropriate;\na notice in writing:\n\n(d) specifying what the Minister is proposing to publish; and\n\n(e) inviting the person to make a written submission to the\nMinister within 14 days after the notice is given identifying\nany information the person considers should not be published\nbecause of its confidential commercial nature.\n\nChapter 2  Access to services"
    },
