    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44pb",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44PB Report on conduct of tender process",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44pb"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.201",
      "values:originalText": "Report\n\n(1) If the Commission approves a tender process as a competitive\ntender process, it must, after a tenderer is chosen, ask the applicant\nunder subsection 44PA(1), by notice in writing, to give the\nCommission a written report on the conduct of the tender process.\n\n(2) The report must be in accordance with the regulations.\nCommission may ask for further information\n\n(3) After the Commission receives the report, it may ask the applicant\nunder subsection 44PA(1), by notice in writing, to give the\nCommission further information in relation to the conduct of the\ntender process.\nLegislation Act 2003\n\n(4) A report under subsection (1) is not a legislative instrument.",
      "skos:definition": "Report\n\n(1) If the Commission approves a tender process as a competitive\ntender process, it must, after a tenderer is chosen, ask the applicant\nunder subsection 44PA(1), by notice in writing, to give the\nCommission a written report on the conduct of the tender process.\n\n(2) The report must be in accordance with the regulations.\nCommission may ask for further information\n\n(3) After the Commission receives the report, it may ask the applicant\nunder subsection 44PA(1), by notice in writing, to give the\nCommission further information in relation to the conduct of the\ntender process.\nLegislation Act 2003\n\n(4) A report under subsection (1) is not a legislative instrument.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44pb-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44pb-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44pb-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44pb-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b6ce788d9786917c9d19adaa0d904213365607c7f683d7277f508dcf142b4cc2"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44pb",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44PB Report on conduct of tender process",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 201,
      "values:originalText": "Report\n\n(1) If the Commission approves a tender process as a competitive\ntender process, it must, after a tenderer is chosen, ask the applicant\nunder subsection 44PA(1), by notice in writing, to give the\nCommission a written report on the conduct of the tender process.\n\n(2) The report must be in accordance with the regulations.\nCommission may ask for further information\n\n(3) After the Commission receives the report, it may ask the applicant\nunder subsection 44PA(1), by notice in writing, to give the\nCommission further information in relation to the conduct of the\ntender process.\nLegislation Act 2003\n\n(4) A report under subsection (1) is not a legislative instrument."
    },
