    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44pc",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44PC Revocation of approval decision",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44pc"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.201",
      "values:originalText": "Discretionary revocation\n\n(1) The Commission may, by writing, revoke a decision to approve a\ntender process as a competitive tender process if it is satisfied that\nthe assessment of the tenders was not in accordance with that\nprocess.\n\nChapter 2  Access to services",
      "skos:definition": "Discretionary revocation\n\n(1) The Commission may, by writing, revoke a decision to approve a\ntender process as a competitive tender process if it is satisfied that\nthe assessment of the tenders was not in accordance with that\nprocess.\n\nChapter 2  Access to services",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44pc-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44pc-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "304d241c816fd0e68087b6a001d8fb40e56b43a009d1dc33804da02bbc852678",
      "skos:note": "Revocation of approval decision"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44pc",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44PC Revocation of approval decision",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 201,
      "values:originalText": "Discretionary revocation\n\n(1) The Commission may, by writing, revoke a decision to approve a\ntender process as a competitive tender process if it is satisfied that\nthe assessment of the tenders was not in accordance with that\nprocess.\n\nChapter 2  Access to services"
    },
    {
