    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44pd",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44PD Time limit for Commission decisions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44pd"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.203",
      "values:originalText": "Commission to make decision within 90 days\n\n(1) The Commission must make a decision on an application under\nsubsection 44PA(1) within the period of 90 days (the expected\nperiod) starting at the start of the day the application is received.\nStopping the clock\n\n(2) In working out the expected period in relation to a decision on an\napplication under subsection 44PA(1), in a situation referred to in\ncolumn 1 of an item of the following table, disregard any day in a\nperiod:\n\n(a) starting on the day referred to in column 2 of the item; and\n\n(b) ending on the day referred to in column 3 of the item.\n\nStopping the clock\nItem\nColumn 1\nSituation\nColumn 2\nStart day\nColumn 3\nEnd day\nAn agreement is\nmade in relation to\nthe application under\nsubsection (4)\nThe first day\nof the period\nspecified in\nthe agreement\nThe last day of the period\nspecified in the agreement\n\nChapter 2  Access to services",
      "skos:definition": "Commission to make decision within 90 days\n\n(1) The Commission must make a decision on an application under\nsubsection 44PA(1) within the period of 90 days (the expected\nperiod) starting at the start of the day the application is received.\nStopping the clock\n\n(2) In working out the expected period in relation to a decision on an\napplication under subsection 44PA(1), in a situation referred to in\ncolumn 1 of an item of the following table, disregard any day in a\nperiod:\n\n(a) starting on the day referred to in column 2 of the item; and\n\n(b) ending on the day referred to in column 3 of the item.\n\nStopping the clock\nItem\nColumn 1\nSituation\nColumn 2\nStart day\nColumn 3\nEnd day\nAn agreement is\nmade in relation to\nthe application under\nsubsection (4)\nThe first day\nof the period\nspecified in\nthe agreement\nThe last day of the period\nspecified in the agreement\n\nChapter 2  Access to services",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44pd-ss-1"
        },
