    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44pe",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44PE Commission may invite public submissions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44pe"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.205",
      "values:originalText": "Invitation\n\n(1) The Commission may publish, by electronic or other means, a\nnotice inviting public submissions:\n\n(a) on an application under subsection 44PA(1); or\n\n(b) on any proposed decision under subsection 44PC(1) or (2) to\nrevoke a decision under subsection 44PA(3) to approve a\ntender process as a competitive tender process;\nif it considers that it is appropriate and practicable to do so.\n\n(2) The notice must specify how submissions may be made and the\nday by which submissions may be made (which must be at least 14\ndays after the day the notice is published).\nConsideration of submissions\n\n(3) Subject to subsection (6), in making its decision, the Commission:\n\n(a) must have regard to any submission made on or before the\nday specified in the notice; and\n\n(b) may disregard any submission made after the day specified in\nthe notice.\nCommission may make submissions publicly available\n\n(4) The Commission may make any written submission, or a written\nrecord (which may be a summary) of any oral submission, publicly\navailable.\nConfidentiality\n\n(5) A person may, at the time of making a submission, request that the\nCommission:\n\nChapter 2  Access to services",
      "skos:definition": "Invitation\n\n(1) The Commission may publish, by electronic or other means, a\nnotice inviting public submissions:\n\n(a) on an application under subsection 44PA(1); or\n\n(b) on any proposed decision under subsection 44PC(1) or (2) to\nrevoke a decision under subsection 44PA(3) to approve a\ntender process as a competitive tender process;\nif it considers that it is appropriate and practicable to do so.\n\n(2) The notice must specify how submissions may be made and the\nday by which submissions may be made (which must be at least 14\ndays after the day the notice is published).\nConsideration of submissions\n\n(3) Subject to subsection (6), in making its decision, the Commission:\n\n(a) must have regard to any submission made on or before the\nday specified in the notice; and\n\n(b) may disregard any submission made after the day specified in\nthe notice.\nCommission may make submissions publicly available\n\n(4) The Commission may make any written submission, or a written\nrecord (which may be a summary) of any oral submission, publicly\navailable.\nConfidentiality\n\n(5) A person may, at the time of making a submission, request that the\nCommission:\n\nChapter 2  Access to services",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44pe-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44pe-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44pe-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44pe-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44pe-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "af4ea02852eb08ea7b96b093b59e744da12779a5997fd70804d7068c90a7cda0"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44pe",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44PE Commission may invite public submissions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 205,
      "values:originalText": "Invitation\n\n(1) The Commission may publish, by electronic or other means, a\nnotice inviting public submissions:\n\n(a) on an application under subsection 44PA(1); or\n\n(b) on any proposed decision under subsection 44PC(1) or (2) to\nrevoke a decision under subsection 44PA(3) to approve a\ntender process as a competitive tender process;\nif it considers that it is appropriate and practicable to do so.\n\n(2) The notice must specify how submissions may be made and the\nday by which submissions may be made (which must be at least 14\ndays after the day the notice is published).\nConsideration of submissions\n\n(3) Subject to subsection (6), in making its decision, the Commission:\n\n(a) must have regard to any submission made on or before the\nday specified in the notice; and\n\n(b) may disregard any submission made after the day specified in\nthe notice.\nCommission may make submissions publicly available\n\n(4) The Commission may make any written submission, or a written\nrecord (which may be a summary) of any oral submission, publicly\navailable.\nConfidentiality\n\n(5) A person may, at the time of making a submission, request that the\nCommission:\n\nChapter 2  Access to services"
    },
