    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44r",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44R Constitutional limits on operation of this Division",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44r"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.212",
      "values:originalText": "This Division does not apply in relation to a third party’s access to\na service unless:\n\n(a) the provider is a corporation (or a partnership or joint venture\nconsisting wholly of corporations); or\n\n(b) the third party is a corporation; or\n\n(c) the access is (or would be) in the course of, or for the\npurposes of, constitutional trade or commerce.\nSubdivision B—Notification of access disputes",
      "skos:definition": "This Division does not apply in relation to a third party’s access to\na service unless:\n\n(a) the provider is a corporation (or a partnership or joint venture\nconsisting wholly of corporations); or\n\n(b) the third party is a corporation; or\n\n(c) the access is (or would be) in the course of, or for the\npurposes of, constitutional trade or commerce.\nSubdivision B—Notification of access disputes",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44r-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44r-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "31f50704446f741dcf50fa54b85325eab3273e71a8a8f856831c88b039f8a2e9",
      "skos:note": "Restricts access to services by third parties under certain conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44r",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44R Constitutional limits on operation of this Division",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 212,
      "values:originalText": "This Division does not apply in relation to a third party’s access to\na service unless:\n\n(a) the provider is a corporation (or a partnership or joint venture\nconsisting wholly of corporations); or\n\n(b) the third party is a corporation; or\n\n(c) the access is (or would be) in the course of, or for the\npurposes of, constitutional trade or commerce.\nSubdivision B—Notification of access disputes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44r-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44r"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44r-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits access to services by third parties under certain conditions.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "None",
      "cml:conclusionText": "None"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44s",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44S Notification of access disputes",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44s"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.212",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a third party is unable to agree with the provider on one or more\naspects of access to a declared service, either the provider or the\nthird party may notify the Commission in writing that an access\ndispute exists, but only to the extent that those aspects of access are\nnot the subject of an access undertaking that is in operation in\nrelation to the service.\nNote:\nAn example of one of the things on which a provider and third party\nmight disagree is whether a previous determination ought to be varied.\n\n(2) On receiving the notification, the Commission must give notice in\nwriting of the access dispute to:\n\n(a) the provider, if the third party notified the access dispute;\n\n(b) the third party, if the provider notified the access dispute;\n\n(c) any other person whom the Commission thinks might want to\nbecome a party to the arbitration.\n\nAccess to services  Chapter 2\nAccess to services  Part IIIA\nAccess to declared services  Division 3\n\nSection 44T\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If a third party is unable to agree with the provider on one or more\naspects of access to a declared service, either the provider or the\nthird party may notify the Commission in writing that an access\ndispute exists, but only to the extent that those aspects of access are\nnot the subject of an access undertaking that is in operation in\nrelation to the service.\nNote:\nAn example of one of the things on which a provider and third party\nmight disagree is whether a previous determination ought to be varied.\n\n(2) On receiving the notification, the Commission must give notice in\nwriting of the access dispute to:\n\n(a) the provider, if the third party notified the access dispute;\n\n(b) the third party, if the provider notified the access dispute;\n\n(c) any other person whom the Commission thinks might want to\nbecome a party to the arbitration.\n\nAccess to services  Chapter 2\nAccess to services  Part IIIA\nAccess to declared services  Division 3\n\nSection 44T\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44s-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44s-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cd75bf2cba22508c4cb699ecc816e84799a44e6125ed4faffd48830d83cc0600"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44s",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44S Notification of access disputes",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 212,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a third party is unable to agree with the provider on one or more\naspects of access to a declared service, either the provider or the\nthird party may notify the Commission in writing that an access\ndispute exists, but only to the extent that those aspects of access are\nnot the subject of an access undertaking that is in operation in\nrelation to the service.\nNote:\nAn example of one of the things on which a provider and third party\nmight disagree is whether a previous determination ought to be varied.\n\n(2) On receiving the notification, the Commission must give notice in\nwriting of the access dispute to:\n\n(a) the provider, if the third party notified the access dispute;\n\n(b) the third party, if the provider notified the access dispute;\n\n(c) any other person whom the Commission thinks might want to\nbecome a party to the arbitration.\n\nAccess to services  Chapter 2\nAccess to services  Part IIIA\nAccess to declared services  Division 3\n\nSection 44T\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026"
    },
