    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44t",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44T Withdrawal of notifications",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44t"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.213",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A notification may be withdrawn as follows (and not otherwise):\n\n(a) if the provider notified the dispute:\n\n(i) the provider may withdraw the notification at any time\nbefore the Commission makes its final determination;\n\n(ii) the third party may withdraw the provider’s notification\nat any time after the Commission issues a draft final\ndetermination, but before it makes its final\ndetermination;\n\n(b) if the third party notified the dispute, the third party may\nwithdraw the notification at any time before the Commission\nmakes its final determination.\n\n(2) Despite subparagraph (1)(a)(ii), if the provider notified a dispute\nover variation of a final determination, the third party may not\nwithdraw the provider’s notification.\n\n(3) If the notification is withdrawn, it is taken for the purposes of this\nPart never to have been given.\nSubdivision C—Arbitration of access disputes",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A notification may be withdrawn as follows (and not otherwise):\n\n(a) if the provider notified the dispute:\n\n(i) the provider may withdraw the notification at any time\nbefore the Commission makes its final determination;\n\n(ii) the third party may withdraw the provider’s notification\nat any time after the Commission issues a draft final\ndetermination, but before it makes its final\ndetermination;\n\n(b) if the third party notified the dispute, the third party may\nwithdraw the notification at any time before the Commission\nmakes its final determination.\n\n(2) Despite subparagraph (1)(a)(ii), if the provider notified a dispute\nover variation of a final determination, the third party may not\nwithdraw the provider’s notification.\n\n(3) If the notification is withdrawn, it is taken for the purposes of this\nPart never to have been given.\nSubdivision C—Arbitration of access disputes",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44t-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44t-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44t-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "48be4d81811636d96a755b45c19b3218a14ded58c8910675c4caa6166827d71b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44t",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44T Withdrawal of notifications",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 213,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A notification may be withdrawn as follows (and not otherwise):\n\n(a) if the provider notified the dispute:\n\n(i) the provider may withdraw the notification at any time\nbefore the Commission makes its final determination;\n\n(ii) the third party may withdraw the provider’s notification\nat any time after the Commission issues a draft final\ndetermination, but before it makes its final\ndetermination;\n\n(b) if the third party notified the dispute, the third party may\nwithdraw the notification at any time before the Commission\nmakes its final determination.\n\n(2) Despite subparagraph (1)(a)(ii), if the provider notified a dispute\nover variation of a final determination, the third party may not\nwithdraw the provider’s notification.\n\n(3) If the notification is withdrawn, it is taken for the purposes of this\nPart never to have been given.\nSubdivision C—Arbitration of access disputes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44t-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44T(1) Withdrawal of notifications",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44t-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.213",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A notification may be withdrawn as follows (and not otherwise):\n\n(a) if the provider notified the dispute:\n\n(i) the provider may withdraw the notification at any time\nbefore the Commission makes its final determination;\n\n(ii) the third party may withdraw the provider’s notification\nat any time after the Commission issues a draft final\ndetermination, but before it makes its final\ndetermination;\n\n(b) if the third party notified the dispute, the third party may\nwithdraw the notification at any time before the Commission\nmakes its final determination.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A notification may be withdrawn as follows (and not otherwise):\n\n(a) if the provider notified the dispute:\n\n(i) the provider may withdraw the notification at any time\nbefore the Commission makes its final determination;\n\n(ii) the third party may withdraw the provider’s notification\nat any time after the Commission issues a draft final\ndetermination, but before it makes its final\ndetermination;\n\n(b) if the third party notified the dispute, the third party may\nwithdraw the notification at any time before the Commission\nmakes its final determination.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44t"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44t-ss-1-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c30cd4ca6f1cacf6f33c3607038b454895be2505e8b5cc609a9ce1844823a7d9",
      "skos:note": "Withdrawal of notifications"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44t-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44T(1) Withdrawal of notifications",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 213,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A notification may be withdrawn as follows (and not otherwise):\n\n(a) if the provider notified the dispute:\n\n(i) the provider may withdraw the notification at any time\nbefore the Commission makes its final determination;\n\n(ii) the third party may withdraw the provider’s notification\nat any time after the Commission issues a draft final\ndetermination, but before it makes its final\ndetermination;\n\n(b) if the third party notified the dispute, the third party may\nwithdraw the notification at any time before the Commission\nmakes its final determination."
    },
