      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(2) Paragraphs (1)(a) and (b) do not apply in relation to the requirements and rights of the third party and the provider when the Commission is making a determination in arbitration of an access dispute relating to an earlier determination of an access dispute between the third party and the provider."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44x",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44X Matters that the Commission must take into account",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44x"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.217",
      "values:originalText": "Final determinations\n\n(1) The Commission must take the following matters into account in\nmaking a final determination:\n\n(aa) the objects of this Part;\n\n(a) the legitimate business interests of the provider, and the\nprovider’s investment in the facility;\n\n(b) the public interest, including the public interest in having\ncompetition in markets (whether or not in Australia);\n\n(c) the interests of all persons who have rights to use the service;\n\n(d) the direct costs of providing access to the service;\n\n(e) the value to the provider of extensions (including expansions\nof capacity and expansions of geographical reach) whose cost\nis borne by someone else;\n\n(ea) the value to the provider of interconnections to the facility\nwhose cost is borne by someone else;\n\n(f) the operational and technical requirements necessary for the\nsafe and reliable operation of the facility;\n\n(g) the economically efficient operation of the facility;\n\n(h) the pricing principles specified in section 44ZZCA.\n\n(2) The Commission may take into account any other matters that it\nthinks are relevant.\nInterim determinations\n\n(3) The Commission may take the following matters into account in\nmaking an interim determination:\n\n(a) a matter referred to in subsection (1);\n\n(b) any other matter it considers relevant.\n\n(4) In making an interim determination, the Commission does not have\na duty to consider whether to take into account a matter referred to\nin subsection (1).\n\nChapter 2  Access to services",
      "skos:definition": "Final determinations\n\n(1) The Commission must take the following matters into account in\nmaking a final determination:\n\n(aa) the objects of this Part;\n\n(a) the legitimate business interests of the provider, and the\nprovider’s investment in the facility;\n\n(b) the public interest, including the public interest in having\ncompetition in markets (whether or not in Australia);\n\n(c) the interests of all persons who have rights to use the service;\n\n(d) the direct costs of providing access to the service;\n\n(e) the value to the provider of extensions (including expansions\nof capacity and expansions of geographical reach) whose cost\nis borne by someone else;\n\n(ea) the value to the provider of interconnections to the facility\nwhose cost is borne by someone else;\n\n(f) the operational and technical requirements necessary for the\nsafe and reliable operation of the facility;\n\n(g) the economically efficient operation of the facility;\n\n(h) the pricing principles specified in section 44ZZCA.\n\n(2) The Commission may take into account any other matters that it\nthinks are relevant.\nInterim determinations\n\n(3) The Commission may take the following matters into account in\nmaking an interim determination:\n\n(a) a matter referred to in subsection (1);\n\n(b) any other matter it considers relevant.\n\n(4) In making an interim determination, the Commission does not have\na duty to consider whether to take into account a matter referred to\nin subsection (1).\n\nChapter 2  Access to services",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44x-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44x-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44x-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44x-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0415c390de75128f0fa7b46212aef75ea24019cd33e832dd7c7ec2c8ab2dae75"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44x",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44X Matters that the Commission must take into account",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 217,
      "values:originalText": "Final determinations\n\n(1) The Commission must take the following matters into account in\nmaking a final determination:\n\n(aa) the objects of this Part;\n\n(a) the legitimate business interests of the provider, and the\nprovider’s investment in the facility;\n\n(b) the public interest, including the public interest in having\ncompetition in markets (whether or not in Australia);\n\n(c) the interests of all persons who have rights to use the service;\n\n(d) the direct costs of providing access to the service;\n\n(e) the value to the provider of extensions (including expansions\nof capacity and expansions of geographical reach) whose cost\nis borne by someone else;\n\n(ea) the value to the provider of interconnections to the facility\nwhose cost is borne by someone else;\n\n(f) the operational and technical requirements necessary for the\nsafe and reliable operation of the facility;\n\n(g) the economically efficient operation of the facility;\n\n(h) the pricing principles specified in section 44ZZCA.\n\n(2) The Commission may take into account any other matters that it\nthinks are relevant.\nInterim determinations\n\n(3) The Commission may take the following matters into account in\nmaking an interim determination:\n\n(a) a matter referred to in subsection (1);\n\n(b) any other matter it considers relevant.\n\n(4) In making an interim determination, the Commission does not have\na duty to consider whether to take into account a matter referred to\nin subsection (1).\n\nChapter 2  Access to services"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44x-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44X(1) Matters that the Commission must take into account",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
