      "cml:premiseText": "(3) The Commission may take the following matters into account..."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44x-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44X(4) Matters that the Commission must take into account",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44x-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.217",
      "values:originalText": "(4) In making an interim determination, the Commission does not have\na duty to consider whether to take into account a matter referred to\nin subsection (1).\n\nChapter 2  Access to services",
      "skos:definition": "(4) In making an interim determination, the Commission does not have\na duty to consider whether to take into account a matter referred to\nin subsection (1).\n\nChapter 2  Access to services",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44x"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44x-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44x-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44x-ss-4-logic-linearlogic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44x-ss-4-logic-deontic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44x-ss-4-logic-linearlogic-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c26e5c71c5e606613c92ce0237a83b2c7b0a57c2f62adb8246576753a8776ba8",
      "skos:note": "Duty to consider matter in making interim determination"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44x-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44X(4) Matters that the Commission must take into account",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 217,
      "values:originalText": "(4) In making an interim determination, the Commission does not have\na duty to consider whether to take into account a matter referred to\nin subsection (1).\n\nChapter 2  Access to services"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44x-ss-4-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44x-ss-4"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44x-ss-4-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Must consider matter",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(4) In making an interim determination, the Commission does not have a duty to consider whether to take into account a matter referred to in subsection (1).",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The Commission MUST consider the matter."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44x-ss-4-logic-linearlogic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LinearLogic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "⇒",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Duty to consider matter implies consideration of matter",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::linear",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(4) In making an interim determination, the Commission does not have a duty to consider whether to take into account a matter referred to in subsection (1).",
      "cml:conclusionText": "If the Commission has a duty to consider the matter, then the Commission MUST consider the matter."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44x-ss-4-logic-deontic-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST NOT",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Must not consider matter in making interim determination",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(4) In making an interim determination, the Commission does not have a duty to consider whether to take into account a matter referred to in subsection (1).",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The Commission MUST NOT consider the matter."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44x-ss-4-logic-linearlogic-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LinearLogic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "⇒",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Not considering matter implies duty not to consider matter",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::linear",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(4) In making an interim determination, the Commission does not have a duty to consider whether to take into account a matter referred to in subsection (1).",
      "cml:conclusionText": "If the Commission does NOT consider the matter, then the Commission MUST NOT consider the matter."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44xa",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44XA Time limit for Commission’s final determination",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44xa"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.218",
      "values:originalText": "Commission to make final determination within 180 days\n\n(1) The Commission must make a final determination within the\nperiod of 180 days (the expected period) starting at the start of the\nday the application is received.\nStopping the clock\n\n(2) In working out the expected period in relation to a final\ndetermination, in a situation referred to in column 1 of an item of\nthe following table, disregard any day in a period:\n\n(a) starting on the day referred to in column 2 of the item; and\n\n(b) ending on the day referred to in column 3 of the item.\n\nStopping the clock\nItem\nColumn 1\nSituation\nColumn 2\nStart day\nColumn 3\nEnd day\nAn agreement is made in\nrelation to the arbitration\nunder subsection (4)\nThe first day of\nthe period\nspecified in the\nagreement\nThe last day of the period\nspecified in the agreement\nA direction is given\nunder\nsubsection 44ZG(1) to\ngive information or make\na submission within a\nspecified period\nThe first day of\nthe period\nspecified for the\ngiving of the\ninformation or\nthe making of\nthe submission\nThe last day of the period\nspecified for the giving of\nthe information or the\nmaking of the submission\nA decision is published\nunder\nsubsection 44ZZCB(4)\ndeferring consideration\nof the dispute while the\nCommission considers\nan access undertaking\nThe day on\nwhich the\ndecision is\npublished\nThe day on which the\nCommission makes its\ndecision on the access\nundertaking under\nsubsection 44ZZA(3)\n\nAccess to services  Chapter 2\nAccess to services  Part IIIA\nAccess to declared services  Division 3\n\nSection 44Y\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nStopping the clock\nItem\nColumn 1\nSituation\nColumn 2\nStart day\nColumn 3\nEnd day\nThe Commission, under\nsubsection 44ZZCBA(1)\nor (2), defers arbitrating\nthe dispute while a\ndeclaration is under\nreview by the Tribunal\nThe day on\nwhich the\nCommission\ngives the notice\nto defer\narbitrating the\ndispute\nThe day the Tribunal makes\nits decision under\nsection 44K on the review\n\n(3) Despite subsection (2), do not disregard any day more than once.\nStopping the clock by agreement\n\n(4) The Commission and the parties to the access dispute may agree in\nwriting that a specified period is to be disregarded in working out\nthe expected period.\n\n(5) The Commission must publish, by electronic or other means, the\nagreement.\nDeemed final determination\n\n(6) If the Commission does not publish under section 44ZNB a written\nreport about a final determination within the expected period, it is\ntaken, immediately after the end of the expected period, to have:\n\n(a) made a final determination that does not impose any\nobligations on the parties or alter any obligations (if any) that\nexist at that time between the parties; and\n\n(b) published a written report about the final determination under\nsection 44ZNB.",
      "skos:definition": "Commission to make final determination within 180 days\n\n(1) The Commission must make a final determination within the\nperiod of 180 days (the expected period) starting at the start of the\nday the application is received.\nStopping the clock\n\n(2) In working out the expected period in relation to a final\ndetermination, in a situation referred to in column 1 of an item of\nthe following table, disregard any day in a period:\n\n(a) starting on the day referred to in column 2 of the item; and\n\n(b) ending on the day referred to in column 3 of the item.\n\nStopping the clock\nItem\nColumn 1\nSituation\nColumn 2\nStart day\nColumn 3\nEnd day\nAn agreement is made in\nrelation to the arbitration\nunder subsection (4)\nThe first day of\nthe period\nspecified in the\nagreement\nThe last day of the period\nspecified in the agreement\nA direction is given\nunder\nsubsection 44ZG(1) to\ngive information or make\na submission within a\nspecified period\nThe first day of\nthe period\nspecified for the\ngiving of the\ninformation or\nthe making of\nthe submission\nThe last day of the period\nspecified for the giving of\nthe information or the\nmaking of the submission\nA decision is published\nunder\nsubsection 44ZZCB(4)\ndeferring consideration\nof the dispute while the\nCommission considers\nan access undertaking\nThe day on\nwhich the\ndecision is\npublished\nThe day on which the\nCommission makes its\ndecision on the access\nundertaking under\nsubsection 44ZZA(3)\n\nAccess to services  Chapter 2\nAccess to services  Part IIIA\nAccess to declared services  Division 3\n\nSection 44Y\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nStopping the clock\nItem\nColumn 1\nSituation\nColumn 2\nStart day\nColumn 3\nEnd day\nThe Commission, under\nsubsection 44ZZCBA(1)\nor (2), defers arbitrating\nthe dispute while a\ndeclaration is under\nreview by the Tribunal\nThe day on\nwhich the\nCommission\ngives the notice\nto defer\narbitrating the\ndispute\nThe day the Tribunal makes\nits decision under\nsection 44K on the review\n\n(3) Despite subsection (2), do ",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44xa-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44xa-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44xa-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44xa-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44xa-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44xa-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8d790747318ec85a84d89e1ce78ee9516d963b1864fea6472b1146dda14a804d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44xa",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44XA Time limit for Commission’s final determination",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 218,
      "values:originalText": "Commission to make final determination within 180 days\n\n(1) The Commission must make a final determination within the\nperiod of 180 days (the expected period) starting at the start of the\nday the application is received.\nStopping the clock\n\n(2) In working out the expected period in relation to a final\ndetermination, in a situation referred to in column 1 of an item of\nthe following table, disregard any day in a period:\n\n(a) starting on the day referred to in column 2 of the item; and\n\n(b) ending on the day referred to in column 3 of the item.\n\nStopping the clock\nItem\nColumn 1\nSituation\nColumn 2\nStart day\nColumn 3\nEnd day\nAn agreement is made in\nrelation to the arbitration\nunder subsection (4)\nThe first day of\nthe period\nspecified in the\nagreement\nThe last day of the period\nspecified in the agreement\nA direction is given\nunder\nsubsection 44ZG(1) to\ngive information or make\na submission within a\nspecified period\nThe first day of\nthe period\nspecified for the\ngiving of the\ninformation or\nthe making of\nthe submission\nThe last day of the period\nspecified for the giving of\nthe information or the\nmaking of the submission\nA decision is published\nunder\nsubsection 44ZZCB(4)\ndeferring consideration\nof the dispute while the\nCommission considers\nan access undertaking\nThe day on\nwhich the\ndecision is\npublished\nThe day on which the\nCommission makes its\ndecision on the access\nundertaking under\nsubsection 44ZZA(3)\n\nAccess to services  Chapter 2\nAccess to services  Part IIIA\nAccess to declared services  Division 3\n\nSection 44Y\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nStopping the clock\nItem\nColumn 1\nSituation\nColumn 2\nStart day\nColumn 3\nEnd day\nThe Commission, under\nsubsection 44ZZCBA(1)\nor (2), defers arbitrating\nthe dispute while a\ndeclaration is under\nreview by the Tribunal\nThe day on\nwhich the\nCommission\ngives the notice\nto defer\narbitrating the\ndispute\nThe day the Tribunal makes\nits decision under\nsection 44K on the review\n\n(3) Despite subsection (2), do not disregard any day more than once.\nStopping the clock by agreement\n\n(4) The Commission and the parties to the access dispute may agree in\nwriting that a specified period is to be disregarded in working out\nthe expected period.\n\n(5) The Commission must publish, by electronic or other means, the\nagreement.\nDeemed final determination\n\n(6) If the Commission does not publish under section 44ZNB a written\nreport about a final determination within the expected period, it is\ntaken, immediately after the end of the expected period, to have:\n\n(a) made a final determination that does not impose any\nobligations on the parties or alter any obligations (if any) that\nexist at that time between the parties; and\n\n(b) published a written report about the final determination under\nsection 44ZNB."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44xa-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44XA(1) Time limit for Commission’s final determination",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44xa-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
