      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.219",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commission may at any time terminate an arbitration (without\nmaking a final determination) if it thinks that:\n\n(a) the notification of the dispute was vexatious; or\n\nChapter 2  Access to services",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Commission may at any time terminate an arbitration (without\nmaking a final determination) if it thinks that:\n\n(a) the notification of the dispute was vexatious; or\n\nChapter 2  Access to services",
