      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zf",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44ZF Procedure of Commission",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44zf"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.222",
      "values:originalText": "(1) In an arbitration hearing about an access dispute, the Commission:\n\n(a) is not bound by technicalities, legal forms or rules of\nevidence; and\n\n(b) must act as speedily as a proper consideration of the dispute\nallows, having regard to the need to carefully and quickly\ninquire into and investigate the dispute and all matters\naffecting the merits, and fair settlement, of the dispute; and\n\n(c) may inform itself of any matter relevant to the dispute in any\nway it thinks appropriate.\n\n(2) The Commission may determine the periods that are reasonably\nnecessary for the fair and adequate presentation of the respective\ncases of the parties to an access dispute, and may require that the\ncases be presented within those periods.\n\n(3) The Commission may require evidence or argument to be\npresented in writing, and may decide the matters on which it will\nhear oral evidence or argument.\n\nAccess to services  Chapter 2\nAccess to services  Part IIIA\nAccess to declared services  Division 3\n\nSection 44ZG\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(1) In an arbitration hearing about an access dispute, the Commission:\n\n(a) is not bound by technicalities, legal forms or rules of\nevidence; and\n\n(b) must act as speedily as a proper consideration of the dispute\nallows, having regard to the need to carefully and quickly\ninquire into and investigate the dispute and all matters\naffecting the merits, and fair settlement, of the dispute; and\n\n(c) may inform itself of any matter relevant to the dispute in any\nway it thinks appropriate.\n\n(2) The Commission may determine the periods that are reasonably\nnecessary for the fair and adequate presentation of the respective\ncases of the parties to an access dispute, and may require that the\ncases be presented within those periods.\n\n(3) The Commission may require evidence or argument to be\npresented in writing, and may decide the matters on which it will\nhear oral evidence or argument.\n\nAccess to services  Chapter 2\nAccess to services  Part IIIA\nAccess to declared services  Division 3\n\nSection 44ZG\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zf-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zf-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zf-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "29379897601443f309e6e97910b0c34887d2e884ed97e3df7ddc97aebff8c46b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44zf",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44ZF Procedure of Commission",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 222,
      "values:originalText": "(1) In an arbitration hearing about an access dispute, the Commission:\n\n(a) is not bound by technicalities, legal forms or rules of\nevidence; and\n\n(b) must act as speedily as a proper consideration of the dispute\nallows, having regard to the need to carefully and quickly\ninquire into and investigate the dispute and all matters\naffecting the merits, and fair settlement, of the dispute; and\n\n(c) may inform itself of any matter relevant to the dispute in any\nway it thinks appropriate.\n\n(2) The Commission may determine the periods that are reasonably\nnecessary for the fair and adequate presentation of the respective\ncases of the parties to an access dispute, and may require that the\ncases be presented within those periods.\n\n(3) The Commission may require evidence or argument to be\npresented in writing, and may decide the matters on which it will\nhear oral evidence or argument.\n\nAccess to services  Chapter 2\nAccess to services  Part IIIA\nAccess to declared services  Division 3\n\nSection 44ZG\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026"
    },
