    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zi",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44ZI Failing to attend as a witness",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44zi"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.224",
      "values:originalText": "A person who is served, as prescribed, with a summons to appear\nas a witness before the Commission must not, without reasonable\nexcuse:\n\n(a) fail to attend as required by the summons; or\n\n(b) fail to appear and report himself or herself from day to day\nunless excused, or released from further attendance, by a\nmember of the Commission.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 6 months.\n44ZJ  Failing to answer questions etc.\n\n(1) A person appearing as a witness before the Commission must not,\nwithout reasonable excuse:\n\n(a) refuse or fail to be sworn or to make an affirmation; or\n\n(b) refuse or fail to answer a question that the person is required\nto answer by the Commission; or\n\n(c) refuse or fail to produce a document that he or she was\nrequired to produce by a summons under this Part served on\nhim or her as prescribed.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 6 months.\n\n(2) It is a reasonable excuse for the purposes of subsection (1) for an\nindividual to refuse or fail to answer a question or produce a\ndocument on the ground that the answer or the production of the\ndocument might tend to incriminate the individual or to expose the\nindividual to a penalty. This subsection does not limit what is a\nreasonable excuse for the purposes of subsection (1).\n\nAccess to services  Chapter 2\nAccess to services  Part IIIA\nAccess to declared services  Division 3\n\nSection 44ZK\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "skos:definition": "A person who is served, as prescribed, with a summons to appear\nas a witness before the Commission must not, without reasonable\nexcuse:\n\n(a) fail to attend as required by the summons; or\n\n(b) fail to appear and report himself or herself from day to day\nunless excused, or released from further attendance, by a\nmember of the Commission.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 6 months.\n44ZJ  Failing to answer questions etc.\n\n(1) A person appearing as a witness before the Commission must not,\nwithout reasonable excuse:\n\n(a) refuse or fail to be sworn or to make an affirmation; or\n\n(b) refuse or fail to answer a question that the person is required\nto answer by the Commission; or\n\n(c) refuse or fail to produce a document that he or she was\nrequired to produce by a summons under this Part served on\nhim or her as prescribed.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 6 months.\n\n(2) It is a reasonable excuse for the purposes of subsection (1) for an\nindividual to refuse or fail to answer a question or produce a\ndocument on the ground that the answer or the production of the\ndocument might tend to incriminate the individual or to expose the\nindividual to a penalty. This subsection does not limit what is a\nreasonable excuse for the purposes of subsection (1).\n\nAccess to services  Chapter 2\nAccess to services  Part IIIA\nAccess to declared services  Division 3\n\nSection 44ZK\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zi-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zi-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b2a2466c6982c4164ec946b815c312c8b5d7b6190392f8b9c6470a33f740f907"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44zi",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44ZI Failing to attend as a witness",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 224,
      "values:originalText": "A person who is served, as prescribed, with a summons to appear\nas a witness before the Commission must not, without reasonable\nexcuse:\n\n(a) fail to attend as required by the summons; or\n\n(b) fail to appear and report himself or herself from day to day\nunless excused, or released from further attendance, by a\nmember of the Commission.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 6 months.\n44ZJ  Failing to answer questions etc.\n\n(1) A person appearing as a witness before the Commission must not,\nwithout reasonable excuse:\n\n(a) refuse or fail to be sworn or to make an affirmation; or\n\n(b) refuse or fail to answer a question that the person is required\nto answer by the Commission; or\n\n(c) refuse or fail to produce a document that he or she was\nrequired to produce by a summons under this Part served on\nhim or her as prescribed.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 6 months.\n\n(2) It is a reasonable excuse for the purposes of subsection (1) for an\nindividual to refuse or fail to answer a question or produce a\ndocument on the ground that the answer or the production of the\ndocument might tend to incriminate the individual or to expose the\nindividual to a penalty. This subsection does not limit what is a\nreasonable excuse for the purposes of subsection (1).\n\nAccess to services  Chapter 2\nAccess to services  Part IIIA\nAccess to declared services  Division 3\n\nSection 44ZK\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zi-ss-1",
