          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zn-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zn-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5eb9d5a75617afdc1c2c87ae70287283bccdac019a833b6b1eaaf4df8f2b3954",
      "skos:note": "Chairperson must give notice to parties before doing something",
      "dc:description": "written submission within 14 days"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44zn-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44ZN(3) Parties to pay costs of an arbitration",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 226,
      "values:originalText": "(3) Before doing so, the Chairperson must give each party to the\narbitration of each nominated dispute a notice in writing:\n\n(a) specifying what the Chairperson is proposing to do; and\n\n(b) inviting the party to make a written submission on the\nproposal to the Chairperson within 14 days after the notice is\ngiven."
    },
