    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zr",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44ZR Appeals to Federal Court from determinations of the",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44zr"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.233",
      "values:originalText": "Tribunal\n\n(1) A party to an arbitration may appeal to the Federal Court, on a\nquestion of law, from the decision of the Tribunal under\nsection 44ZP.\n\n(2) An appeal by a person under subsection (1) must be instituted:\n\n(a) not later than the 28th day after the day on which the decision\nof the Tribunal is made or within such further period as the\nFederal Court (whether before or after the end of that day)\nallows; and\n\n(b) in accordance with the Rules of Court made under the\nFederal Court of Australia Act 1976.\n\n(3) The Federal Court must hear and determine the appeal and may\nmake any order that it thinks appropriate.\n\n(4) The orders that may be made by the Federal Court on appeal\ninclude (but are not limited to):\n\n(a) an order affirming or setting aside the decision of the\nTribunal; and\n\nChapter 2  Access to services",
      "skos:definition": "Tribunal\n\n(1) A party to an arbitration may appeal to the Federal Court, on a\nquestion of law, from the decision of the Tribunal under\nsection 44ZP.\n\n(2) An appeal by a person under subsection (1) must be instituted:\n\n(a) not later than the 28th day after the day on which the decision\nof the Tribunal is made or within such further period as the\nFederal Court (whether before or after the end of that day)\nallows; and\n\n(b) in accordance with the Rules of Court made under the\nFederal Court of Australia Act 1976.\n\n(3) The Federal Court must hear and determine the appeal and may\nmake any order that it thinks appropriate.\n\n(4) The orders that may be made by the Federal Court on appeal\ninclude (but are not limited to):\n\n(a) an order affirming or setting aside the decision of the\nTribunal; and\n\nChapter 2  Access to services",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zr-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zr-ss-2"
        },
