    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zt",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44ZT Transmission of documents",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44zt"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.234",
      "values:originalText": "If an appeal is instituted in the Federal Court:\n\nAccess to services  Chapter 2\nAccess to services  Part IIIA\nAccess to declared services  Division 3\n\nSection 44ZU\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(a) the Tribunal must send to the Federal Court all documents\nthat were before the Tribunal in connection with the matter to\nwhich the appeal relates; and\n\n(b) at the conclusion of the proceedings before the Federal Court\nin relation to the appeal, the Federal Court must return the\ndocuments to the Tribunal.\nSubdivision G—Variation and revocation of determinations",
      "skos:definition": "If an appeal is instituted in the Federal Court:\n\nAccess to services  Chapter 2\nAccess to services  Part IIIA\nAccess to declared services  Division 3\n\nSection 44ZU\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(a) the Tribunal must send to the Federal Court all documents\nthat were before the Tribunal in connection with the matter to\nwhich the appeal relates; and\n\n(b) at the conclusion of the proceedings before the Federal Court\nin relation to the appeal, the Federal Court must return the\ndocuments to the Tribunal.\nSubdivision G—Variation and revocation of determinations",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zt-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9157ef8890d17671e944bd074a05bf9559a9096c4d96738009e56941983ebfe7",
      "skos:note": "Transmission of documents in Federal Court proceedings"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44zt",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44ZT Transmission of documents",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 234,
      "values:originalText": "If an appeal is instituted in the Federal Court:\n\nAccess to services  Chapter 2\nAccess to services  Part IIIA\nAccess to declared services  Division 3\n\nSection 44ZU\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(a) the Tribunal must send to the Federal Court all documents\nthat were before the Tribunal in connection with the matter to\nwhich the appeal relates; and\n\n(b) at the conclusion of the proceedings before the Federal Court\nin relation to the appeal, the Federal Court must return the\ndocuments to the Tribunal.\nSubdivision G—Variation and revocation of determinations"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zt-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zt"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zu",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44ZU Variation of final determinations",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44zu"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.235",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commission may vary a final determination on the application\nof any party to the determination. However, it cannot vary the final\ndetermination if any other party objects.\nNote:\nIf the parties cannot agree on a variation, a new access dispute can be\nnotified under section 44S.\n\n(2) Sections 44W and 44X apply to a variation under this section as if:\n\n(a) an access dispute arising out of the final determination had\nbeen notified when the application was made to the\nCommission for the variation of the determination; and\n\n(b) the variation were the making of a final determination in the\nterms of the varied determination.\n44ZUA  Variation and revocation of interim determinations\n\n(1) The Commission may, by writing, vary or revoke an interim\ndetermination.\n\n(2) The Commission must, by writing, revoke an interim determination\nif requested to do so by the parties to the determination.\n\nChapter 2  Access to services",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Commission may vary a final determination on the application\nof any party to the determination. However, it cannot vary the final\ndetermination if any other party objects.\nNote:\nIf the parties cannot agree on a variation, a new access dispute can be\nnotified under section 44S.\n\n(2) Sections 44W and 44X apply to a variation under this section as if:\n\n(a) an access dispute arising out of the final determination had\nbeen notified when the application was made to the\nCommission for the variation of the determination; and\n\n(b) the variation were the making of a final determination in the\nterms of the varied determination.\n44ZUA  Variation and revocation of interim determinations\n\n(1) The Commission may, by writing, vary or revoke an interim\ndetermination.\n\n(2) The Commission must, by writing, revoke an interim determination\nif requested to do so by the parties to the determination.\n\nChapter 2  Access to services",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zu-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zu-ss-2"
        },
