    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zv",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44ZV Constitutional limits on operation of this Division",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44zv"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.236",
      "values:originalText": "This Division does not apply to a contract unless:\n\n(a) the contract provides for access to a declared service; and\n\n(b) the contract was made after the service was declared; and\n\n(c) the parties to the contract are the provider of the service and a\nthird party; and\n\n(d) at least one of the following conditions is met:\n\n(i) the provider is a corporation (or a partnership or joint\nventure consisting wholly of corporations);\n\n(ii) the third party is a corporation;\n\n(iii) the access is (or would be) in the course of, or for the\npurposes of, constitutional trade or commerce.",
      "skos:definition": "This Division does not apply to a contract unless:\n\n(a) the contract provides for access to a declared service; and\n\n(b) the contract was made after the service was declared; and\n\n(c) the parties to the contract are the provider of the service and a\nthird party; and\n\n(d) at least one of the following conditions is met:\n\n(i) the provider is a corporation (or a partnership or joint\nventure consisting wholly of corporations);\n\n(ii) the third party is a corporation;\n\n(iii) the access is (or would be) in the course of, or for the\npurposes of, constitutional trade or commerce.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zv-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zv-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b3d9acc6241a3752bacc1bccd21f5f9d9490934ea7a7706f3a7f82648e5fafe8",
      "skos:note": "Contract exemption based on declaration of service and conditions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44zv",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44ZV Constitutional limits on operation of this Division",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 236,
      "values:originalText": "This Division does not apply to a contract unless:\n\n(a) the contract provides for access to a declared service; and\n\n(b) the contract was made after the service was declared; and\n\n(c) the parties to the contract are the provider of the service and a\nthird party; and\n\n(d) at least one of the following conditions is met:\n\n(i) the provider is a corporation (or a partnership or joint\nventure consisting wholly of corporations);\n\n(ii) the third party is a corporation;\n\n(iii) the access is (or would be) in the course of, or for the\npurposes of, constitutional trade or commerce."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zv-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zv"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zv-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "and",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Multiple conditions for exemption",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zw",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44ZW Registration of contract",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44zw"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.236",
      "values:originalText": "(1) On application by all the parties to a contract, the Commission\nmust:\n\n(a) register the contract by entering the following details on a\npublic register:\n\n(i) the names of the parties to the contract;\n\n(ii) the service to which the contract relates;\n\n(iii) the date on which the contract was made; or\n\n(b) decide not to register the contract.\n\n(2) In deciding whether to register a contract, the Commission must\ntake into account:\n\n(aa) the objects of this Part; and\n\n(a) the public interest, including the public interest in having\ncompetition in markets (whether or not in Australia); and\n\n(b) the interests of all persons who have rights to use the service\nto which the contract relates.\n\nAccess to services  Chapter 2\nAccess to services  Part IIIA\nRegistered contracts for access to declared services  Division 4\n\nSection 44ZX\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(2A) The Commission must not register a contract if it deals with a\nmatter or matters relating to access to the service that are dealt with\nin an access undertaking that is in operation.\n\n(3) The Commission must publish a decision not to register a contract.\n\n(4) If the Commission publishes a decision not to register a contract, it\nmust give the parties to the contract reasons for the decision when\nit publishes the decision.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) On application by all the parties to a contract, the Commission\nmust:\n\n(a) register the contract by entering the following details on a\npublic register:\n\n(i) the names of the parties to the contract;\n\n(ii) the service to which the contract relates;\n\n(iii) the date on which the contract was made; or\n\n(b) decide not to register the contract.\n\n(2) In deciding whether to register a contract, the Commission must\ntake into account:\n\n(aa) the objects of this Part; and\n\n(a) the public interest, including the public interest in having\ncompetition in markets (whether or not in Australia); and\n\n(b) the interests of all persons who have rights to use the service\nto which the contract relates.\n\nAccess to services  Chapter 2\nAccess to services  Part IIIA\nRegistered contracts for access to declared services  Division 4\n\nSection 44ZX\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(2A) The Commission must not register a contract if it deals with a\nmatter or matters relating to access to the service that are dealt with\nin an access undertaking that is in operation.\n\n(3) The Commission must publish a decision not to register a contract.\n\n(4) If the Commission publishes a decision not to register a contract, it\nmust give the parties to the contract reasons for the decision when\nit publishes the decision.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zw-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zw-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zw-ss-2a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zw-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zw-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "66a6d6a80affb7fec2f3d684544e3b1e1269e336007af51ff7418d0c42b842c7"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44zw",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44ZW Registration of contract",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 236,
      "values:originalText": "(1) On application by all the parties to a contract, the Commission\nmust:\n\n(a) register the contract by entering the following details on a\npublic register:\n\n(i) the names of the parties to the contract;\n\n(ii) the service to which the contract relates;\n\n(iii) the date on which the contract was made; or\n\n(b) decide not to register the contract.\n\n(2) In deciding whether to register a contract, the Commission must\ntake into account:\n\n(aa) the objects of this Part; and\n\n(a) the public interest, including the public interest in having\ncompetition in markets (whether or not in Australia); and\n\n(b) the interests of all persons who have rights to use the service\nto which the contract relates.\n\nAccess to services  Chapter 2\nAccess to services  Part IIIA\nRegistered contracts for access to declared services  Division 4\n\nSection 44ZX\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(2A) The Commission must not register a contract if it deals with a\nmatter or matters relating to access to the service that are dealt with\nin an access undertaking that is in operation.\n\n(3) The Commission must publish a decision not to register a contract.\n\n(4) If the Commission publishes a decision not to register a contract, it\nmust give the parties to the contract reasons for the decision when\nit publishes the decision."
    },
