    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zx",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44ZX Review of decision not to register contract",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44zx"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.237",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the Commission decides not to register a contract, a party to the\ncontract may apply in writing to the Tribunal for review of the\ndecision.\n\n(2) An application for review must be made within 21 days after\npublication of the Commission’s decision.\n\n(3) The review by the Tribunal is a re-consideration of the matter\nbased on the information, reports and things referred to in\nsection 44ZZOAA.\nNote:\nThere are limits on the information to which the Tribunal may have\nregard (see section 44ZZOAA) and time limits that apply to the\nTribunal’s decision on the review (see section 44ZZOA).\n\n(4) For the purposes of the review, the Tribunal has the same powers\nas the Commission.\n\n(5) The member of the Tribunal presiding at the review may require\nthe Commission to give assistance for the purposes of the review.\n\n(5A) Without limiting subsection (5), the member may, by written\nnotice, require the Commission to give information, and to make\nreports, of a kind specified in the notice, within the period\nspecified in the notice, for the purposes of the review.\n\n(5B) The Tribunal must:\n\n(a) give a copy of the notice to:\n\n(i) the person who applied for review; and\n\nChapter 2  Access to services",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If the Commission decides not to register a contract, a party to the\ncontract may apply in writing to the Tribunal for review of the\ndecision.\n\n(2) An application for review must be made within 21 days after\npublication of the Commission’s decision.\n\n(3) The review by the Tribunal is a re-consideration of the matter\nbased on the information, reports and things referred to in\nsection 44ZZOAA.\nNote:\nThere are limits on the information to which the Tribunal may have\nregard (see section 44ZZOAA) and time limits that apply to the\nTribunal’s decision on the review (see section 44ZZOA).\n\n(4) For the purposes of the review, the Tribunal has the same powers\nas the Commission.\n\n(5) The member of the Tribunal presiding at the review may require\nthe Commission to give assistance for the purposes of the review.\n\n(5A) Without limiting subsection (5), the member may, by written\nnotice, require the Commission to give information, and to make\nreports, of a kind specified in the notice, within the period\nspecified in the notice, for the purposes of the review.\n\n(5B) The Tribunal must:\n\n(a) give a copy of the notice to:\n\n(i) the person who applied for review; and\n\nChapter 2  Access to services",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zx-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zx-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zx-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zx-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zx-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zx-ss-5a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zx-ss-5b"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "fe27e8c2bca2ab35e58d7d55f43b039c664d99ce0416372b1dc7781a3cb0e279"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44zx",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44ZX Review of decision not to register contract",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 237,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the Commission decides not to register a contract, a party to the\ncontract may apply in writing to the Tribunal for review of the\ndecision.\n\n(2) An application for review must be made within 21 days after\npublication of the Commission’s decision.\n\n(3) The review by the Tribunal is a re-consideration of the matter\nbased on the information, reports and things referred to in\nsection 44ZZOAA.\nNote:\nThere are limits on the information to which the Tribunal may have\nregard (see section 44ZZOAA) and time limits that apply to the\nTribunal’s decision on the review (see section 44ZZOA).\n\n(4) For the purposes of the review, the Tribunal has the same powers\nas the Commission.\n\n(5) The member of the Tribunal presiding at the review may require\nthe Commission to give assistance for the purposes of the review.\n\n(5A) Without limiting subsection (5), the member may, by written\nnotice, require the Commission to give information, and to make\nreports, of a kind specified in the notice, within the period\nspecified in the notice, for the purposes of the review.\n\n(5B) The Tribunal must:\n\n(a) give a copy of the notice to:\n\n(i) the person who applied for review; and\n\nChapter 2  Access to services"
    },
