    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zy",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44ZY Effect of registration of contract",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44zy"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.238",
      "values:originalText": "The parties to a contract that has been registered:\n\n(a) may enforce the contract under Division 7 as if the contract\nwere a determination of the Commission under section 44V\nand they were parties to the determination; and\n\n(b) cannot enforce the contract by any other means.\n\nAccess to services  Chapter 2\nAccess to services  Part IIIA\nHindering access to declared services  Division 5\n\nSection 44ZZ\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "skos:definition": "The parties to a contract that has been registered:\n\n(a) may enforce the contract under Division 7 as if the contract\nwere a determination of the Commission under section 44V\nand they were parties to the determination; and\n\n(b) cannot enforce the contract by any other means.\n\nAccess to services  Chapter 2\nAccess to services  Part IIIA\nHindering access to declared services  Division 5\n\nSection 44ZZ\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zy-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zy-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zy-logic-deontic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "55f61543a3cdb6f8bb5d8f7219c0e87df471ca28cb1eb5f1ebef3e5d2d1079a9",
      "skos:note": "Parties to a registered contract can enforce it under Division 7 as if it were a determination of the Commission."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44zy",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44ZY Effect of registration of contract",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 238,
      "values:originalText": "The parties to a contract that has been registered:\n\n(a) may enforce the contract under Division 7 as if the contract\nwere a determination of the Commission under section 44V\nand they were parties to the determination; and\n\n(b) cannot enforce the contract by any other means.\n\nAccess to services  Chapter 2\nAccess to services  Part IIIA\nHindering access to declared services  Division 5\n\nSection 44ZZ\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zy-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zy"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zy-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "can",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Enforcement obligation",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Parties to a registered contract can enforce it.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Under Division 7 as if it were a determination of the Commission."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zy-logic-deontic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "cannot",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibition on other means of enforcement",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Parties to a registered contract cannot enforce it by any other means."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zz",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44ZZ Prohibition on hindering access to declared services",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-44zz"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.239",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The provider or a user of a service to which a third party has access\nunder a determination, or a body corporate related to the provider\nor a user of the service, must not engage in conduct for the purpose\nof preventing or hindering the third party’s access to the service\nunder the determination.\n\n(2) A person may be taken to have engaged in conduct for the purpose\nreferred to in subsection (1) even though, after all the evidence has\nbeen considered, the existence of that purpose is ascertainable only\nby inference from the conduct of the person or from other relevant\ncircumstances. This subsection does not limit the manner in which\nthe purpose of a person may be established for the purposes of\nsubsection (1).\n\n(3) In this section, a user of a service includes a person who has a right\nto use the service.\n\nChapter 2  Access to services",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The provider or a user of a service to which a third party has access\nunder a determination, or a body corporate related to the provider\nor a user of the service, must not engage in conduct for the purpose\nof preventing or hindering the third party’s access to the service\nunder the determination.\n\n(2) A person may be taken to have engaged in conduct for the purpose\nreferred to in subsection (1) even though, after all the evidence has\nbeen considered, the existence of that purpose is ascertainable only\nby inference from the conduct of the person or from other relevant\ncircumstances. This subsection does not limit the manner in which\nthe purpose of a person may be established for the purposes of\nsubsection (1).\n\n(3) In this section, a user of a service includes a person who has a right\nto use the service.\n\nChapter 2  Access to services",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zz-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zz-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zz-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5425a0820c5cbfa76775d80b0fe7ff0438cb6c67a7cbe4ffea0df775cf2e7f82"
    },
