    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45af",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "45AF Making a contract etc. containing a cartel provision",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-45af"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.291",
      "values:originalText": "Offence\n\n(1) A corporation commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the corporation makes a contract or arrangement, or arrives at\nan understanding; and\n\n(b) the contract, arrangement or understanding contains a cartel\nprovision.\nNote:\nChapter 2 of the Criminal Code sets out the general principles of\ncriminal responsibility.\n\n(2) The fault element for paragraph (1)(b) is knowledge or belief.\nPenalty\n\n(3) An offence against subsection (1) is punishable on conviction by a\nfine not exceeding the greater of the following:\n\n(a) $100,000,000;\n\n(b) if the court can determine the total value of the benefits that:\n\n(i) have been obtained by one or more persons; and\n\n(ii) are reasonably attributable to the commission of the\noffence;\n\n3 times that total value;\n\nChapter 3  Restrictive trade practices",
      "skos:definition": "Offence\n\n(1) A corporation commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the corporation makes a contract or arrangement, or arrives at\nan understanding; and\n\n(b) the contract, arrangement or understanding contains a cartel\nprovision.\nNote:\nChapter 2 of the Criminal Code sets out the general principles of\ncriminal responsibility.\n\n(2) The fault element for paragraph (1)(b) is knowledge or belief.\nPenalty\n\n(3) An offence against subsection (1) is punishable on conviction by a\nfine not exceeding the greater of the following:\n\n(a) $100,000,000;\n\n(b) if the court can determine the total value of the benefits that:\n\n(i) have been obtained by one or more persons; and\n\n(ii) are reasonably attributable to the commission of the\noffence;\n\n3 times that total value;\n\nChapter 3  Restrictive trade practices",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45af-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45af-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45af-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cd25b8565d4b57e8f856cf50c696d80d49eb0c79087d2888c0de2bddefadce7e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-45af",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "45AF Making a contract etc. containing a cartel provision",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 291,
      "values:originalText": "Offence\n\n(1) A corporation commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the corporation makes a contract or arrangement, or arrives at\nan understanding; and\n\n(b) the contract, arrangement or understanding contains a cartel\nprovision.\nNote:\nChapter 2 of the Criminal Code sets out the general principles of\ncriminal responsibility.\n\n(2) The fault element for paragraph (1)(b) is knowledge or belief.\nPenalty\n\n(3) An offence against subsection (1) is punishable on conviction by a\nfine not exceeding the greater of the following:\n\n(a) $100,000,000;\n\n(b) if the court can determine the total value of the benefits that:\n\n(i) have been obtained by one or more persons; and\n\n(ii) are reasonably attributable to the commission of the\noffence;\n\n3 times that total value;\n\nChapter 3  Restrictive trade practices"
    },
