      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.292",
      "values:originalText": "(3) An offence against subsection (1) is punishable on conviction by a\nfine not exceeding the greater of the following:\n\n(a) $100,000,000;\n\n(b) if the court can determine the total value of the benefits that:\n\n(i) have been obtained by one or more persons; and\n\n(ii) are reasonably attributable to the commission of the\noffence;\n\n3 times that total value;\n\n(c) if the court cannot determine the total value of those\nbenefits—30% of the corporation’s adjusted turnover during\nthe breach turnover period for the offence.\n\nRestrictive trade practices  Chapter 3\nRestrictive trade practices  Part IV\nCartel conduct  Division 1\n\nSection 45AH\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nPre-commencement contracts etc.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) An offence against subsection (1) is punishable on conviction by a\nfine not exceeding the greater of the following:\n\n(a) $100,000,000;\n\n(b) if the court can determine the total value of the benefits that:\n\n(i) have been obtained by one or more persons; and\n\n(ii) are reasonably attributable to the commission of the\noffence;\n\n3 times that total value;\n\n(c) if the court cannot determine the total value of those\nbenefits—30% of the corporation’s adjusted turnover during\nthe breach turnover period for the offence.\n\nRestrictive trade practices  Chapter 3\nRestrictive trade practices  Part IV\nCartel conduct  Division 1\n\nSection 45AH\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nPre-commencement contracts etc.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45ag"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45ag-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45ag-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bbe0bf5b51f94f6b1a3ec344062a57de12b567f1166435771273678f0b4dbb40",
      "skos:note": "Offence against subsection (1) is punishable by a fine not exceeding the greater of the following."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-45ag-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "45AG(3) Giving effect to a cartel provision",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 292,
      "values:originalText": "(3) An offence against subsection (1) is punishable on conviction by a\nfine not exceeding the greater of the following:\n\n(a) $100,000,000;\n\n(b) if the court can determine the total value of the benefits that:\n\n(i) have been obtained by one or more persons; and\n\n(ii) are reasonably attributable to the commission of the\noffence;\n\n3 times that total value;\n\n(c) if the court cannot determine the total value of those\nbenefits—30% of the corporation’s adjusted turnover during\nthe breach turnover period for the offence.\n\nRestrictive trade practices  Chapter 3\nRestrictive trade practices  Part IV\nCartel conduct  Division 1\n\nSection 45AH\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nPre-commencement contracts etc."
    },
