        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "All other parties to the contract, arrangement or understanding have been acquitted of such an offence.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The finding of guilt repeats in time with the acquittal of other parties."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45ah-ss-2-logic-deontic-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Implies",
      "cml:logicSummary": "If all other parties are acquitted, then the corporation is not found guilty.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "All other parties to the contract have been acquitted.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The corporation is not found guilty of an offence against section 45AF or 45AG."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45ah-ss-2-logic-deontic-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Implies",
      "cml:logicSummary": "If a finding of guilt would be inconsistent with the acquittal, then the corporation cannot be found guilty.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "A finding of guilt would be inconsistent with their acquittal.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The corporation cannot be found guilty of an offence against section 45AF or 45AG."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45ai",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "45AI Court may make related civil orders",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-45ai"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.293",
      "values:originalText": "If a prosecution against a person for an offence against\nsection 45AF or 45AG is being, or has been, heard by a court, the\ncourt may:\n\n(a) grant an injunction under section 80 against the person in\nrelation to:\n\n(i) the conduct that constitutes, or is alleged to constitute,\nthe offence; or\n\n(ii) other conduct of that kind; or\n\nChapter 3  Restrictive trade practices",
      "skos:definition": "If a prosecution against a person for an offence against\nsection 45AF or 45AG is being, or has been, heard by a court, the\ncourt may:\n\n(a) grant an injunction under section 80 against the person in\nrelation to:\n\n(i) the conduct that constitutes, or is alleged to constitute,\nthe offence; or\n\n(ii) other conduct of that kind; or\n\nChapter 3  Restrictive trade practices",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45ai-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45ai-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "fb571095d14bbea9cfb933e8adb0a406a8e1dd8adefbf896e69245db4f169a2c",
      "skos:note": "Court may grant injunctions against a person in relation to the conduct that constitutes or is alleged to constitute an offence."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-45ai",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "45AI Court may make related civil orders",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 293,
      "values:originalText": "If a prosecution against a person for an offence against\nsection 45AF or 45AG is being, or has been, heard by a court, the\ncourt may:\n\n(a) grant an injunction under section 80 against the person in\nrelation to:\n\n(i) the conduct that constitutes, or is alleged to constitute,\nthe offence; or\n\n(ii) other conduct of that kind; or\n\nChapter 3  Restrictive trade practices"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45ai-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
