    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45al",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "45AL Conduct notified",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-45al"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.295",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Sections 45AF, 45AG, 45AJ and 45AK do not apply to a\ncorporation in relation to a contract, arrangement or understanding\ncontaining a cartel provision, in so far as:\n\n(a) the cartel provision:\n\n(i) has the purpose, or has or is likely to have the effect,\nmentioned in subsection 45AD(2); or\n\n(ii) has the purpose mentioned in a paragraph of\nsubsection 45AD(3) other than paragraph (c); and\n\n(b) the corporation has given the Commission a collective\nbargaining notice under subsection 93AB(1A) setting out\nparticulars of the contract, arrangement or understanding; and\n\n(c) the notice is in force under section 93AD.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (1) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code and\nsubsection (2) of this section).\n\n(2) A person who wishes to rely on subsection (1) in relation to a\ncontravention of section 45AJ or 45AK bears an evidential burden\nin relation to that matter.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Sections 45AF, 45AG, 45AJ and 45AK do not apply to a\ncorporation in relation to a contract, arrangement or understanding\ncontaining a cartel provision, in so far as:\n\n(a) the cartel provision:\n\n(i) has the purpose, or has or is likely to have the effect,\nmentioned in subsection 45AD(2); or\n\n(ii) has the purpose mentioned in a paragraph of\nsubsection 45AD(3) other than paragraph (c); and\n\n(b) the corporation has given the Commission a collective\nbargaining notice under subsection 93AB(1A) setting out\nparticulars of the contract, arrangement or understanding; and\n\n(c) the notice is in force under section 93AD.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (1) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code and\nsubsection (2) of this section).\n\n(2) A person who wishes to rely on subsection (1) in relation to a\ncontravention of section 45AJ or 45AK bears an evidential burden\nin relation to that matter.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45al-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45al-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "689c44def77f091e626b979d4f101d289a94e0e98a1e088fce18de70fa0d8b74"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-45al",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "45AL Conduct notified",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 295,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Sections 45AF, 45AG, 45AJ and 45AK do not apply to a\ncorporation in relation to a contract, arrangement or understanding\ncontaining a cartel provision, in so far as:\n\n(a) the cartel provision:\n\n(i) has the purpose, or has or is likely to have the effect,\nmentioned in subsection 45AD(2); or\n\n(ii) has the purpose mentioned in a paragraph of\nsubsection 45AD(3) other than paragraph (c); and\n\n(b) the corporation has given the Commission a collective\nbargaining notice under subsection 93AB(1A) setting out\nparticulars of the contract, arrangement or understanding; and\n\n(c) the notice is in force under section 93AD.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (1) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code and\nsubsection (2) of this section).\n\n(2) A person who wishes to rely on subsection (1) in relation to a\ncontravention of section 45AJ or 45AK bears an evidential burden\nin relation to that matter."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45al-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "45AL(1) Conduct notified",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-45al-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.295",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Sections 45AF, 45AG, 45AJ and 45AK do not apply to a\ncorporation in relation to a contract, arrangement or understanding\ncontaining a cartel provision, in so far as:\n\n(a) the cartel provision:\n\n(i) has the purpose, or has or is likely to have the effect,\nmentioned in subsection 45AD(2); or\n\n(ii) has the purpose mentioned in a paragraph of\nsubsection 45AD(3) other than paragraph (c); and\n\n(b) the corporation has given the Commission a collective\nbargaining notice under subsection 93AB(1A) setting out\nparticulars of the contract, arrangement or understanding; and\n\n(c) the notice is in force under section 93AD.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (1) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code and\nsubsection (2) of this section).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Sections 45AF, 45AG, 45AJ and 45AK do not apply to a\ncorporation in relation to a contract, arrangement or understanding\ncontaining a cartel provision, in so far as:\n\n(a) the cartel provision:\n\n(i) has the purpose, or has or is likely to have the effect,\nmentioned in subsection 45AD(2); or\n\n(ii) has the purpose mentioned in a paragraph of\nsubsection 45AD(3) other than paragraph (c); and\n\n(b) the corporation has given the Commission a collective\nbargaining notice under subsection 93AB(1A) setting out\nparticulars of the contract, arrangement or understanding; and\n\n(c) the notice is in force under section 93AD.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (1) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code and\nsubsection (2) of this section).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45al"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45al-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45al-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "80d8fae3214c375d6bdd573c0648f7cd549a060de8b8df86ee0a7722054389a0",
      "skos:note": "Exempts corporations from cartel provisions under certain conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-45al-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "45AL(1) Conduct notified",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 295,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Sections 45AF, 45AG, 45AJ and 45AK do not apply to a\ncorporation in relation to a contract, arrangement or understanding\ncontaining a cartel provision, in so far as:\n\n(a) the cartel provision:\n\n(i) has the purpose, or has or is likely to have the effect,\nmentioned in subsection 45AD(2); or\n\n(ii) has the purpose mentioned in a paragraph of\nsubsection 45AD(3) other than paragraph (c); and\n\n(b) the corporation has given the Commission a collective\nbargaining notice under subsection 93AB(1A) setting out\nparticulars of the contract, arrangement or understanding; and\n\n(c) the notice is in force under section 93AD.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (1) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code and\nsubsection (2) of this section)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45al-ss-1-norm",
