    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45am",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "45AM Cartel provision subject to grant of authorisation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-45am"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.295",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Sections 45AF and 45AJ do not apply in relation to the making of\na contract that contains a cartel provision if:\n\n(a) the contract is subject to a condition that the provision will\nnot come into force unless and until the corporation is\ngranted an authorisation to give effect to the provision; and\n\n(b) the corporation applies for the grant of such an authorisation\nwithin 14 days after the contract is made.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (1) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code and\nsubsection (2) of this section).\n\nChapter 3  Restrictive trade practices",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Sections 45AF and 45AJ do not apply in relation to the making of\na contract that contains a cartel provision if:\n\n(a) the contract is subject to a condition that the provision will\nnot come into force unless and until the corporation is\ngranted an authorisation to give effect to the provision; and\n\n(b) the corporation applies for the grant of such an authorisation\nwithin 14 days after the contract is made.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (1) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code and\nsubsection (2) of this section).\n\nChapter 3  Restrictive trade practices",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45am-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45am-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1381c8882a76466be7644b8184fbe96879e35f384c6a64f70bf1a9dc3bb8cdf5",
      "skos:note": "Grant of authorisation required for cartel provision"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-45am",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "45AM Cartel provision subject to grant of authorisation",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 295,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Sections 45AF and 45AJ do not apply in relation to the making of\na contract that contains a cartel provision if:\n\n(a) the contract is subject to a condition that the provision will\nnot come into force unless and until the corporation is\ngranted an authorisation to give effect to the provision; and\n\n(b) the corporation applies for the grant of such an authorisation\nwithin 14 days after the contract is made.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (1) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code and\nsubsection (2) of this section).\n\nChapter 3  Restrictive trade practices"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45am-norm",
      "@type": "values:Permission",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45am"
      },
