      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45an",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "45AN Contracts, arrangements or understandings between related",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-45an"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.296",
      "values:originalText": "bodies corporate\n\n(1) Sections 45AF, 45AG, 45AJ and 45AK do not apply in relation to\na contract, arrangement or understanding if the only parties to the\ncontract, arrangement or understanding are bodies corporate that\nare related to each other.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (1) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code and\nsubsection (2) of this section).\n\n(2) A person who wishes to rely on subsection (1) in relation to a\ncontravention of section 45AJ or 45AK bears an evidential burden\nin relation to that matter.",
      "skos:definition": "bodies corporate\n\n(1) Sections 45AF, 45AG, 45AJ and 45AK do not apply in relation to\na contract, arrangement or understanding if the only parties to the\ncontract, arrangement or understanding are bodies corporate that\nare related to each other.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (1) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code and\nsubsection (2) of this section).\n\n(2) A person who wishes to rely on subsection (1) in relation to a\ncontravention of section 45AJ or 45AK bears an evidential burden\nin relation to that matter.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45an-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45an-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a6a4208d48c2f887281312b9ede7a7cc13256610ce7c9de89f2eed59015a360b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-45an",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "45AN Contracts, arrangements or understandings between related",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 296,
      "values:originalText": "bodies corporate\n\n(1) Sections 45AF, 45AG, 45AJ and 45AK do not apply in relation to\na contract, arrangement or understanding if the only parties to the\ncontract, arrangement or understanding are bodies corporate that\nare related to each other.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (1) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code and\nsubsection (2) of this section).\n\n(2) A person who wishes to rely on subsection (1) in relation to a\ncontravention of section 45AJ or 45AK bears an evidential burden\nin relation to that matter."
    },
