    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45aq",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "45AQ Resale price maintenance",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-45aq"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.298",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Sections 45AF, 45AG, 45AJ and 45AK do not apply in relation to\na contract, arrangement or understanding containing a cartel\nprovision, in so far as the cartel provision relates to:\n\n(a) conduct that contravenes section 48; or\n\n(b) conduct that would contravene section 48 but for the\noperation of section 88; or\n\nRestrictive trade practices  Chapter 3\nRestrictive trade practices  Part IV\nCartel conduct  Division 1\n\nSection 45AR\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(c) conduct that would contravene section 48 if this Act defined\nthe acts constituting the practice of resale price maintenance\nby reference to the maximum price at which goods or\nservices are to be sold or supplied or are to be advertised,\ndisplayed or offered for sale or supply.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (1) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code and\nsubsection (2) of this section).\n\n(2) A person who wishes to rely on subsection (1) in relation to a\ncontravention of section 45AJ or 45AK bears an evidential burden\nin relation to that matter.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Sections 45AF, 45AG, 45AJ and 45AK do not apply in relation to\na contract, arrangement or understanding containing a cartel\nprovision, in so far as the cartel provision relates to:\n\n(a) conduct that contravenes section 48; or\n\n(b) conduct that would contravene section 48 but for the\noperation of section 88; or\n\nRestrictive trade practices  Chapter 3\nRestrictive trade practices  Part IV\nCartel conduct  Division 1\n\nSection 45AR\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(c) conduct that would contravene section 48 if this Act defined\nthe acts constituting the practice of resale price maintenance\nby reference to the maximum price at which goods or\nservices are to be sold or supplied or are to be advertised,\ndisplayed or offered for sale or supply.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (1) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code and\nsubsection (2) of this section).\n\n(2) A person who wishes to rely on subsection (1) in relation to a\ncontravention of section 45AJ or 45AK bears an evidential burden\nin relation to that matter.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45aq-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45aq-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c9842975a7a90062e7228285d3562bfdec429ea64f54a2919c965cb033e5cd4d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-45aq",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "45AQ Resale price maintenance",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 298,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Sections 45AF, 45AG, 45AJ and 45AK do not apply in relation to\na contract, arrangement or understanding containing a cartel\nprovision, in so far as the cartel provision relates to:\n\n(a) conduct that contravenes section 48; or\n\n(b) conduct that would contravene section 48 but for the\noperation of section 88; or\n\nRestrictive trade practices  Chapter 3\nRestrictive trade practices  Part IV\nCartel conduct  Division 1\n\nSection 45AR\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(c) conduct that would contravene section 48 if this Act defined\nthe acts constituting the practice of resale price maintenance\nby reference to the maximum price at which goods or\nservices are to be sold or supplied or are to be advertised,\ndisplayed or offered for sale or supply.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (1) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code and\nsubsection (2) of this section).\n\n(2) A person who wishes to rely on subsection (1) in relation to a\ncontravention of section 45AJ or 45AK bears an evidential burden\nin relation to that matter."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45aq-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "45AQ(1) Resale price maintenance",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-45aq-ss-1"
