    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45as",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "45AS Dual listed company arrangement",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-45as"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.300",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Sections 45AF and 45AJ do not apply in relation to the making of\na contract, arrangement or understanding that contains a cartel\nprovision, in so far as:\n\n(a) the contract, arrangement or understanding is a dual listed\ncompany arrangement; and\n\n(b) the making of the contract, arrangement or understanding\nwould, or would apart from section 88, contravene\nsection 49.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (1) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code and\nsubsection (3) of this section).\n\n(2) Sections 45AG and 45AK do not apply in relation to the giving\neffect to a cartel provision, in so far as:\n\n(a) the cartel provision is a provision of a dual listed company\narrangement; and\n\n(b) the giving effect to the cartel provision would, or would apart\nfrom section 88, contravene section 49.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (2) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code and\nsubsection (3) of this section).\n\nRestrictive trade practices  Chapter 3\nRestrictive trade practices  Part IV\nCartel conduct  Division 1\n\nSection 45AT\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(3) A person who wishes to rely on subsection (1) or (2) in relation to\na contravention of section 45AJ or 45AK bears an evidential\nburden in relation to that matter.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Sections 45AF and 45AJ do not apply in relation to the making of\na contract, arrangement or understanding that contains a cartel\nprovision, in so far as:\n\n(a) the contract, arrangement or understanding is a dual listed\ncompany arrangement; and\n\n(b) the making of the contract, arrangement or understanding\nwould, or would apart from section 88, contravene\nsection 49.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (1) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code and\nsubsection (3) of this section).\n\n(2) Sections 45AG and 45AK do not apply in relation to the giving\neffect to a cartel provision, in so far as:\n\n(a) the cartel provision is a provision of a dual listed company\narrangement; and\n\n(b) the giving effect to the cartel provision would, or would apart\nfrom section 88, contravene section 49.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (2) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code and\nsubsection (3) of this section).\n\nRestrictive trade practices  Chapter 3\nRestrictive trade practices  Part IV\nCartel conduct  Division 1\n\nSection 45AT\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(3) A person who wishes to rely on subsection (1) or (2) in relation to\na contravention of section 45AJ or 45AK bears an evidential\nburden in relation to that matter.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45as-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45as-ss-2"
        },
