    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45at",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "45AT Acquisition of shares or assets",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-45at"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.301",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Sections 45AF, 45AG, 45AJ and 45AK do not apply in relation to\na contract, arrangement or understanding containing a cartel\nprovision, in so far as the cartel provision provides directly or\nindirectly for the acquisition of:\n\n(a) any shares in the capital of a body corporate; or\n\n(b) any assets of a person.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (1) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code and\nsubsection (2) of this section).\n\n(2) A person who wishes to rely on subsection (1) in relation to a\ncontravention of section 45AJ or 45AK bears an evidential burden\nin relation to that matter.\n\n(3) Sections 45AF, 45AG, 45AJ and 45AK do not apply in relation to\na contract, arrangement or understanding containing a cartel\nprovision, in so far as the cartel provision provides for an\nacquisition, if the acquisition is a notified acquisition.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this\nsubsection (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code and\nsubsection (4) of this section).\n\n(4) A person who wishes to rely on subsection (3) in relation to a\ncontravention of section 45AJ or 45AK bears an evidential burden\nin relation to that matter.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Sections 45AF, 45AG, 45AJ and 45AK do not apply in relation to\na contract, arrangement or understanding containing a cartel\nprovision, in so far as the cartel provision provides directly or\nindirectly for the acquisition of:\n\n(a) any shares in the capital of a body corporate; or\n\n(b) any assets of a person.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (1) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code and\nsubsection (2) of this section).\n\n(2) A person who wishes to rely on subsection (1) in relation to a\ncontravention of section 45AJ or 45AK bears an evidential burden\nin relation to that matter.\n\n(3) Sections 45AF, 45AG, 45AJ and 45AK do not apply in relation to\na contract, arrangement or understanding containing a cartel\nprovision, in so far as the cartel provision provides for an\nacquisition, if the acquisition is a notified acquisition.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this\nsubsection (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code and\nsubsection (4) of this section).\n\n(4) A person who wishes to rely on subsection (3) in relation to a\ncontravention of section 45AJ or 45AK bears an evidential burden\nin relation to that matter.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45at-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45at-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45at-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45at-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "751f4cb75bbb0455d86d0a1bbe49a120e4693e25f5dd6d5460850d3beabe233a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-45at",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "45AT Acquisition of shares or assets",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 301,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Sections 45AF, 45AG, 45AJ and 45AK do not apply in relation to\na contract, arrangement or understanding containing a cartel\nprovision, in so far as the cartel provision provides directly or\nindirectly for the acquisition of:\n\n(a) any shares in the capital of a body corporate; or\n\n(b) any assets of a person.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (1) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code and\nsubsection (2) of this section).\n\n(2) A person who wishes to rely on subsection (1) in relation to a\ncontravention of section 45AJ or 45AK bears an evidential burden\nin relation to that matter.\n\n(3) Sections 45AF, 45AG, 45AJ and 45AK do not apply in relation to\na contract, arrangement or understanding containing a cartel\nprovision, in so far as the cartel provision provides for an\nacquisition, if the acquisition is a notified acquisition.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this\nsubsection (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code and\nsubsection (4) of this section).\n\n(4) A person who wishes to rely on subsection (3) in relation to a\ncontravention of section 45AJ or 45AK bears an evidential burden\nin relation to that matter."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45at-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "45AT(1) Acquisition of shares or assets",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-45at-ss-1"
      },
