    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45aw",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "45AW Commission must be notified of acquisitions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-45aw"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.303",
      "values:originalText": "A person contravenes this section if:\n\n(a) the person is a principal party to an acquisition; and\n\n(b) the acquisition is required to be notified; and\n\n(c) the acquisition is put into effect; and\n\n(d) when the acquisition is put into effect:\n\n(i) the acquisition is not a notified acquisition; or\n\n(ii) no notification of the acquisition has an effective\nnotification date (see section 51ABZ); or\n\n(iii) the latest notification of the acquisition that has an\neffective notification date is stale.\nNote 1:\nFor when an acquisition is required to be notified, see Division 2 of",
      "skos:definition": "A person contravenes this section if:\n\n(a) the person is a principal party to an acquisition; and\n\n(b) the acquisition is required to be notified; and\n\n(c) the acquisition is put into effect; and\n\n(d) when the acquisition is put into effect:\n\n(i) the acquisition is not a notified acquisition; or\n\n(ii) no notification of the acquisition has an effective\nnotification date (see section 51ABZ); or\n\n(iii) the latest notification of the acquisition that has an\neffective notification date is stale.\nNote 1:\nFor when an acquisition is required to be notified, see Division 2 of",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45aw-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45aw-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7bd2b4b0110f956af5072a699b8b642d2b756c4eafcd43f0d4a61cc2ecf36d83",
      "skos:note": "Failure to notify acquisitions is prohibited."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-45aw",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "45AW Commission must be notified of acquisitions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 303,
      "values:originalText": "A person contravenes this section if:\n\n(a) the person is a principal party to an acquisition; and\n\n(b) the acquisition is required to be notified; and\n\n(c) the acquisition is put into effect; and\n\n(d) when the acquisition is put into effect:\n\n(i) the acquisition is not a notified acquisition; or\n\n(ii) no notification of the acquisition has an effective\nnotification date (see section 51ABZ); or\n\n(iii) the latest notification of the acquisition that has an\neffective notification date is stale.\nNote 1:\nFor when an acquisition is required to be notified, see Division 2 of"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45aw-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45aw"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45aw-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibition of failure to notify acquisitions.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Acquisitions must be notified.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Failure to notify is prohibited."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45ax",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "45AX Commission must be notified of material changes of fact in",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-45ax"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.304",
      "values:originalText": "relation to notified acquisitions\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a person is the notifying party of a notification of an\nacquisition; and\n\n(b) a change of fact occurs; and\n\n(c) the change of fact is material to the Commission making a\ndetermination under subsection 51ABZE(1) in respect of the\nnotification; and\n\n(d) the person becomes aware of the change of fact at a time:\n\n(i) occurring on or after the effective notification date of\nthe notification; and\n\n(ii) at which the Commission has not decided to cease\nconsidering the notification under section 51ABZD; and\n\n(iii) at which the Commission has not made a determination\nin respect of the notification under\nsubsection 51ABZE(1); and\n\n(iv) if the notification is subject to phase 2 review—\noccurring at least 15 business days (within the meaning\nof section 51ABK) before the end of the phase 2\ndetermination period for the notification.\n\n(2) For the purposes of this section, the person is taken to become\naware of the change of fact at the earliest time at which the person\nis:\n\n(a) aware of the change of fact; and\n\n(b) aware that the change of fact is material in the way described\nin paragraph (1)(c).\n\n(3) This section also applies if:\n\n(a) a person is the notifying party of a notification of an\nacquisition; and\n\n(b) the notifying party has made a public benefit application in\nrelation to the notification; and\n\n(c) a change of fact occurs; and\n\nRestrictive trade practices  Chapter 3\nRestrictive trade practices  Part IV\nAcquisitions  Division 1A\n\nSection 45AY\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(d) the change of fact is material to the Commission making a\ndetermination under subsection 51ABZW(1) in respect of the\napplication; and\n\n(e) the person becomes aware of the change of fact at a time:\n\n(i) occurring on or after the effective application date of the\napplication; and\n\n(ii) at which the Commission has not decided to cease\nconsidering the application under section 51ABZV; and\n\n(iii) at which the Commission has not made a determination\nunder subsection 51ABZW(1) in respect of the\napplication.\n\n(4) For the purposes of this section, the person is taken to become\naware of the change of fact at the earliest time at which the person\nis:\n\n(a) aware of the change of fact; and\n\n(b) aware that the change of fact is material in the way described\nin paragraph (3)(d).\n\n(5) The person contravenes this subsection if the Commission is not\nnotified of the change of fact, as soon as practicable after the\nperson becomes aware of the change, by:\n\n(a) if the person is the only notifying party of the notification of\nthe acquisition—the person; or\n\n(b) otherwise—all of the notifying parties jointly.\nNote:\nFor enforcement, see Part VI.\n\n(6) For the purposes of this section, a person who ought reasonably to\nbe aware of something is taken to be aware of it.",
      "skos:definition": "relation to notified acquisitions\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a person is the notifying party of a notification of an\nacquisition; and\n\n(b) a change of fact occurs; and\n\n(c) the change of fact is material to the Commission making a\ndetermination under subsection 51ABZE(1) in respect of the\nnotification; and\n\n(d) the person becomes aware of the change of fact at a time:\n\n(i) occurring on or after the effective notification date of\nthe notification; and\n\n(ii) at which the Commission has not decided to cease\nconsidering the notification under section 51ABZD; and\n\n(iii) at which the Commission has not made a determination\nin respect of the notification under\nsubsection 51ABZE(1); and\n\n(iv) if the notification is subject to phase 2 review—\noccurring at least 15 business days (within the meaning\nof section 51ABK) before the end of the phase 2\ndetermination period for the notification.\n\n(2) For the purposes of this section, the person is taken to become\naware of the change of fact at the earliest time at which the person\nis:\n\n(a) aware of the change of fact; and\n\n(b) aware that the change of fact is material in the way described\nin paragraph (1)(c).\n\n(3) This section also applies if:\n\n(a) a person is the notifying party of a notification of an\nacquisition; and\n\n(b) the notifying party has made a public benefit application in\nrelation to the notification; and\n\n(c) a change of fact occurs; and\n\nRestrictive trade practices  Chapter 3\nRestrictive trade practices  Part IV\nAcquisitions  Division 1A\n\nSection 45AY\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(d) the change of fact is material to the Commission making a\ndetermination under subsection 51ABZW(1) in respect of the\napplication; and\n\n(e) the person becomes aware of the change of fact at a time:\n\n(i) occurring on or after the effective application date of the\napplication; and\n\n(ii) at which the Commission has not decided to cease\nconsidering the application under section 51ABZV; and\n\n(iii) at ",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45ax-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45ax-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45ax-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45ax-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45ax-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45ax-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "23b548b3eb87792add053c5685b5dff178296bf555691c0eddc2c19098e780fa"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-45ax",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "45AX Commission must be notified of material changes of fact in",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 304,
      "values:originalText": "relation to notified acquisitions\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a person is the notifying party of a notification of an\nacquisition; and\n\n(b) a change of fact occurs; and\n\n(c) the change of fact is material to the Commission making a\ndetermination under subsection 51ABZE(1) in respect of the\nnotification; and\n\n(d) the person becomes aware of the change of fact at a time:\n\n(i) occurring on or after the effective notification date of\nthe notification; and\n\n(ii) at which the Commission has not decided to cease\nconsidering the notification under section 51ABZD; and\n\n(iii) at which the Commission has not made a determination\nin respect of the notification under\nsubsection 51ABZE(1); and\n\n(iv) if the notification is subject to phase 2 review—\noccurring at least 15 business days (within the meaning\nof section 51ABK) before the end of the phase 2\ndetermination period for the notification.\n\n(2) For the purposes of this section, the person is taken to become\naware of the change of fact at the earliest time at which the person\nis:\n\n(a) aware of the change of fact; and\n\n(b) aware that the change of fact is material in the way described\nin paragraph (1)(c).\n\n(3) This section also applies if:\n\n(a) a person is the notifying party of a notification of an\nacquisition; and\n\n(b) the notifying party has made a public benefit application in\nrelation to the notification; and\n\n(c) a change of fact occurs; and\n\nRestrictive trade practices  Chapter 3\nRestrictive trade practices  Part IV\nAcquisitions  Division 1A\n\nSection 45AY\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(d) the change of fact is material to the Commission making a\ndetermination under subsection 51ABZW(1) in respect of the\napplication; and\n\n(e) the person becomes aware of the change of fact at a time:\n\n(i) occurring on or after the effective application date of the\napplication; and\n\n(ii) at which the Commission has not decided to cease\nconsidering the application under section 51ABZV; and\n\n(iii) at which the Commission has not made a determination\nunder subsection 51ABZW(1) in respect of the\napplication.\n\n(4) For the purposes of this section, the person is taken to become\naware of the change of fact at the earliest time at which the person\nis:\n\n(a) aware of the change of fact; and\n\n(b) aware that the change of fact is material in the way described\nin paragraph (3)(d).\n\n(5) The person contravenes this subsection if the Commission is not\nnotified of the change of fact, as soon as practicable after the\nperson becomes aware of the change, by:\n\n(a) if the person is the only notifying party of the notification of\nthe acquisition—the person; or\n\n(b) otherwise—all of the notifying parties jointly.\nNote:\nFor enforcement, see Part VI.\n\n(6) For the purposes of this section, a person who ought reasonably to\nbe aware of something is taken to be aware of it."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45ax-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "45AX(1) Commission must be notified of material changes of fact in",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-45ax-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
