    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45ay",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "45AY Stayed acquisitions must not be put into effect",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-45ay"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.305",
      "values:originalText": "A person contravenes this section if:\n\n(a) the person puts an acquisition into effect; and\n\n(b) the acquisition is stayed.\nNote 1:\nFor when an acquisition is stayed, see section 51ABE.\nNote 2:\nFor enforcement, see Part VI.\n\nChapter 3  Restrictive trade practices",
      "skos:definition": "A person contravenes this section if:\n\n(a) the person puts an acquisition into effect; and\n\n(b) the acquisition is stayed.\nNote 1:\nFor when an acquisition is stayed, see section 51ABE.\nNote 2:\nFor enforcement, see Part VI.\n\nChapter 3  Restrictive trade practices",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45ay-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45ay-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a65f47c93663e2a3a2bcd1f94ec3fdc4c37df7a2e7aeaf12bccb2ae71fb4c4cf",
      "skos:note": "Acquisitions stayed must not be put into effect"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-45ay",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "45AY Stayed acquisitions must not be put into effect",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 305,
      "values:originalText": "A person contravenes this section if:\n\n(a) the person puts an acquisition into effect; and\n\n(b) the acquisition is stayed.\nNote 1:\nFor when an acquisition is stayed, see section 51ABE.\nNote 2:\nFor enforcement, see Part VI.\n\nChapter 3  Restrictive trade practices"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45ay-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45ay"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45ay-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits putting acquisitions into effect when stayed",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Acquisition is stayed",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Cannot put acquisition into effect"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45az",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "45AZ Conditions must be complied with",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-45az"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.306",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies to a person who puts a notified acquisition into\neffect, if putting the acquisition into effect is subject to conditions.\nNote:\nFor when putting an acquisition into effect is subject to conditions, see\nsection 51ABH.\n\n(2) The person contravenes this subsection if any of those conditions\nare not complied with.\nNote:\nFor enforcement, see Part VI.\nSubdivision C—Acquisitions void if put into effect while stayed\n45AZA  Acquisitions void if put into effect while stayed\n\n(1) This section applies to an acquisition that is put into effect, or\npurportedly put into effect, in contravention of section 45AY.\n\n(2) The acquisition is, and is taken always to have been, void by force\nof this subsection.\nSubdivision D—Miscellaneous\n45AZB  Providing false or misleading information\n\nA person contravenes this section if:\n\n(a) the person gives information to the Commission or the\nTribunal under an acquisitions provision; and\n\n(b) the information is false or misleading in a material particular;\nand\n\n(c) the person knows that, or is reckless as to whether, the\ninformation is false or misleading in a material particular.\nNote:\nFor enforcement, see Part VI.\n\nRestrictive trade practices  Chapter 3\nRestrictive trade practices  Part IV\nOther provisions  Division 2\n\nSection 45\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies to a person who puts a notified acquisition into\neffect, if putting the acquisition into effect is subject to conditions.\nNote:\nFor when putting an acquisition into effect is subject to conditions, see\nsection 51ABH.\n\n(2) The person contravenes this subsection if any of those conditions\nare not complied with.\nNote:\nFor enforcement, see Part VI.\nSubdivision C—Acquisitions void if put into effect while stayed\n45AZA  Acquisitions void if put into effect while stayed\n\n(1) This section applies to an acquisition that is put into effect, or\npurportedly put into effect, in contravention of section 45AY.\n\n(2) The acquisition is, and is taken always to have been, void by force\nof this subsection.\nSubdivision D—Miscellaneous\n45AZB  Providing false or misleading information\n\nA person contravenes this section if:\n\n(a) the person gives information to the Commission or the\nTribunal under an acquisitions provision; and\n\n(b) the information is false or misleading in a material particular;\nand\n\n(c) the person knows that, or is reckless as to whether, the\ninformation is false or misleading in a material particular.\nNote:\nFor enforcement, see Part VI.\n\nRestrictive trade practices  Chapter 3\nRestrictive trade practices  Part IV\nOther provisions  Division 2\n\nSection 45\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45az-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45az-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45az-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45az-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e550fec92bd71d9d7ab195a79fbc05ca79820694aa4f0bfd75967fa7f61e758f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-45az",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "45AZ Conditions must be complied with",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 306,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies to a person who puts a notified acquisition into\neffect, if putting the acquisition into effect is subject to conditions.\nNote:\nFor when putting an acquisition into effect is subject to conditions, see\nsection 51ABH.\n\n(2) The person contravenes this subsection if any of those conditions\nare not complied with.\nNote:\nFor enforcement, see Part VI.\nSubdivision C—Acquisitions void if put into effect while stayed\n45AZA  Acquisitions void if put into effect while stayed\n\n(1) This section applies to an acquisition that is put into effect, or\npurportedly put into effect, in contravention of section 45AY.\n\n(2) The acquisition is, and is taken always to have been, void by force\nof this subsection.\nSubdivision D—Miscellaneous\n45AZB  Providing false or misleading information\n\nA person contravenes this section if:\n\n(a) the person gives information to the Commission or the\nTribunal under an acquisitions provision; and\n\n(b) the information is false or misleading in a material particular;\nand\n\n(c) the person knows that, or is reckless as to whether, the\ninformation is false or misleading in a material particular.\nNote:\nFor enforcement, see Part VI.\n\nRestrictive trade practices  Chapter 3\nRestrictive trade practices  Part IV\nOther provisions  Division 2\n\nSection 45\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026"
    },
    {
