    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45d",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "45D Secondary boycotts for the purpose of causing substantial loss",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-45d"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.311",
      "values:originalText": "or damage\n\n(1) In the circumstances specified in subsection (3) or (4), a person\nmust not, in concert with a second person, engage in conduct:\n\n(a) that hinders or prevents:\n\n(i) a third person supplying goods or services to a fourth\nperson (who is not an employer of the first person or the\nsecond person); or\n\n(ii) a third person acquiring goods or services from a fourth\nperson (who is not an employer of the first person or the\nsecond person); and\n\n(b) that is engaged in for the purpose, and would have or be\nlikely to have the effect, of causing substantial loss or\ndamage to the business of the fourth person.\nNote 1:\nConduct that would otherwise contravene this section can be\nauthorised under section 88.\nNote 2:\nThis section also has effect subject to section 45DD, which deals with\npermitted boycotts.\n\n(2) A person is taken to engage in conduct for a purpose mentioned in\nsubsection (1) if the person engages in the conduct for purposes\nthat include that purpose.\n\nChapter 3  Restrictive trade practices",
      "skos:definition": "or damage\n\n(1) In the circumstances specified in subsection (3) or (4), a person\nmust not, in concert with a second person, engage in conduct:\n\n(a) that hinders or prevents:\n\n(i) a third person supplying goods or services to a fourth\nperson (who is not an employer of the first person or the\nsecond person); or\n\n(ii) a third person acquiring goods or services from a fourth\nperson (who is not an employer of the first person or the\nsecond person); and\n\n(b) that is engaged in for the purpose, and would have or be\nlikely to have the effect, of causing substantial loss or\ndamage to the business of the fourth person.\nNote 1:\nConduct that would otherwise contravene this section can be\nauthorised under section 88.\nNote 2:\nThis section also has effect subject to section 45DD, which deals with\npermitted boycotts.\n\n(2) A person is taken to engage in conduct for a purpose mentioned in\nsubsection (1) if the person engages in the conduct for purposes\nthat include that purpose.\n\nChapter 3  Restrictive trade practices",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45d-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45d-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "146423aa386df2a693c3e36c807354dacdf405580c9ebcfb859feba8d9a55e94"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-45d",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "45D Secondary boycotts for the purpose of causing substantial loss",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 311,
      "values:originalText": "or damage\n\n(1) In the circumstances specified in subsection (3) or (4), a person\nmust not, in concert with a second person, engage in conduct:\n\n(a) that hinders or prevents:\n\n(i) a third person supplying goods or services to a fourth\nperson (who is not an employer of the first person or the\nsecond person); or\n\n(ii) a third person acquiring goods or services from a fourth\nperson (who is not an employer of the first person or the\nsecond person); and\n\n(b) that is engaged in for the purpose, and would have or be\nlikely to have the effect, of causing substantial loss or\ndamage to the business of the fourth person.\nNote 1:\nConduct that would otherwise contravene this section can be\nauthorised under section 88.\nNote 2:\nThis section also has effect subject to section 45DD, which deals with\npermitted boycotts.\n\n(2) A person is taken to engage in conduct for a purpose mentioned in\nsubsection (1) if the person engages in the conduct for purposes\nthat include that purpose.\n\nChapter 3  Restrictive trade practices"
    },
