    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45db",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "45DB Boycotts affecting trade or commerce",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-45db"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.313",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person must not, in concert with another person, engage in\nconduct for the purpose, and having or likely to have the effect, of\npreventing or substantially hindering a third person (who is not an\nemployer of the first person) from engaging in trade or commerce\ninvolving the movement of goods between Australia and places\noutside Australia.\nNote 1:\nConduct that would otherwise contravene this section can be\nauthorised under section 88.\nNote 2:\nThis section also has effect subject to section 45DD, which deals with\npermitted boycotts.\n\n(2) A person is taken to engage in conduct for a purpose mentioned in\nsubsection (1) if the person engages in the conduct for purposes\nthat include that purpose.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person must not, in concert with another person, engage in\nconduct for the purpose, and having or likely to have the effect, of\npreventing or substantially hindering a third person (who is not an\nemployer of the first person) from engaging in trade or commerce\ninvolving the movement of goods between Australia and places\noutside Australia.\nNote 1:\nConduct that would otherwise contravene this section can be\nauthorised under section 88.\nNote 2:\nThis section also has effect subject to section 45DD, which deals with\npermitted boycotts.\n\n(2) A person is taken to engage in conduct for a purpose mentioned in\nsubsection (1) if the person engages in the conduct for purposes\nthat include that purpose.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45db-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45db-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9b70009a5c423ae3ea9f1c15e17e51d7c4c42c72866e24663cf4a121a5094b25"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-45db",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "45DB Boycotts affecting trade or commerce",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 313,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person must not, in concert with another person, engage in\nconduct for the purpose, and having or likely to have the effect, of\npreventing or substantially hindering a third person (who is not an\nemployer of the first person) from engaging in trade or commerce\ninvolving the movement of goods between Australia and places\noutside Australia.\nNote 1:\nConduct that would otherwise contravene this section can be\nauthorised under section 88.\nNote 2:\nThis section also has effect subject to section 45DD, which deals with\npermitted boycotts.\n\n(2) A person is taken to engage in conduct for a purpose mentioned in\nsubsection (1) if the person engages in the conduct for purposes\nthat include that purpose."
    },
