    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45dc",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "45DC Involvement and liability of employee organisations",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-45dc"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.313",
      "values:originalText": "Certain organisations taken to be acting in concert\n\n(1) If 2 or more persons (the participants), each of whom is a member\nor officer of the same organisation of employees, engage in\nconduct in concert with one another, whether or not the conduct is\nalso engaged in in concert with another person, then, unless the\norganisation proves otherwise, the organisation is taken for the\npurposes of sections 45D, 45DA and 45DB:\n\n(a) to engage in that conduct in concert with the participants; and\n\n(b) to have engaged in that conduct for the purposes for which\nthe participants engaged in it.\n\nChapter 3  Restrictive trade practices",
      "skos:definition": "Certain organisations taken to be acting in concert\n\n(1) If 2 or more persons (the participants), each of whom is a member\nor officer of the same organisation of employees, engage in\nconduct in concert with one another, whether or not the conduct is\nalso engaged in in concert with another person, then, unless the\norganisation proves otherwise, the organisation is taken for the\npurposes of sections 45D, 45DA and 45DB:\n\n(a) to engage in that conduct in concert with the participants; and\n\n(b) to have engaged in that conduct for the purposes for which\nthe participants engaged in it.\n\nChapter 3  Restrictive trade practices",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45dc-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45dc-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45dc-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45dc-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45dc-logic-argumentation-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9addd4969abf564219da16001daefc583dd8bee34daf5a7c3ef87e6ebc385819",
      "skos:note": "Organisation is taken for purposes of sections 45D, 45DA and 45DB if participants engage in conduct in concert."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-45dc",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "45DC Involvement and liability of employee organisations",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 313,
      "values:originalText": "Certain organisations taken to be acting in concert\n\n(1) If 2 or more persons (the participants), each of whom is a member\nor officer of the same organisation of employees, engage in\nconduct in concert with one another, whether or not the conduct is\nalso engaged in in concert with another person, then, unless the\norganisation proves otherwise, the organisation is taken for the\npurposes of sections 45D, 45DA and 45DB:\n\n(a) to engage in that conduct in concert with the participants; and\n\n(b) to have engaged in that conduct for the purposes for which\nthe participants engaged in it.\n\nChapter 3  Restrictive trade practices"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45dc-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45dc"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45dc-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Organisation is obligated to engage in conduct in concert with participants.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Participants engage in conduct in concert.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Organisation is taken for purposes of sections 45D, 45DA and 45DB."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45dc-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Overlaps",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Conduct in concert with participants overlaps with conduct of the organisation.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Participants engage in conduct in concert.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Organisation is taken for purposes of sections 45D, 45DA and 45DB."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45dc-logic-ltl-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LTL"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Repeats",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Conduct in concert with participants repeats over time.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::temporal_ltl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Participants engage in conduct in concert.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Organisation is taken for purposes of sections 45D, 45DA and 45DB."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45dc-logic-argumentation-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Argumentation"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Implication",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Engagement in conduct in concert implies organisation's involvement.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::argumentation",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Participants engage in conduct in concert.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Organisation is taken for purposes of sections 45D, 45DA and 45DB."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45dd",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "45DD Situations in which boycotts permitted",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-45dd"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.315",
      "values:originalText": "Dominant purpose of conduct relates to employment matters—\nconduct by a person\n\n(1) A person does not contravene, and is not involved in a\ncontravention of, subsection 45D(1), 45DA(1) or 45DB(1) by\nengaging in conduct if the dominant purpose for which the conduct\nis engaged in is substantially related to the remuneration,\nconditions of employment, hours of work or working conditions of\nthat person or of another person employed by an employer of that\nperson.\n\nChapter 3  Restrictive trade practices",
      "skos:definition": "Dominant purpose of conduct relates to employment matters—\nconduct by a person\n\n(1) A person does not contravene, and is not involved in a\ncontravention of, subsection 45D(1), 45DA(1) or 45DB(1) by\nengaging in conduct if the dominant purpose for which the conduct\nis engaged in is substantially related to the remuneration,\nconditions of employment, hours of work or working conditions of\nthat person or of another person employed by an employer of that\nperson.\n\nChapter 3  Restrictive trade practices",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45dd-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45dd-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b3c254a19b692c8b918b1dba04b978c13ab324a0ddddd84cb787357f7fdba46f",
      "skos:note": "Boycotts permitted if dominant purpose is related to employment matters"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-45dd",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "45DD Situations in which boycotts permitted",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 315,
      "values:originalText": "Dominant purpose of conduct relates to employment matters—\nconduct by a person\n\n(1) A person does not contravene, and is not involved in a\ncontravention of, subsection 45D(1), 45DA(1) or 45DB(1) by\nengaging in conduct if the dominant purpose for which the conduct\nis engaged in is substantially related to the remuneration,\nconditions of employment, hours of work or working conditions of\nthat person or of another person employed by an employer of that\nperson.\n\nChapter 3  Restrictive trade practices"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45dd-norm",
      "@type": "values:Permission",
