    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-46",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "46 Misuse of market power",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-46"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.323",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A corporation that has a substantial degree of power in a market\nmust not engage in conduct that has the purpose, or has or is likely\nto have the effect, of substantially lessening competition in:\n\n(a) that market; or\n\n(b) any other market in which that corporation, or a body\ncorporate that is related to that corporation:\n\n(i) supplies goods or services, or is likely to supply goods\nor services; or\n\n(ii) supplies goods or services, or is likely to supply goods\nor services, indirectly through one or more other\npersons; or\n\n(c) any other market in which that corporation, or a body\ncorporate that is related to that corporation:\n\n(i) acquires goods or services, or is likely to acquire goods\nor services; or\n\n(ii) acquires goods or services, or is likely to acquire goods\nor services, indirectly through one or more other\npersons.\n\nChapter 3  Restrictive trade practices",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A corporation that has a substantial degree of power in a market\nmust not engage in conduct that has the purpose, or has or is likely\nto have the effect, of substantially lessening competition in:\n\n(a) that market; or\n\n(b) any other market in which that corporation, or a body\ncorporate that is related to that corporation:\n\n(i) supplies goods or services, or is likely to supply goods\nor services; or\n\n(ii) supplies goods or services, or is likely to supply goods\nor services, indirectly through one or more other\npersons; or\n\n(c) any other market in which that corporation, or a body\ncorporate that is related to that corporation:\n\n(i) acquires goods or services, or is likely to acquire goods\nor services; or\n\n(ii) acquires goods or services, or is likely to acquire goods\nor services, indirectly through one or more other\npersons.\n\nChapter 3  Restrictive trade practices",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-46-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-46-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-46-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-46-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-46-logic-diffusion-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-46-logic-cogai-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "91f8338dc990c70b04750956c17fd32b7a32dc3ebb1266d8ea410a69481c1958",
      "skos:note": "Must not engage in conduct that has the purpose or effect of substantially lessening competition."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-46",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "46 Misuse of market power",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 323,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A corporation that has a substantial degree of power in a market\nmust not engage in conduct that has the purpose, or has or is likely\nto have the effect, of substantially lessening competition in:\n\n(a) that market; or\n\n(b) any other market in which that corporation, or a body\ncorporate that is related to that corporation:\n\n(i) supplies goods or services, or is likely to supply goods\nor services; or\n\n(ii) supplies goods or services, or is likely to supply goods\nor services, indirectly through one or more other\npersons; or\n\n(c) any other market in which that corporation, or a body\ncorporate that is related to that corporation:\n\n(i) acquires goods or services, or is likely to acquire goods\nor services; or\n\n(ii) acquires goods or services, or is likely to acquire goods\nor services, indirectly through one or more other\npersons.\n\nChapter 3  Restrictive trade practices"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-46-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-46"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-46-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Must not engage in conduct.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(1) A corporation that has a substantial degree of power in a market must not...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...must not engage in conduct that has the purpose or effect of substantially lessening competition."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-46-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Temporal relation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Relates to temporal interval of prohibition.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(1) A corporation that has a substantial degree of power in a market must not...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...must not engage in conduct for the duration of the prohibition."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-46-logic-ltl-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LTL"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Recurring trace",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Relates to recurring traces of prohibited conduct.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::temporal_ltl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(1) A corporation that has a substantial degree of power in a market must not...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...must not engage in conduct with a recurring pattern."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-46-logic-diffusion-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Diffusion"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Diffusion",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Relates to diffusion of prohibited information.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::diffusion",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(1) A corporation that has a substantial degree of power in a market must not...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...must not engage in conduct that diffuses prohibited information."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-46-logic-cogai-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:CogAI"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Knowledge representation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Relates to knowledge representation of prohibited conduct.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "sparql_library::parsers::chk_parser",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(1) A corporation that has a substantial degree of power in a market must not...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...must not engage in conduct that is represented as prohibited."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-46a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "46A Misuse of market power—corporation with substantial degree",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-46a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.325",
      "values:originalText": "of power in trans-Tasman market\n\n(1) In this section:\nconduct, in relation to a market, means conduct in the market\neither as a supplier or acquirer of goods or services in the market.\nimpact market means a market in Australia that is not a market\nexclusively for services.\nmarket power, in relation to a market, means market power in the\nmarket either as a supplier or acquirer of goods or services in the\nmarket.\ntrans-Tasman market means a market in Australia, New Zealand\nor Australia and New Zealand for goods or services.\n\nChapter 3  Restrictive trade practices",
      "skos:definition": "of power in trans-Tasman market\n\n(1) In this section:\nconduct, in relation to a market, means conduct in the market\neither as a supplier or acquirer of goods or services in the market.\nimpact market means a market in Australia that is not a market\nexclusively for services.\nmarket power, in relation to a market, means market power in the\nmarket either as a supplier or acquirer of goods or services in the\nmarket.\ntrans-Tasman market means a market in Australia, New Zealand\nor Australia and New Zealand for goods or services.\n\nChapter 3  Restrictive trade practices",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-46a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-46a-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-46a-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-46a-logic-alleninterval-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-46a-logic-argumentation-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-46a-logic-diffusion-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-46a-logic-cogai-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "acdb392f71d41724e2e79b2e6d4c1607d6ad4949fd24e13be4f6be964c69c733",
      "skos:note": "Prohibition on misuse of market power by corporations with substantial degree"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-46a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "46A Misuse of market power—corporation with substantial degree",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 325,
      "values:originalText": "of power in trans-Tasman market\n\n(1) In this section:\nconduct, in relation to a market, means conduct in the market\neither as a supplier or acquirer of goods or services in the market.\nimpact market means a market in Australia that is not a market\nexclusively for services.\nmarket power, in relation to a market, means market power in the\nmarket either as a supplier or acquirer of goods or services in the\nmarket.\ntrans-Tasman market means a market in Australia, New Zealand\nor Australia and New Zealand for goods or services.\n\nChapter 3  Restrictive trade practices"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-46a-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-46a"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-46a-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits misuse of market power",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Market power must not be used for personal gain",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Corporations with substantial degree must not engage in such conduct"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-46a-logic-descriptionlogic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:DescriptionLogic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Classify",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Classifies market power as a key concept",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::dl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Market power is a critical aspect of the trans-Tasman market",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The definition of market power must be clearly understood"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-46a-logic-alleninterval-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Temporal",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Defines temporal scope for market power",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Market power is only applicable within the trans-Tasman market",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The duration of market power must be clearly defined"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-46a-logic-argumentation-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Argumentation"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Imply",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Implies a causal relationship between market power and conduct",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::argumentation",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Market power can lead to conduct that harms others",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The use of market power must be carefully considered"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-46a-logic-diffusion-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Diffusion"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Spread",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Spreads the concept of market power throughout the trans-Tasman market",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::diffusion",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Market power is a key concept that affects multiple stakeholders",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The definition of market power must be widely understood"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-46a-logic-cogai-6",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:CogAI"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Recognize",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Recognizes the importance of artificial intelligence in understanding market power",
      "cml:executionSurface": "sparql_library::parsers::chk_parser",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Artificial intelligence can help analyze market power data",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The use of AI must be considered when evaluating market power"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-46b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "46B No immunity from jurisdiction in relation to certain New",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-46b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.328",
      "values:originalText": "Zealand laws\n\n(1) It is hereby declared, for the avoidance of doubt, that the\nCommonwealth, the States, the Australian Capital Territory and the\nNorthern Territory, and their authorities, are not immune, and may\nnot claim immunity, from the jurisdiction of the courts of Australia\nand New Zealand in relation to matters arising under sections 36A,\n98H and 99A of the Commerce Act 1986 of New Zealand.\n\n(2) This section applies in and outside Australia.",
      "skos:definition": "Zealand laws\n\n(1) It is hereby declared, for the avoidance of doubt, that the\nCommonwealth, the States, the Australian Capital Territory and the\nNorthern Territory, and their authorities, are not immune, and may\nnot claim immunity, from the jurisdiction of the courts of Australia\nand New Zealand in relation to matters arising under sections 36A,\n98H and 99A of the Commerce Act 1986 of New Zealand.\n\n(2) This section applies in and outside Australia.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-46b-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-46b-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3c6b9abe2c2741f1140cb79260703dd62c28a7de8196c74ff99ec20f31ffa0bb"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-46b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "46B No immunity from jurisdiction in relation to certain New",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 328,
      "values:originalText": "Zealand laws\n\n(1) It is hereby declared, for the avoidance of doubt, that the\nCommonwealth, the States, the Australian Capital Territory and the\nNorthern Territory, and their authorities, are not immune, and may\nnot claim immunity, from the jurisdiction of the courts of Australia\nand New Zealand in relation to matters arising under sections 36A,\n98H and 99A of the Commerce Act 1986 of New Zealand.\n\n(2) This section applies in and outside Australia."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-46b-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "46B(1) No immunity from jurisdiction in relation to certain New",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-46b-ss-1"
      },
