    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-51",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "51 Exceptions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-51"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.341",
      "values:originalText": "(1) In deciding whether a person has contravened this Part, the\nfollowing must be disregarded:\n\n(a) anything specified in, and specifically authorised by:\n\n(i) an Act (not including an Act relating to patents, trade\nmarks, designs or copyrights); or\n\n(ii) regulations made under such an Act;\n\n(b) anything done in a State, if the thing is specified in, and\nspecifically authorised by:\n\n(i) an Act passed by the Parliament of that State; or\n\nChapter 3  Restrictive trade practices",
      "skos:definition": "(1) In deciding whether a person has contravened this Part, the\nfollowing must be disregarded:\n\n(a) anything specified in, and specifically authorised by:\n\n(i) an Act (not including an Act relating to patents, trade\nmarks, designs or copyrights); or\n\n(ii) regulations made under such an Act;\n\n(b) anything done in a State, if the thing is specified in, and\nspecifically authorised by:\n\n(i) an Act passed by the Parliament of that State; or\n\nChapter 3  Restrictive trade practices",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-51-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "05dce85adbeabafed69d8269cd87178f10cacc2547041ab6de3583342afed091",
      "skos:note": "Exceptions from contravention of Part 51"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-51",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "51 Exceptions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 341,
      "values:originalText": "(1) In deciding whether a person has contravened this Part, the\nfollowing must be disregarded:\n\n(a) anything specified in, and specifically authorised by:\n\n(i) an Act (not including an Act relating to patents, trade\nmarks, designs or copyrights); or\n\n(ii) regulations made under such an Act;\n\n(b) anything done in a State, if the thing is specified in, and\nspecifically authorised by:\n\n(i) an Act passed by the Parliament of that State; or\n\nChapter 3  Restrictive trade practices"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-51-norm",
