          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52e-ss-3-logic-diffusion-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6c974fd62b655cfa30c0045623ffb445b8a03c576ebc8c1b8c78258ebaea6c65",
      "skos:note": "Minister must consider significant bargaining power imbalance and contribution to news industry sustainability when making designation determination."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-52e-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "52E(3) Minister may make designation determination",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 451,
      "values:originalText": "(3) In making the determination, the Minister must consider:\n\n(a) whether there is a significant bargaining power imbalance\nbetween Australian news businesses and the group comprised\nof the corporation and all of its related bodies corporate; and\n\n(b) whether that group has made a significant contribution to the\nsustainability of the Australian news industry through\nagreements relating to news content of Australian news\nbusinesses (including agreements to remunerate those\nbusinesses for their news content)."
    },
