    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52h-ss-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "52H(6) Revocation of registration or endorsement—general",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-52h-ss-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.454",
      "values:originalText": "(6) The ACMA may revoke the endorsement of a registered news\nbusiness corporation as the registered news business corporation\nfor a registered news business if the ACMA considers that the\ncorporation does not meet the requirement in section 52L\n(connection between corporation and news business) in relation to\nthe registered news business.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.\nPart IVBA  News media and digital platforms mandatory bargaining code",
      "skos:definition": "(6) The ACMA may revoke the endorsement of a registered news\nbusiness corporation as the registered news business corporation\nfor a registered news business if the ACMA considers that the\ncorporation does not meet the requirement in section 52L\n(connection between corporation and news business) in relation to\nthe registered news business.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.\nPart IVBA  News media and digital platforms mandatory bargaining code",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52h"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
