      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.456",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The registered news business corporation for a registered news\nbusiness must notify the ACMA, as soon as practicable, if any of\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nNews media and digital platforms mandatory bargaining code  Part IVBA\nRegistered news businesses and registered news business corporations  Division 3\n\nSection 52K\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nthe following requirements are no longer met in relation to the\nregistered news business corporation or the registered news\nbusiness:\n\n(a) the requirement in subsection 52N(1) (the content test);\n\n(b) the requirement in subsection 52O(1) (the Australian\naudience test);\n\n(c) the requirement in subsection 52P(1) (the professional\nstandards test);\n\n(d) the requirement in subsection 52M(1) (the revenue test);\n\n(e) the requirement in section 52L (connection between\ncorporation and news business).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The registered news business corporation for a registered news\nbusiness must notify the ACMA, as soon as practicable, if any of\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nNews media and digital platforms mandatory bargaining code  Part IVBA\nRegistered news businesses and registered news business corporations  Division 3\n\nSection 52K\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nthe following requirements are no longer met in relation to the\nregistered news business corporation or the registered news\nbusiness:\n\n(a) the requirement in subsection 52N(1) (the content test);\n\n(b) the requirement in subsection 52O(1) (the Australian\naudience test);\n\n(c) the requirement in subsection 52P(1) (the professional\nstandards test);\n\n(d) the requirement in subsection 52M(1) (the revenue test);\n\n(e) the requirement in section 52L (connection between\ncorporation and news business).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52j"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52j-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52j-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bbcb31d3b30261a758910f07c5d20c9875f559f295d70c5a85ba7bb3884a1eb3",
      "skos:note": "Registered news business corporation must notify ACMA if requirements are no longer met."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-52j-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "52J(1) Obligation on registered news business corporation to notify",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 456,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The registered news business corporation for a registered news\nbusiness must notify the ACMA, as soon as practicable, if any of\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nNews media and digital platforms mandatory bargaining code  Part IVBA\nRegistered news businesses and registered news business corporations  Division 3\n\nSection 52K\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nthe following requirements are no longer met in relation to the\nregistered news business corporation or the registered news\nbusiness:\n\n(a) the requirement in subsection 52N(1) (the content test);\n\n(b) the requirement in subsection 52O(1) (the Australian\naudience test);\n\n(c) the requirement in subsection 52P(1) (the professional\nstandards test);\n\n(d) the requirement in subsection 52M(1) (the revenue test);\n\n(e) the requirement in section 52L (connection between\ncorporation and news business)."
    },
