    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52n",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "52N Content test",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-52n"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.459",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The requirement in this subsection is met in relation to a news\nbusiness if the primary purpose of each news source covered by\nsubsection (2) is to create content that is core news content.\n\n(2) This subsection covers a news source if it comprises, whether by\nitself or together with other news sources, the news business.\n\n(3) For the purposes of subsection (1), in determining whether the\nprimary purpose of a news source is to create content that is core\nnews content, take into account the following matters:\n\n(a) the amount of core news content created by the news source;\n\n(b) the frequency with which the news source creates core news\ncontent;\n\n(c) the degree of prominence given to core news content created\nby the news source, compared with the degree of prominence\ngiven to other content created by the news source;\n\n(d) any other relevant matter.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The requirement in this subsection is met in relation to a news\nbusiness if the primary purpose of each news source covered by\nsubsection (2) is to create content that is core news content.\n\n(2) This subsection covers a news source if it comprises, whether by\nitself or together with other news sources, the news business.\n\n(3) For the purposes of subsection (1), in determining whether the\nprimary purpose of a news source is to create content that is core\nnews content, take into account the following matters:\n\n(a) the amount of core news content created by the news source;\n\n(b) the frequency with which the news source creates core news\ncontent;\n\n(c) the degree of prominence given to core news content created\nby the news source, compared with the degree of prominence\ngiven to other content created by the news source;\n\n(d) any other relevant matter.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52n-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52n-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52n-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "780eca1f6127d3429d5e780c470111b4ac9da93ffa5e4195cd5ac90a756de955"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-52n",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "52N Content test",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 459,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The requirement in this subsection is met in relation to a news\nbusiness if the primary purpose of each news source covered by\nsubsection (2) is to create content that is core news content.\n\n(2) This subsection covers a news source if it comprises, whether by\nitself or together with other news sources, the news business.\n\n(3) For the purposes of subsection (1), in determining whether the\nprimary purpose of a news source is to create content that is core\nnews content, take into account the following matters:\n\n(a) the amount of core news content created by the news source;\n\n(b) the frequency with which the news source creates core news\ncontent;\n\n(c) the degree of prominence given to core news content created\nby the news source, compared with the degree of prominence\ngiven to other content created by the news source;\n\n(d) any other relevant matter."
    },
