    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52r",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "52R Giving list and explanation of data provided to registered news",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-52r"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.461",
      "values:originalText": "businesses\n\n(1) If the designated digital platform service makes available covered\nnews content of the registered news business, the responsible\ndigital platform corporation for the designated digital platform\nservice must ensure that:\n\n(a) information covered by subsection (2) is given to the\nregistered news business corporation for the registered news\nbusiness; and\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.\nPart IVBA  News media and digital platforms mandatory bargaining code",
      "skos:definition": "businesses\n\n(1) If the designated digital platform service makes available covered\nnews content of the registered news business, the responsible\ndigital platform corporation for the designated digital platform\nservice must ensure that:\n\n(a) information covered by subsection (2) is given to the\nregistered news business corporation for the registered news\nbusiness; and\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.\nPart IVBA  News media and digital platforms mandatory bargaining code",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52r-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52r-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a03229dd77935dea7eec2cf332249939d0dd62f630a4246a0e5e7ad15f63a45d",
      "skos:note": "Digital platform corporation must provide information to registered news business",
      "dc:description": "information covered by subsection (2)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-52r",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "52R Giving list and explanation of data provided to registered news",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 461,
      "values:originalText": "businesses\n\n(1) If the designated digital platform service makes available covered\nnews content of the registered news business, the responsible\ndigital platform corporation for the designated digital platform\nservice must ensure that:\n\n(a) information covered by subsection (2) is given to the\nregistered news business corporation for the registered news\nbusiness; and\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.\nPart IVBA  News media and digital platforms mandatory bargaining code"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52r-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52r"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52r-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Digital platform corporation must provide information",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52s",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "52S Change to algorithm to bring about identified alteration to",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-52s"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.463",
      "values:originalText": "distribution of content with significant effect on referral\ntraffic\n\n(1) Subsection (2) applies if:\n\n(a) a change is planned to be made to an algorithm of the\ndesignated digital platform service; and\n\n(b) the dominant purpose of the change is to bring about an\nidentified alteration to the ways in which the designated\ndigital platform service distributes content that is made\navailable by the service; and\n\n(c) the change is likely to have a significant effect on the referral\ntraffic from the designated digital platform service to the\ncovered news content of registered news businesses\n(considered as a whole) that the service makes available.\n\n(2) The responsible digital platform corporation for the designated\ndigital platform service must ensure that:\n\n(a) notice of the change is given to the registered news business\ncorporation for each registered news business; and\n\n(b) the notice is given:\n\n(i) unless subparagraph (ii) applies—at least 14 days before\nthe change is made; or\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.\nPart IVBA  News media and digital platforms mandatory bargaining code",
      "skos:definition": "distribution of content with significant effect on referral\ntraffic\n\n(1) Subsection (2) applies if:\n\n(a) a change is planned to be made to an algorithm of the\ndesignated digital platform service; and\n\n(b) the dominant purpose of the change is to bring about an\nidentified alteration to the ways in which the designated\ndigital platform service distributes content that is made\navailable by the service; and\n\n(c) the change is likely to have a significant effect on the referral\ntraffic from the designated digital platform service to the\ncovered news content of registered news businesses\n(considered as a whole) that the service makes available.\n\n(2) The responsible digital platform corporation for the designated\ndigital platform service must ensure that:\n\n(a) notice of the change is given to the registered news business\ncorporation for each registered news business; and\n\n(b) the notice is given:\n\n(i) unless subparagraph (ii) applies—at least 14 days before\nthe change is made; or\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.\nPart IVBA  News media and digital platforms mandatory bargaining code",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52s-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52s-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "069eea1ddc1e3ba3b0f865730e84810ed14258f91f35089e9bad1b2a6d0f16a5"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-52s",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "52S Change to algorithm to bring about identified alteration to",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 463,
      "values:originalText": "distribution of content with significant effect on referral\ntraffic\n\n(1) Subsection (2) applies if:\n\n(a) a change is planned to be made to an algorithm of the\ndesignated digital platform service; and\n\n(b) the dominant purpose of the change is to bring about an\nidentified alteration to the ways in which the designated\ndigital platform service distributes content that is made\navailable by the service; and\n\n(c) the change is likely to have a significant effect on the referral\ntraffic from the designated digital platform service to the\ncovered news content of registered news businesses\n(considered as a whole) that the service makes available.\n\n(2) The responsible digital platform corporation for the designated\ndigital platform service must ensure that:\n\n(a) notice of the change is given to the registered news business\ncorporation for each registered news business; and\n\n(b) the notice is given:\n\n(i) unless subparagraph (ii) applies—at least 14 days before\nthe change is made; or\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.\nPart IVBA  News media and digital platforms mandatory bargaining code"
    },
