        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Digital platform corporation must ensure notice is given",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Registered news business corporation must receive notice"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52v",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "52V Section 52S—dominant purpose",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-52v"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.464",
      "values:originalText": "For the purposes of paragraph 52S(1)(b), treat a change as not\nhaving the dominant purpose mentioned in that paragraph if the\nchange is any of the following:\n\n(a) a change to an algorithm made as part of routine maintenance\nwith the dominant purpose of ensuring the ongoing\neffectiveness of the algorithm;\n\n(b) a change to an algorithm with the dominant purpose of\nensuring that the algorithm operates more quickly or more\nefficiently.",
      "skos:definition": "For the purposes of paragraph 52S(1)(b), treat a change as not\nhaving the dominant purpose mentioned in that paragraph if the\nchange is any of the following:\n\n(a) a change to an algorithm made as part of routine maintenance\nwith the dominant purpose of ensuring the ongoing\neffectiveness of the algorithm;\n\n(b) a change to an algorithm with the dominant purpose of\nensuring that the algorithm operates more quickly or more\nefficiently.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52v-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "12c8b5eff92043c423598ee9946a036960f5214cf75dfb031032ff51503f1b44",
      "skos:note": "Exemptions from dominant purpose test"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-52v",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "52V Section 52S—dominant purpose",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 464,
      "values:originalText": "For the purposes of paragraph 52S(1)(b), treat a change as not\nhaving the dominant purpose mentioned in that paragraph if the\nchange is any of the following:\n\n(a) a change to an algorithm made as part of routine maintenance\nwith the dominant purpose of ensuring the ongoing\neffectiveness of the algorithm;\n\n(b) a change to an algorithm with the dominant purpose of\nensuring that the algorithm operates more quickly or more\nefficiently."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52v-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52v"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52w",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "52W Section 52S—significant effect",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-52w"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.464",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of paragraph 52S(1)(c), in determining whether\nthe change is likely to have the significant effect mentioned in the\nparagraph, take into account the following matters:\n\n(a) whether, as a result of the change, there is likely to be a\nsignificant variation to the amount of covered news content\nmade available by the designated digital platform service;\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nNews media and digital platforms mandatory bargaining code  Part IVBA\nGeneral requirements  Division 4\n\nSection 52X\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(b) whether, as a result of the change, there is likely to be a\nsignificant variation to the proportion of content made\navailable by the designated digital platform service\nrepresented by covered news content;\n\n(c) any other relevant matter (subject to subsection (2)).\n\n(2) For the purposes of paragraph 52S(1)(c), in determining whether\nthe change is likely to have the significant effect mentioned in the\nparagraph, disregard the following matters:\n\n(a) whether, as a result of the change, there is likely to be a\nsignificant variation to the proportion of covered news\ncontent of all registered news businesses made available by\nthe designated digital platform service represented by the\ncovered news content of a particular registered news\nbusiness;\n\n(b) the relative turnover of registered news businesses whose\ncovered news content is made available by the designated\ndigital platform service;\n\n(c) the relative volume of covered news content created by\nregistered news businesses whose covered news content is\nmade available by the designated digital platform service;\n\n(d) the relative financial position of registered news businesses\nwhose covered news content is made available by the\ndesignated digital platform service.\nSubdivision C—Recognition of original covered news content",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of paragraph 52S(1)(c), in determining whether\nthe change is likely to have the significant effect mentioned in the\nparagraph, take into account the following matters:\n\n(a) whether, as a result of the change, there is likely to be a\nsignificant variation to the amount of covered news content\nmade available by the designated digital platform service;\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nNews media and digital platforms mandatory bargaining code  Part IVBA\nGeneral requirements  Division 4\n\nSection 52X\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(b) whether, as a result of the change, there is likely to be a\nsignificant variation to the proportion of content made\navailable by the designated digital platform service\nrepresented by covered news content;\n\n(c) any other relevant matter (subject to subsection (2)).\n\n(2) For the purposes of paragraph 52S(1)(c), in determining whether\nthe change is likely to have the significant effect mentioned in the\nparagraph, disregard the following matters:\n\n(a) whether, as a result of the change, there is likely to be a\nsignificant variation to the proportion of covered news\ncontent of all registered news businesses made available by\nthe designated digital platform service represented by the\ncovered news content of a particular registered news\nbusiness;\n\n(b) the relative turnover of registered news businesses whose\ncovered news content is made available by the designated\ndigital platform service;\n\n(c) the relative volume of covered news content created by\nregistered news businesses whose covered news content is\nmade available by the designated digital platform service;\n\n(d) the relative financial position of registered news businesses\nwhose covered news content is made available by the\ndesignated digital platform service.\nSubdivision C—Recognition of original covered news content",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52w-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52w-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "82ea8415f7a3a3587f3b2fc7c42c2c15168633f1e630ede5579c6fa6c9175b87"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-52w",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "52W Section 52S—significant effect",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 464,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of paragraph 52S(1)(c), in determining whether\nthe change is likely to have the significant effect mentioned in the\nparagraph, take into account the following matters:\n\n(a) whether, as a result of the change, there is likely to be a\nsignificant variation to the amount of covered news content\nmade available by the designated digital platform service;\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nNews media and digital platforms mandatory bargaining code  Part IVBA\nGeneral requirements  Division 4\n\nSection 52X\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(b) whether, as a result of the change, there is likely to be a\nsignificant variation to the proportion of content made\navailable by the designated digital platform service\nrepresented by covered news content;\n\n(c) any other relevant matter (subject to subsection (2)).\n\n(2) For the purposes of paragraph 52S(1)(c), in determining whether\nthe change is likely to have the significant effect mentioned in the\nparagraph, disregard the following matters:\n\n(a) whether, as a result of the change, there is likely to be a\nsignificant variation to the proportion of covered news\ncontent of all registered news businesses made available by\nthe designated digital platform service represented by the\ncovered news content of a particular registered news\nbusiness;\n\n(b) the relative turnover of registered news businesses whose\ncovered news content is made available by the designated\ndigital platform service;\n\n(c) the relative volume of covered news content created by\nregistered news businesses whose covered news content is\nmade available by the designated digital platform service;\n\n(d) the relative financial position of registered news businesses\nwhose covered news content is made available by the\ndesignated digital platform service.\nSubdivision C—Recognition of original covered news content"
    },
