    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52x",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "52X Recognition of original covered news content",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-52x"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.465",
      "values:originalText": "The responsible digital platform corporation for the designated\ndigital platform service must ensure that:\n\n(a) a proposal is developed for the designated digital platform\nservice to recognise original covered news content when it\nmakes available and distributes that content; and\n\n(b) registered news business corporations are consulted in\ndeveloping that proposal before it is published; and\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.\nPart IVBA  News media and digital platforms mandatory bargaining code",
      "skos:definition": "The responsible digital platform corporation for the designated\ndigital platform service must ensure that:\n\n(a) a proposal is developed for the designated digital platform\nservice to recognise original covered news content when it\nmakes available and distributes that content; and\n\n(b) registered news business corporations are consulted in\ndeveloping that proposal before it is published; and\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.\nPart IVBA  News media and digital platforms mandatory bargaining code",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52x-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52x-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f165ae3d705568d11b8fc3aaf2959311b2d27930c80f8e31d334de22b6e56a62",
      "skos:note": "Digital platform corporation must develop proposal for recognizing original covered news content."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-52x",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "52X Recognition of original covered news content",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 465,
      "values:originalText": "The responsible digital platform corporation for the designated\ndigital platform service must ensure that:\n\n(a) a proposal is developed for the designated digital platform\nservice to recognise original covered news content when it\nmakes available and distributes that content; and\n\n(b) registered news business corporations are consulted in\ndeveloping that proposal before it is published; and\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.\nPart IVBA  News media and digital platforms mandatory bargaining code"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52x-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52x"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52x-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to develop proposal",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52y",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "52Y Facilitating open communication—responsible digital platform",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-52y"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.466",
      "values:originalText": "corporation for designated digital platform service\n\nThe responsible digital platform corporation for a designated\ndigital platform service must:\n\n(a) set up a point of contact in Australia for the purpose of this\nsection no later than 28 days after the Minister makes a\ndetermination under section 52E specifying the designated\ndigital platform corporation; and\n\n(b) if regulations made for the purposes of this paragraph specify\nrequirements for the point of contact—ensure that the point\nof contact meets those requirements; and\n\n(c) give details of that point of contact to every registered news\nbusiness corporation:\n\n(i) unless subparagraph (ii) applies—no later than 10\nbusiness days after the responsible digital platform\ncorporation sets up the point of contact; or\n\n(ii) if the registered news business corporation is registered\nunder section 52G after the responsible digital platform\ncorporation sets up the point of contact—no later than\n10 business days after the registered news business\ncorporation is registered under section 52G; and\n\n(d) acknowledge every communication to that point of contact\nfrom a registered news business corporation for a registered\nnews business that relates to the registered news business’\ncovered news content made available by the designated\ndigital platform service; and\n\n(e) if regulations made for the purposes of this paragraph specify\nrequirements for the acknowledgement—ensure that the\nacknowledgement meets those requirements.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nNews media and digital platforms mandatory bargaining code  Part IVBA\nGeneral requirements  Division 4\n\nSection 52Z\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "skos:definition": "corporation for designated digital platform service\n\nThe responsible digital platform corporation for a designated\ndigital platform service must:\n\n(a) set up a point of contact in Australia for the purpose of this\nsection no later than 28 days after the Minister makes a\ndetermination under section 52E specifying the designated\ndigital platform corporation; and\n\n(b) if regulations made for the purposes of this paragraph specify\nrequirements for the point of contact—ensure that the point\nof contact meets those requirements; and\n\n(c) give details of that point of contact to every registered news\nbusiness corporation:\n\n(i) unless subparagraph (ii) applies—no later than 10\nbusiness days after the responsible digital platform\ncorporation sets up the point of contact; or\n\n(ii) if the registered news business corporation is registered\nunder section 52G after the responsible digital platform\ncorporation sets up the point of contact—no later than\n10 business days after the registered news business\ncorporation is registered under section 52G; and\n\n(d) acknowledge every communication to that point of contact\nfrom a registered news business corporation for a registered\nnews business that relates to the registered news business’\ncovered news content made available by the designated\ndigital platform service; and\n\n(e) if regulations made for the purposes of this paragraph specify\nrequirements for the acknowledgement—ensure that the\nacknowledgement meets those requirements.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nNews media and digital platforms mandatory bargaining code  Part IVBA\nGeneral requirements  Division 4\n\nSection 52Z\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52y-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52y-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "da3ea874c6fcfc0647c03846fa2a2c5f2a99f9f94eb16321e9885a6e929e293a",
      "skos:note": "Responsible digital platform corporation must set up a point of contact and acknowledge communications.",
      "dc:description": "Details of the point of contact, acknowledgement of communications"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-52y",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "52Y Facilitating open communication—responsible digital platform",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 466,
      "values:originalText": "corporation for designated digital platform service\n\nThe responsible digital platform corporation for a designated\ndigital platform service must:\n\n(a) set up a point of contact in Australia for the purpose of this\nsection no later than 28 days after the Minister makes a\ndetermination under section 52E specifying the designated\ndigital platform corporation; and\n\n(b) if regulations made for the purposes of this paragraph specify\nrequirements for the point of contact—ensure that the point\nof contact meets those requirements; and\n\n(c) give details of that point of contact to every registered news\nbusiness corporation:\n\n(i) unless subparagraph (ii) applies—no later than 10\nbusiness days after the responsible digital platform\ncorporation sets up the point of contact; or\n\n(ii) if the registered news business corporation is registered\nunder section 52G after the responsible digital platform\ncorporation sets up the point of contact—no later than\n10 business days after the registered news business\ncorporation is registered under section 52G; and\n\n(d) acknowledge every communication to that point of contact\nfrom a registered news business corporation for a registered\nnews business that relates to the registered news business’\ncovered news content made available by the designated\ndigital platform service; and\n\n(e) if regulations made for the purposes of this paragraph specify\nrequirements for the acknowledgement—ensure that the\nacknowledgement meets those requirements.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nNews media and digital platforms mandatory bargaining code  Part IVBA\nGeneral requirements  Division 4\n\nSection 52Z\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026"
    },
