    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52zk",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "52ZK Register of bargaining code arbitrators",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-52zk"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.477",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACMA must establish and keep a register of bargaining code\narbitrators.\n\n(2) Each such person listed on the register must be:\n\n(a) a person experienced in legal matters, economic matters or\nindustry matters; or\n\n(b) a person who the ACMA considers has appropriate\nexperience to be a member of an arbitral panel for the\npurposes of this Part.\n\n(3) In listing a person on the register, the ACMA must consider\nrequirements (if any) specified in regulations made for the\npurposes of this subsection.\nSubdivision B—Starting arbitration",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The ACMA must establish and keep a register of bargaining code\narbitrators.\n\n(2) Each such person listed on the register must be:\n\n(a) a person experienced in legal matters, economic matters or\nindustry matters; or\n\n(b) a person who the ACMA considers has appropriate\nexperience to be a member of an arbitral panel for the\npurposes of this Part.\n\n(3) In listing a person on the register, the ACMA must consider\nrequirements (if any) specified in regulations made for the\npurposes of this subsection.\nSubdivision B—Starting arbitration",
