    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52zl",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "52ZL Notification of arbitration",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-52zl"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.477",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a notification has been made for the purposes of\nsubsection 52ZE(1) to a responsible digital platform\ncorporation for a designated digital platform service; and\n\n(b) one of the core bargaining issues (the remuneration issue)\nconcerns the remuneration to be paid to a registered news\nbusiness for the making available of the registered news\nbusiness’ covered news content by the designated digital\nplatform service.\n\n(2) The bargaining party that is the bargaining news business\nrepresentative may give a notice to the Commission that arbitration\nabout the remuneration issue should start, if:\n\n(a) both of the following conditions are satisfied:\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.\nPart IVBA  News media and digital platforms mandatory bargaining code",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a notification has been made for the purposes of\nsubsection 52ZE(1) to a responsible digital platform\ncorporation for a designated digital platform service; and\n\n(b) one of the core bargaining issues (the remuneration issue)\nconcerns the remuneration to be paid to a registered news\nbusiness for the making available of the registered news\nbusiness’ covered news content by the designated digital\nplatform service.\n\n(2) The bargaining party that is the bargaining news business\nrepresentative may give a notice to the Commission that arbitration\nabout the remuneration issue should start, if:\n\n(a) both of the following conditions are satisfied:\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.\nPart IVBA  News media and digital platforms mandatory bargaining code",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52zl-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52zl-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f113d505f45d227feacd833861f04fe7f3c438600f0a9d63c8f8974fe3d39195"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-52zl",
