        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52zl-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1b0d70cba40e1b44a5a8e868a7e79a4215fd9dfadf0db1300832c42da67e068c",
      "skos:note": "Notification of arbitration required when conditions are met"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-52zl-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "52ZL(2) Notification of arbitration",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 477,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The bargaining party that is the bargaining news business\nrepresentative may give a notice to the Commission that arbitration\nabout the remuneration issue should start, if:\n\n(a) both of the following conditions are satisfied:\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.\nPart IVBA  News media and digital platforms mandatory bargaining code"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52zl-ss-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
