    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52zp",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "52ZP Chair to notify start of arbitration",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-52zp"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.481",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Chair must notify the bargaining parties that arbitration about\nterms for resolving the remuneration issue will start on a specified\nday that is no later than 5 business days (or, if the regulations\nspecify a different period, the end of that period) after the\nappointment of the Chair.\n\n(2) The notice must:\n\n(a) be in writing; and\n\n(b) if regulations made for the purposes of this paragraph specify\nrequirements—meet those requirements.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Chair must notify the bargaining parties that arbitration about\nterms for resolving the remuneration issue will start on a specified\nday that is no later than 5 business days (or, if the regulations\nspecify a different period, the end of that period) after the\nappointment of the Chair.\n\n(2) The notice must:\n\n(a) be in writing; and\n\n(b) if regulations made for the purposes of this paragraph specify\nrequirements—meet those requirements.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52zp-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52zp-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f752ab4fa307cec728912b151e6103f2c664f92e984cd4ea16b1da9da9370c0b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-52zp",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "52ZP Chair to notify start of arbitration",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 481,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Chair must notify the bargaining parties that arbitration about\nterms for resolving the remuneration issue will start on a specified\nday that is no later than 5 business days (or, if the regulations\nspecify a different period, the end of that period) after the\nappointment of the Chair.\n\n(2) The notice must:\n\n(a) be in writing; and\n\n(b) if regulations made for the purposes of this paragraph specify\nrequirements—meet those requirements."
    },
