    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52zq",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "52ZQ Bargaining parties’ agreement about dealing with extra",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-52zq"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.481",
      "values:originalText": "services in arbitration\n\n(1) The bargaining parties may agree, in writing, that specified\nservices other than the designated digital platform service should\nbe dealt with in the arbitration.\n\n(2) If the bargaining parties notify the Chair of the agreement before\nthe start of the arbitration, Subdivision C applies as if:\n\n(a) the remuneration issue related to the designated digital\nplatform service and the specified services mentioned in\nsubsection (1); and\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.\nPart IVBA  News media and digital platforms mandatory bargaining code",
      "skos:definition": "services in arbitration\n\n(1) The bargaining parties may agree, in writing, that specified\nservices other than the designated digital platform service should\nbe dealt with in the arbitration.\n\n(2) If the bargaining parties notify the Chair of the agreement before\nthe start of the arbitration, Subdivision C applies as if:\n\n(a) the remuneration issue related to the designated digital\nplatform service and the specified services mentioned in\nsubsection (1); and\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.\nPart IVBA  News media and digital platforms mandatory bargaining code",
      "cml:hasPart": [
