      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52zu",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "52ZU Information request by bargaining party—challenges by",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-52zu"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.484",
      "values:originalText": "other bargaining party\n\n(1) The other bargaining party may apply to the panel, in writing, for a\nruling that it is not reasonable for the bargaining party to make the\nrequest for the purposes of this Division, in relation to all or a\nspecified part of the information requested.\n\n(2) An application under subsection (1) can be made no later than 10\nbusiness days after the bargaining party gives the request to the\nother bargaining party.\n\n(3) If an application is made under subsection (1), the panel must make\na ruling in relation to it no later than 10 business days after it is\nmade.\n\n(4) The ruling may relate to all or a specified part of the information\nrequested.\n\n(5) In making the ruling, the panel must consider the matters\nmentioned in subsection 52ZZ(1).\n\n(6) Nothing in section 52ZT requires the giving of information to the\nextent (if any) that the panel makes a ruling under subsection (3)\nthat it was not reasonable for the bargaining party to make the\nrequest for the purposes of this Division, in relation to all or a\nspecified part of the information requested.",
      "skos:definition": "other bargaining party\n\n(1) The other bargaining party may apply to the panel, in writing, for a\nruling that it is not reasonable for the bargaining party to make the\nrequest for the purposes of this Division, in relation to all or a\nspecified part of the information requested.\n\n(2) An application under subsection (1) can be made no later than 10\nbusiness days after the bargaining party gives the request to the\nother bargaining party.\n\n(3) If an application is made under subsection (1), the panel must make\na ruling in relation to it no later than 10 business days after it is\nmade.\n\n(4) The ruling may relate to all or a specified part of the information\nrequested.\n\n(5) In making the ruling, the panel must consider the matters\nmentioned in subsection 52ZZ(1).\n\n(6) Nothing in section 52ZT requires the giving of information to the\nextent (if any) that the panel makes a ruling under subsection (3)\nthat it was not reasonable for the bargaining party to make the\nrequest for the purposes of this Division, in relation to all or a\nspecified part of the information requested.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52zu-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52zu-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52zu-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52zu-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52zu-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52zu-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "50c9770c1c5c73cdce876ea8ac09fc6992d87d13b8b607d50a848eb98b400144"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-52zu",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "52ZU Information request by bargaining party—challenges by",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 484,
      "values:originalText": "other bargaining party\n\n(1) The other bargaining party may apply to the panel, in writing, for a\nruling that it is not reasonable for the bargaining party to make the\nrequest for the purposes of this Division, in relation to all or a\nspecified part of the information requested.\n\n(2) An application under subsection (1) can be made no later than 10\nbusiness days after the bargaining party gives the request to the\nother bargaining party.\n\n(3) If an application is made under subsection (1), the panel must make\na ruling in relation to it no later than 10 business days after it is\nmade.\n\n(4) The ruling may relate to all or a specified part of the information\nrequested.\n\n(5) In making the ruling, the panel must consider the matters\nmentioned in subsection 52ZZ(1).\n\n(6) Nothing in section 52ZT requires the giving of information to the\nextent (if any) that the panel makes a ruling under subsection (3)\nthat it was not reasonable for the bargaining party to make the\nrequest for the purposes of this Division, in relation to all or a\nspecified part of the information requested."
    },
