    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52zw",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "52ZW Agreed early termination of arbitration",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-52zw"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.485",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) the bargaining parties agree that the arbitration should\nterminate; and\n\n(b) the panel did not make a determination in accordance with\nsubsection 52ZX(1) before the agreement was made; and\n\n(c) no information was given by a bargaining party in order to\ncomply with a request made under subsection 52ZT(1) before\nthe agreement was made.\n\n(2) The parties must notify the Chair of the agreement as soon as\npracticable after the day on which the agreement is made.\n\n(3) The arbitration terminates in accordance with that agreement, but\nno earlier than the day on which parties notify the Chair of the\nagreement in accordance with subsection (2).\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.\nPart IVBA  News media and digital platforms mandatory bargaining code",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) the bargaining parties agree that the arbitration should\nterminate; and\n\n(b) the panel did not make a determination in accordance with\nsubsection 52ZX(1) before the agreement was made; and\n\n(c) no information was given by a bargaining party in order to\ncomply with a request made under subsection 52ZT(1) before\nthe agreement was made.\n\n(2) The parties must notify the Chair of the agreement as soon as\npracticable after the day on which the agreement is made.\n\n(3) The arbitration terminates in accordance with that agreement, but\nno earlier than the day on which parties notify the Chair of the\nagreement in accordance with subsection (2).\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.\nPart IVBA  News media and digital platforms mandatory bargaining code",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52zw-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52zw-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52zw-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f6cfe6d9073ec8a82b73faa0e84b567708496d6f9793ece78c16a622266dc019"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-52zw",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "52ZW Agreed early termination of arbitration",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 485,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) the bargaining parties agree that the arbitration should\nterminate; and\n\n(b) the panel did not make a determination in accordance with\nsubsection 52ZX(1) before the agreement was made; and\n\n(c) no information was given by a bargaining party in order to\ncomply with a request made under subsection 52ZT(1) before\nthe agreement was made.\n\n(2) The parties must notify the Chair of the agreement as soon as\npracticable after the day on which the agreement is made.\n\n(3) The arbitration terminates in accordance with that agreement, but\nno earlier than the day on which parties notify the Chair of the\nagreement in accordance with subsection (2).\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.\nPart IVBA  News media and digital platforms mandatory bargaining code"
    },
