    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52zx-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "52ZX(4) Final offer arbitration",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-52zx-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.486",
      "values:originalText": "(4) A final offer:\n\n(a) cannot be submitted later than the latest of the following:\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nNews media and digital platforms mandatory bargaining code  Part IVBA\nArbitration about remuneration issue  Division 7\n\nSection 52ZX\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(i) the end of the period of 10 business days after the day\non which the arbitration starts;\n\n(ii) if a bargaining party makes a request under\nsubsection 52ZT(1) (information requests)—the end of\nthe period of 10 business days after the latest day on\nwhich the other bargaining party may comply with the\nrequest in accordance with subsection 52ZT(5);\n\n(iii) if a bargaining party makes an application under\nsubsection 52ZU(1) (challenges to information\nrequests)—the end of the period of 10 business days\nafter the day on which the panel makes a ruling in\nrelation to the application under subsection 52ZU(3);\n\n(iv) if regulations made for the purposes of this\nsubparagraph specify a different period—the end of that\nperiod;\n\n(v) if the panel considers that exceptional circumstances\njustify a different period—the end of that period; and\n\n(b) cannot be more than 30 pages in length.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) A final offer:\n\n(a) cannot be submitted later than the latest of the following:\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nNews media and digital platforms mandatory bargaining code  Part IVBA\nArbitration about remuneration issue  Division 7\n\nSection 52ZX\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(i) the end of the period of 10 business days after the day\non which the arbitration starts;\n\n(ii) if a bargaining party makes a request under\nsubsection 52ZT(1) (information requests)—the end of\nthe period of 10 business days after the latest day on\nwhich the other bargaining party may comply with the\nrequest in accordance with subsection 52ZT(5);\n\n(iii) if a bargaining party makes an application under\nsubsection 52ZU(1) (challenges to information\nrequests)—the end of the period of 10 business days\nafter the day on which the panel makes a ruling in\nrelation to the application under subsection 52ZU(3);\n\n(iv) if regulations made for the purposes of this\nsubparagraph specify a different period—the end of that\nperiod;\n\n(v) if the panel considers that exceptional circumstances\njustify a different period—the end of that period; and\n\n(b) cannot be more than 30 pages in length.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52zx"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52zx-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52zx-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c7fbe8071f5af405eb5df3f9e0152bcf712608bf9f737d48b816ae15f3195108",
      "skos:note": "A final offer must be submitted within a certain timeframe."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-52zx-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "52ZX(4) Final offer arbitration",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 486,
      "values:originalText": "(4) A final offer:\n\n(a) cannot be submitted later than the latest of the following:\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nNews media and digital platforms mandatory bargaining code  Part IVBA\nArbitration about remuneration issue  Division 7\n\nSection 52ZX\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(i) the end of the period of 10 business days after the day\non which the arbitration starts;\n\n(ii) if a bargaining party makes a request under\nsubsection 52ZT(1) (information requests)—the end of\nthe period of 10 business days after the latest day on\nwhich the other bargaining party may comply with the\nrequest in accordance with subsection 52ZT(5);\n\n(iii) if a bargaining party makes an application under\nsubsection 52ZU(1) (challenges to information\nrequests)—the end of the period of 10 business days\nafter the day on which the panel makes a ruling in\nrelation to the application under subsection 52ZU(3);\n\n(iv) if regulations made for the purposes of this\nsubparagraph specify a different period—the end of that\nperiod;\n\n(v) if the panel considers that exceptional circumstances\njustify a different period—the end of that period; and\n\n(b) cannot be more than 30 pages in length."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52zx-ss-4-norm",
