    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52zx-ss-7",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "52ZX(7) Final offer arbitration",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-52zx-ss-7"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.486",
      "values:originalText": "(7) The panel must accept one of the final offers unless the panel\nconsiders that each final offer is not in the public interest because it\nis highly likely to result in serious detriment to:\n\n(a) the provision of covered news content in Australia; or\n\n(b) Australian consumers.",
      "skos:definition": "(7) The panel must accept one of the final offers unless the panel\nconsiders that each final offer is not in the public interest because it\nis highly likely to result in serious detriment to:\n\n(a) the provision of covered news content in Australia; or\n\n(b) Australian consumers.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52zx"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52zx-ss-7-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52zx-ss-7-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52zx-ss-7-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52zx-ss-7-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52zx-ss-7-logic-diffusion-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52zx-ss-7-logic-cogai-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "df88055aece687cc61d9df5f6794f34995bc46bad0b8204560e20a075780ddca",
      "skos:note": "Panel must not accept final offers deemed detrimental to covered news content or Australian consumers."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-52zx-ss-7",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "52ZX(7) Final offer arbitration",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 486,
      "values:originalText": "(7) The panel must accept one of the final offers unless the panel\nconsiders that each final offer is not in the public interest because it\nis highly likely to result in serious detriment to:\n\n(a) the provision of covered news content in Australia; or\n\n(b) Australian consumers."
    },
