    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "53 Object of this Part",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-53"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.506",
      "values:originalText": "The object of this Part is to enhance the welfare of Australians\nthrough:\n\n(a) the regulation of the Australian gas market; and\n\n(b) in particular, limitation of increases in gas prices.",
      "skos:definition": "The object of this Part is to enhance the welfare of Australians\nthrough:\n\n(a) the regulation of the Australian gas market; and\n\n(b) in particular, limitation of increases in gas prices.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a1d93705cfacf9c7dcab020e1340a4d37e85351fe93284f59516c7db103fc8c2",
      "skos:note": "Enhance the welfare of Australians through regulation of the Australian gas market and limitation of increases in gas prices."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-53",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "53 Object of this Part",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 506,
      "values:originalText": "The object of this Part is to enhance the welfare of Australians\nthrough:\n\n(a) the regulation of the Australian gas market; and\n\n(b) in particular, limitation of increases in gas prices."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Regulation is an obligation.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "53A Simplified outline",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-53a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.506",
      "values:originalText": "The regulations may prescribe rules (known as gas market codes)\nregulating conduct relating to supplying or acquiring gas.\nWithout limiting what may be included in a gas market code, a gas\nmarket code may include rules that:\n\n(a)\nregulate dealings between persons who supply or\nacquire gas, including negotiations and agreements\nbetween such persons; or\n\n(b)\ndeal with resolving disputes between persons who\nsupply or acquire gas.\nThe Minister may make orders (known as gas market emergency\nprice orders) regulating the terms (including prices) on which gas\nis supplied or acquired.\nNote:\nThe terms on which gas is supplied or acquired may also be regulated by\na gas market code.\nA person must not enter into a scheme for the purpose of avoiding\nthe application of a gas market code or a gas market emergency\nprice order.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nGas market  Part IVBB\nPreliminary  Division 1\n\nSection 53B\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nConsequences of contravening the gas market provisions include\ncivil penalties, infringement notices, warning notices and orders\nunder Part VI.\nSubdivision B—Definitions",
      "skos:definition": "The regulations may prescribe rules (known as gas market codes)\nregulating conduct relating to supplying or acquiring gas.\nWithout limiting what may be included in a gas market code, a gas\nmarket code may include rules that:\n\n(a)\nregulate dealings between persons who supply or\nacquire gas, including negotiations and agreements\nbetween such persons; or\n\n(b)\ndeal with resolving disputes between persons who\nsupply or acquire gas.\nThe Minister may make orders (known as gas market emergency\nprice orders) regulating the terms (including prices) on which gas\nis supplied or acquired.\nNote:\nThe terms on which gas is supplied or acquired may also be regulated by\na gas market code.\nA person must not enter into a scheme for the purpose of avoiding\nthe application of a gas market code or a gas market emergency\nprice order.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nGas market  Part IVBB\nPreliminary  Division 1\n\nSection 53B\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nConsequences of contravening the gas market provisions include\ncivil penalties, infringement notices, warning notices and orders\nunder Part VI.\nSubdivision B—Definitions",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53a-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "04b2c8461c4ea0b3bfd33341e14f3221f2c13beb800fa3654133b83c454a5863",
      "skos:note": "No scheme for avoiding gas market code or emergency price order"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-53a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "53A Simplified outline",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 506,
      "values:originalText": "The regulations may prescribe rules (known as gas market codes)\nregulating conduct relating to supplying or acquiring gas.\nWithout limiting what may be included in a gas market code, a gas\nmarket code may include rules that:\n\n(a)\nregulate dealings between persons who supply or\nacquire gas, including negotiations and agreements\nbetween such persons; or\n\n(b)\ndeal with resolving disputes between persons who\nsupply or acquire gas.\nThe Minister may make orders (known as gas market emergency\nprice orders) regulating the terms (including prices) on which gas\nis supplied or acquired.\nNote:\nThe terms on which gas is supplied or acquired may also be regulated by\na gas market code.\nA person must not enter into a scheme for the purpose of avoiding\nthe application of a gas market code or a gas market emergency\nprice order.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nGas market  Part IVBB\nPreliminary  Division 1\n\nSection 53B\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nConsequences of contravening the gas market provisions include\ncivil penalties, infringement notices, warning notices and orders\nunder Part VI.\nSubdivision B—Definitions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53a-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53a"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53a-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibition of scheme for avoiding gas market code or emergency price order",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "A person must not enter into a scheme...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "No scheme is allowed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "53B Definitions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-53b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.507",
      "values:originalText": "In this Part:\nagreement includes a contract.\nNote:\nFor the meaning of contract, see subsection 4(1).\nAustralia: see subsection 53E(2).\nconstitutional corporation means a corporation to which\nparagraph 51(xx) of the Constitution applies.\nconstitutional trade or commerce means any of the following:\n\n(a) trade or commerce among the States;\n\n(b) trade or commerce between Australia and places outside\nAustralia;\n\n(c) trade or commerce within a Territory, between a State and a\nTerritory, or between 2 Territories.\nexpression of interest means a non-binding expression of interest\nor invitation issued for the purpose of ascertaining whether a\nperson is interested in acquiring or supplying a gas commodity.\ngas includes gas in a liquid state.\ngas commodity means:\n\n(a) gas; or\n\n(b) goods or services relating to supplying or acquiring gas.\ngas exchange means an exchange or other trading system, platform\nor facility (including an electronic exchange, system, platform or\nfacility) on which:\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.\nPart IVBB  Gas market",
      "skos:definition": "In this Part:\nagreement includes a contract.\nNote:\nFor the meaning of contract, see subsection 4(1).\nAustralia: see subsection 53E(2).\nconstitutional corporation means a corporation to which\nparagraph 51(xx) of the Constitution applies.\nconstitutional trade or commerce means any of the following:\n\n(a) trade or commerce among the States;\n\n(b) trade or commerce between Australia and places outside\nAustralia;\n\n(c) trade or commerce within a Territory, between a State and a\nTerritory, or between 2 Territories.\nexpression of interest means a non-binding expression of interest\nor invitation issued for the purpose of ascertaining whether a\nperson is interested in acquiring or supplying a gas commodity.\ngas includes gas in a liquid state.\ngas commodity means:\n\n(a) gas; or\n\n(b) goods or services relating to supplying or acquiring gas.\ngas exchange means an exchange or other trading system, platform\nor facility (including an electronic exchange, system, platform or\nfacility) on which:\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.\nPart IVBB  Gas market",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53b-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53b-logic-descriptionlogic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53b-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "65b245488fd79c3eaf173942e8a223050f087bd91f91aea3623408705d722bf5",
      "skos:note": "Definitions for Part IVBB"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-53b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "53B Definitions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 507,
      "values:originalText": "In this Part:\nagreement includes a contract.\nNote:\nFor the meaning of contract, see subsection 4(1).\nAustralia: see subsection 53E(2).\nconstitutional corporation means a corporation to which\nparagraph 51(xx) of the Constitution applies.\nconstitutional trade or commerce means any of the following:\n\n(a) trade or commerce among the States;\n\n(b) trade or commerce between Australia and places outside\nAustralia;\n\n(c) trade or commerce within a Territory, between a State and a\nTerritory, or between 2 Territories.\nexpression of interest means a non-binding expression of interest\nor invitation issued for the purpose of ascertaining whether a\nperson is interested in acquiring or supplying a gas commodity.\ngas includes gas in a liquid state.\ngas commodity means:\n\n(a) gas; or\n\n(b) goods or services relating to supplying or acquiring gas.\ngas exchange means an exchange or other trading system, platform\nor facility (including an electronic exchange, system, platform or\nfacility) on which:\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.\nPart IVBB  Gas market"
    },
