      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.522",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A gas market code may provide for the mediation of disputes\nbetween gas market participants relating to gas market conduct,\nincluding providing for any of the following matters:\n\n(a) a process for appointing a mediator;\n\n(b) the powers or functions of a mediator;\n\n(c) a process for commencing mediation;\n\n(d) the mediation process, including rules about any of the\nfollowing matters:\n\n(i) a party giving information to another party or to a\nmediator (including on request);\n\n(ii) a mediator providing a party with an opportunity to be\nheard;\n\n(iii) terminating a mediation;\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nGas market  Part IVBB\nGas market instruments  Division 2\n\nSection 53W\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(e) the extent (if any) to which mediation is compulsory;\n\n(f) the consequences of not participating in mediation;\n\n(g) reporting;\n\n(h) generating and keeping records;\n\n(i) confidentiality;\n\n(j) the costs of mediation, including providing for:\n\n(i) determining the costs; or\n\n(ii) who is liable to pay the costs.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A gas market code may provide for the mediation of disputes\nbetween gas market participants relating to gas market conduct,\nincluding providing for any of the following matters:\n\n(a) a process for appointing a mediator;\n\n(b) the powers or functions of a mediator;\n\n(c) a process for commencing mediation;\n\n(d) the mediation process, including rules about any of the\nfollowing matters:\n\n(i) a party giving information to another party or to a\nmediator (including on request);\n\n(ii) a mediator providing a party with an opportunity to be\nheard;\n\n(iii) terminating a mediation;\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nGas market  Part IVBB\nGas market instruments  Division 2\n\nSection 53W\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(e) the extent (if any) to which mediation is compulsory;\n\n(f) the consequences of not participating in mediation;\n\n(g) reporting;\n\n(h) generating and keeping records;\n\n(i) confidentiality;\n\n(j) the costs of mediation, including providing for:\n\n(i) determining the costs; or\n\n(ii) who is liable to pay the costs.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53w"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53w-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53w-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b2f25b2532e648864ffb3873c8fed1a35ebe510ccb45c75e56ef4d91e511de47",
      "skos:note": "Provides for mediation of disputes between gas market participants relating to gas market conduct.",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-53w-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "53W(1) Mediation and arbitration",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 522,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A gas market code may provide for the mediation of disputes\nbetween gas market participants relating to gas market conduct,\nincluding providing for any of the following matters:\n\n(a) a process for appointing a mediator;\n\n(b) the powers or functions of a mediator;\n\n(c) a process for commencing mediation;\n\n(d) the mediation process, including rules about any of the\nfollowing matters:\n\n(i) a party giving information to another party or to a\nmediator (including on request);\n\n(ii) a mediator providing a party with an opportunity to be\nheard;\n\n(iii) terminating a mediation;\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nGas market  Part IVBB\nGas market instruments  Division 2\n\nSection 53W\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(e) the extent (if any) to which mediation is compulsory;\n\n(f) the consequences of not participating in mediation;\n\n(g) reporting;\n\n(h) generating and keeping records;\n\n(i) confidentiality;\n\n(j) the costs of mediation, including providing for:\n\n(i) determining the costs; or\n\n(ii) who is liable to pay the costs."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53w-ss-1-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53w-ss-1"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53w-ss-1-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Imposes an obligation on the state to provide for mediation of disputes.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53w-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "53W(2) Mediation and arbitration",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-53w-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.522",
      "values:originalText": "(2) A gas market code may provide for the arbitration (including\ncompulsory arbitration) of disputes between gas market\nparticipants relating to gas market conduct, including providing for\nany of the following matters:\n\n(a) establishing or maintaining a register of arbiters;\n\n(b) a process for appointing an arbiter;\n\n(c) the powers or functions of an arbiter;\n\n(d) a process for commencing arbitration, including rules\nrequiring a party to a dispute to take reasonable steps (such\nas mediation) to resolve a dispute before proceeding to\narbitration;\n\n(e) the arbitration process, including rules about any of the\nfollowing matters:\n\n(i) a party to a dispute giving information to another party\nor to an arbiter (including on request);\n\n(ii) an arbiter providing a party with an opportunity to be\nheard;\n\n(iii) terminating an arbitration;\n\n(f) the extent (if any) to which arbitration is compulsory;\n\n(g) the consequences of not participating in arbitration;\n\n(h) decision-making by an arbiter, including processes an arbiter\nuses in decision-making;\n\n(i) a power of an arbiter to decide that a party to a dispute must\nsupply a gas commodity;\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.\nPart IVBB  Gas market",
      "skos:definition": "(2) A gas market code may provide for the arbitration (including\ncompulsory arbitration) of disputes between gas market\nparticipants relating to gas market conduct, including providing for\nany of the following matters:\n\n(a) establishing or maintaining a register of arbiters;\n\n(b) a process for appointing an arbiter;\n\n(c) the powers or functions of an arbiter;\n\n(d) a process for commencing arbitration, including rules\nrequiring a party to a dispute to take reasonable steps (such\nas mediation) to resolve a dispute before proceeding to\narbitration;\n\n(e) the arbitration process, including rules about any of the\nfollowing matters:\n\n(i) a party to a dispute giving information to another party\nor to an arbiter (including on request);\n\n(ii) an arbiter providing a party with an opportunity to be\nheard;\n\n(iii) terminating an arbitration;\n\n(f) the extent (if any) to which arbitration is compulsory;\n\n(g) the consequences of not participating in arbitration;\n\n(h) decision-making by an arbiter, including processes an arbiter\nuses in decision-making;\n\n(i) a power of an arbiter to decide that a party to a dispute must\nsupply a gas commodity;\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.\nPart IVBB  Gas market",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53w"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53w-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53w-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5aeef46bc54e288099c56cc5127dfe1c4ad53b30ff93ae0afb8a02e734a2cac1",
      "skos:note": "Establishing or maintaining a register of arbiters."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-53w-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "53W(2) Mediation and arbitration",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 522,
      "values:originalText": "(2) A gas market code may provide for the arbitration (including\ncompulsory arbitration) of disputes between gas market\nparticipants relating to gas market conduct, including providing for\nany of the following matters:\n\n(a) establishing or maintaining a register of arbiters;\n\n(b) a process for appointing an arbiter;\n\n(c) the powers or functions of an arbiter;\n\n(d) a process for commencing arbitration, including rules\nrequiring a party to a dispute to take reasonable steps (such\nas mediation) to resolve a dispute before proceeding to\narbitration;\n\n(e) the arbitration process, including rules about any of the\nfollowing matters:\n\n(i) a party to a dispute giving information to another party\nor to an arbiter (including on request);\n\n(ii) an arbiter providing a party with an opportunity to be\nheard;\n\n(iii) terminating an arbitration;\n\n(f) the extent (if any) to which arbitration is compulsory;\n\n(g) the consequences of not participating in arbitration;\n\n(h) decision-making by an arbiter, including processes an arbiter\nuses in decision-making;\n\n(i) a power of an arbiter to decide that a party to a dispute must\nsupply a gas commodity;\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.\nPart IVBB  Gas market"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53w-ss-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53w-ss-2"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
