        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...Chapter 4\nGas market  Part IVBB\nGas market instruments  Division 2\n..."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53x-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "53X(2) Terms on which gas commodities are supplied or acquired,",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-53x-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.524",
      "values:originalText": "(2) A gas market emergency price order may include rules about the\nprice at which a gas market participant offers to supply or acquire,\nagrees to supply or acquire or supplies or acquires a gas\ncommodity, including the following:\n\n(a) rules setting a price;\n\n(b) rules setting a maximum price;\n\n(c) rules setting a minimum price;\n\n(d) rules setting a maximum and a minimum price;\n\n(e) rules requiring a price to be reasonable;\n\n(f) rules about the matters that, for the purposes of a gas market\nemergency price order, must, may or must not be taken into\naccount in determining whether a price is reasonable;\n\n(g) rules about determining a price, including matters taken into\naccount in determining a price;\n\n(h) rules about how a price is expressed.\nNote 1:\nA gas market emergency price order may confer on the Minister, the\nCommission or any other person or body the function of setting a\nprice: see section 53ZB.\nNote 2:\nRules of the kind mentioned in this subsection may:\n(a) refer to the prices of any gas commodity inside or outside\nAustralia or any published information about any market; or\n(b) require a price to be equal to the amount worked out by using a\nspecified formula or method.\n\nSee subsection 53ZE(3).",
      "skos:definition": "(2) A gas market emergency price order may include rules about the\nprice at which a gas market participant offers to supply or acquire,\nagrees to supply or acquire or supplies or acquires a gas\ncommodity, including the following:\n\n(a) rules setting a price;\n\n(b) rules setting a maximum price;\n\n(c) rules setting a minimum price;\n\n(d) rules setting a maximum and a minimum price;\n\n(e) rules requiring a price to be reasonable;\n\n(f) rules about the matters that, for the purposes of a gas market\nemergency price order, must, may or must not be taken into\naccount in determining whether a price is reasonable;\n\n(g) rules about determining a price, including matters taken into\naccount in determining a price;\n\n(h) rules about how a price is expressed.\nNote 1:\nA gas market emergency price order may confer on the Minister, the\nCommission or any other person or body the function of setting a\nprice: see section 53ZB.\nNote 2:\nRules of the kind mentioned in this subsection may:\n(a) refer to the prices of any gas commodity inside or outside\nAustralia or any published information about any market; or\n(b) require a price to be equal to the amount worked out by using a\nspecified formula or method.\n\nSee subsection 53ZE(3).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53x"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53x-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53x-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53x-ss-2-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53x-ss-2-logic-linearlogic-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "dabe67e29059bb569042b3cf2fa06c9e15953ffb9b40da7f13a43268819b11de",
      "skos:note": "Rules for setting a price in a gas market emergency price order"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-53x-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "53X(2) Terms on which gas commodities are supplied or acquired,",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 524,
      "values:originalText": "(2) A gas market emergency price order may include rules about the\nprice at which a gas market participant offers to supply or acquire,\nagrees to supply or acquire or supplies or acquires a gas\ncommodity, including the following:\n\n(a) rules setting a price;\n\n(b) rules setting a maximum price;\n\n(c) rules setting a minimum price;\n\n(d) rules setting a maximum and a minimum price;\n\n(e) rules requiring a price to be reasonable;\n\n(f) rules about the matters that, for the purposes of a gas market\nemergency price order, must, may or must not be taken into\naccount in determining whether a price is reasonable;\n\n(g) rules about determining a price, including matters taken into\naccount in determining a price;\n\n(h) rules about how a price is expressed.\nNote 1:\nA gas market emergency price order may confer on the Minister, the\nCommission or any other person or body the function of setting a\nprice: see section 53ZB.\nNote 2:\nRules of the kind mentioned in this subsection may:\n(a) refer to the prices of any gas commodity inside or outside\nAustralia or any published information about any market; or\n(b) require a price to be equal to the amount worked out by using a\nspecified formula or method.\n\nSee subsection 53ZE(3)."
    },
    {
