      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 536,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commission may give a person a notice in writing if the\nCommission reasonably believes that:\n\n(a) any of the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n(i) the person has engaged in prohibited conduct;\n\n(ii) the person is engaging in prohibited conduct; and\n\n(b) one or more other persons has suffered, or is likely to suffer,\ndetriment as a result of the prohibited conduct; and\n\n(c) it is in the public interest to issue the notice.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nGas market  Part IVBB\nCompliance with gas market instruments  Division 3\n\nSection 53ZM\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53zl-ss-1-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53zl-ss-1"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53zl-ss-1-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibition",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Notice for prohibited conduct",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Commission may give notice in writing if reasonable belief of prohibited conduct exists."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53zl-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "53ZL(2) Commission may give draft public warning notice",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-53zl-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.536",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The notice must:\n\n(a) state the day on which the notice is given; and\n\n(b) identify:\n\n(i) the person mentioned in paragraph (1)(a); and\n\n(ii) the prohibited conduct mentioned in paragraph (1)(a);\nand\n\n(c) explain the reasons why the Commission reasonably believes\nthat the requirements in paragraphs (1)(a), (b) and (c) are\nmet; and\n\n(d) state that:\n\n(i) the person may, within 21 days after being given the\nnotice, make representations to the Commission\nregarding the matters mentioned in paragraphs (1)(a),\n(b) and (c); and\n\n(ii) the Commission may issue a public warning notice\nunder section 53ZM in relation to the prohibited\nconduct after those 21 days have passed.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The notice must:\n\n(a) state the day on which the notice is given; and\n\n(b) identify:\n\n(i) the person mentioned in paragraph (1)(a); and\n\n(ii) the prohibited conduct mentioned in paragraph (1)(a);\nand\n\n(c) explain the reasons why the Commission reasonably believes\nthat the requirements in paragraphs (1)(a), (b) and (c) are\nmet; and\n\n(d) state that:\n\n(i) the person may, within 21 days after being given the\nnotice, make representations to the Commission\nregarding the matters mentioned in paragraphs (1)(a),\n(b) and (c); and\n\n(ii) the Commission may issue a public warning notice\nunder section 53ZM in relation to the prohibited\nconduct after those 21 days have passed.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53zl"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53zl-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53zl-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "273873f9b61f49ca0ece9160cebdacf57e925acc0f2b5350fa15b7bba88664d7",
      "skos:note": "The Commission must give a draft public warning notice with specific details.",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-53zl-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "53ZL(2) Commission may give draft public warning notice",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 536,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The notice must:\n\n(a) state the day on which the notice is given; and\n\n(b) identify:\n\n(i) the person mentioned in paragraph (1)(a); and\n\n(ii) the prohibited conduct mentioned in paragraph (1)(a);\nand\n\n(c) explain the reasons why the Commission reasonably believes\nthat the requirements in paragraphs (1)(a), (b) and (c) are\nmet; and\n\n(d) state that:\n\n(i) the person may, within 21 days after being given the\nnotice, make representations to the Commission\nregarding the matters mentioned in paragraphs (1)(a),\n(b) and (c); and\n\n(ii) the Commission may issue a public warning notice\nunder section 53ZM in relation to the prohibited\nconduct after those 21 days have passed."
    },
