    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53zm",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "53ZM Commission may issue public warning notice",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-53zm"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.537",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) the Commission gave a person a notice under section 53ZL\nin relation to prohibited conduct; and\n\n(b) at least 21 days have passed since the Commission gave the\nperson the notice; and\n\n(c) no more than 90 days have passed since the Commission\ngave the person the notice; and\n\n(d) the Commission reasonably believes that any of the\nfollowing conditions are satisfied:\n\n(i) the person has engaged in the prohibited conduct;\n\n(ii) the person is engaging in the prohibited conduct; and\n\n(e) the Commission reasonably believes that one or more other\npersons has suffered, or is likely to suffer, detriment as a\nresult of the prohibited conduct.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.\nPart IVBB  Gas market",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) the Commission gave a person a notice under section 53ZL\nin relation to prohibited conduct; and\n\n(b) at least 21 days have passed since the Commission gave the\nperson the notice; and\n\n(c) no more than 90 days have passed since the Commission\ngave the person the notice; and\n\n(d) the Commission reasonably believes that any of the\nfollowing conditions are satisfied:\n\n(i) the person has engaged in the prohibited conduct;\n\n(ii) the person is engaging in the prohibited conduct; and\n\n(e) the Commission reasonably believes that one or more other\npersons has suffered, or is likely to suffer, detriment as a\nresult of the prohibited conduct.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.\nPart IVBB  Gas market",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53zm-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53zm-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "580be572e3139ce51edc5287489705e8494fe7369088e3bc47aa85eda5db642f",
      "skos:note": "Commission may issue public warning notice for prohibited conduct."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-53zm",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "53ZM Commission may issue public warning notice",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 537,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) the Commission gave a person a notice under section 53ZL\nin relation to prohibited conduct; and\n\n(b) at least 21 days have passed since the Commission gave the\nperson the notice; and\n\n(c) no more than 90 days have passed since the Commission\ngave the person the notice; and\n\n(d) the Commission reasonably believes that any of the\nfollowing conditions are satisfied:\n\n(i) the person has engaged in the prohibited conduct;\n\n(ii) the person is engaging in the prohibited conduct; and\n\n(e) the Commission reasonably believes that one or more other\npersons has suffered, or is likely to suffer, detriment as a\nresult of the prohibited conduct.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.\nPart IVBB  Gas market"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53zm-norm",
