    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53zn-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "53ZN(1) Proceedings for defamation not to lie",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-53zn-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.538",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) a person engaged in conduct (the contravening conduct) that\nconstituted a contravention or a related contravention of a\ncivil penalty provision of a gas market instrument; and\n\n(b) the contravening conduct caused, or is likely to cause, a class\nof persons to suffer loss or damage; and\n\n(c) the class includes persons (non-parties) who are not, or have\nnot been, parties to a proceeding (an enforcement\nproceeding) instituted under Part VI in relation to the\ncontravening conduct;\nany court having jurisdiction in the matter may, on the application\nof the Commission, make such order or orders (other than an award\nof damages) as the court thinks appropriate against a person\nreferred to in subsection (2).\nNote:\nThe orders that the court may make include all or any of the orders set\nout in section 53ZP.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If:\n\n(a) a person engaged in conduct (the contravening conduct) that\nconstituted a contravention or a related contravention of a\ncivil penalty provision of a gas market instrument; and\n\n(b) the contravening conduct caused, or is likely to cause, a class\nof persons to suffer loss or damage; and\n\n(c) the class includes persons (non-parties) who are not, or have\nnot been, parties to a proceeding (an enforcement\nproceeding) instituted under Part VI in relation to the\ncontravening conduct;\nany court having jurisdiction in the matter may, on the application\nof the Commission, make such order or orders (other than an award\nof damages) as the court thinks appropriate against a person\nreferred to in subsection (2).\nNote:\nThe orders that the court may make include all or any of the orders set\nout in section 53ZP.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53zn"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53zn-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53zn-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53zn-ss-1-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53zn-ss-1-logic-deontic-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d5159ceefcde6c5eb68c39fa9440942a6c769cc4cc4975591d8cbd0f424c7470",
      "skos:note": "Court may make orders against a person referred to in subsection (2) if the contravening conduct caused loss or damage to a class of persons. No defamation action against Commonwealth, Commission, or staff in relation to notice issuance."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-53zn-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "53ZN(1) Proceedings for defamation not to lie",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 538,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) a person engaged in conduct (the contravening conduct) that\nconstituted a contravention or a related contravention of a\ncivil penalty provision of a gas market instrument; and\n\n(b) the contravening conduct caused, or is likely to cause, a class\nof persons to suffer loss or damage; and\n\n(c) the class includes persons (non-parties) who are not, or have\nnot been, parties to a proceeding (an enforcement\nproceeding) instituted under Part VI in relation to the\ncontravening conduct;\nany court having jurisdiction in the matter may, on the application\nof the Commission, make such order or orders (other than an award\nof damages) as the court thinks appropriate against a person\nreferred to in subsection (2).\nNote:\nThe orders that the court may make include all or any of the orders set\nout in section 53ZP."
    },
