      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53zp",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "53ZP Kinds of orders that may be made to redress loss or damage",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-53zp"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.541",
      "values:originalText": "suffered by non-parties etc.\n\nWithout limiting subsection 53ZO(1), the orders that a court may\nmake under that subsection against a person (the respondent)\ninclude all or any of the following:\n\n(a) an order declaring the whole or any part of a contract made\nbetween the respondent and a non-party referred to in that\nsubsection, or a collateral arrangement relating to such a\ncontract:\n\n(i) to be void; and\n\n(ii) if the court thinks fit—to have been void ab initio or\nvoid at all times on and after such date as is specified in\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.\nPart IVBB  Gas market",
      "skos:definition": "suffered by non-parties etc.\n\nWithout limiting subsection 53ZO(1), the orders that a court may\nmake under that subsection against a person (the respondent)\ninclude all or any of the following:\n\n(a) an order declaring the whole or any part of a contract made\nbetween the respondent and a non-party referred to in that\nsubsection, or a collateral arrangement relating to such a\ncontract:\n\n(i) to be void; and\n\n(ii) if the court thinks fit—to have been void ab initio or\nvoid at all times on and after such date as is specified in\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.\nPart IVBB  Gas market",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53zp-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "eca3e84685fd1891d174531a1ec065736c38c11e3173763650299ba82b67339d",
      "skos:note": "Orders that may be made to redress loss or damage suffered by non-parties."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-53zp",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "53ZP Kinds of orders that may be made to redress loss or damage",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 541,
      "values:originalText": "suffered by non-parties etc.\n\nWithout limiting subsection 53ZO(1), the orders that a court may\nmake under that subsection against a person (the respondent)\ninclude all or any of the following:\n\n(a) an order declaring the whole or any part of a contract made\nbetween the respondent and a non-party referred to in that\nsubsection, or a collateral arrangement relating to such a\ncontract:\n\n(i) to be void; and\n\n(ii) if the court thinks fit—to have been void ab initio or\nvoid at all times on and after such date as is specified in\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.\nPart IVBB  Gas market"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53zp-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53zp"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53zq",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "53ZQ Schemes for avoidance purposes",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-53zq"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.542",
      "values:originalText": "General prohibition\n\n(1) A person contravenes this subsection if:\n\n(a) the person, either alone or with others, engages in any of the\nfollowing conduct:\n\n(i) enters into a scheme;\n\n(ii) begins to carry out a scheme;\n\n(iii) carries out a scheme; and\n\n(b) having regard to any matters as required under\nsubsection 53ZR(1), it would be reasonable to conclude that\nthe purpose of the person engaging in that conduct was to\navoid the application of a civil penalty provision of a gas\nmarket instrument.\nNote 1:\nFor enforcement, see section 53ZK and Part VI.\nNote 2:\nSee section 4F (references to purpose).\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nGas market  Part IVBB\nCompliance with gas market instruments  Division 3\n\nSection 53ZQ\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nConstitutional corporations\n\n(2) A constitutional corporation contravenes this subsection if:\n\n(a) the corporation, either alone or with other persons, engages\nin any of the following conduct:\n\n(i) enters into a scheme;\n\n(ii) begins to carry out a scheme;\n\n(iii) carries out a scheme; and\n\n(b) having regard to any matters as required under\nsubsection 53ZR(1), it would be reasonable to conclude that\nthe purpose of the corporation engaging in that conduct was\nto avoid the application of a civil penalty provision of a gas\nmarket instrument.\nNote:\nFor enforcement, see section 53ZK and Part VI.\nConstitutional trade and commerce\n\n(3) A person contravenes this subsection if:\n\n(a) in the course of constitutional trade or commerce, the person,\neither alone or with others, engages in any of the following\nconduct:\n\n(i) enters into a scheme;\n\n(ii) begins to carry out a scheme;\n\n(iii) carries out a scheme; and\n\n(b) having regard to any matters as required under\nsubsection 53ZR(1), it would be reasonable to conclude that\nthe purpose of the person engaging in that conduct was to\navoid the application of a civil penalty provision of a gas\nmarket instrument.\nNote:\nFor enforcement, see section 53ZK and Part VI.\nProhibitions independent of each other\n\n(4) To avoid doubt, subsections (1), (2) and (3) are independent from\nand do not limit each other.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.\nPart IVBB  Gas market",
      "skos:definition": "General prohibition\n\n(1) A person contravenes this subsection if:\n\n(a) the person, either alone or with others, engages in any of the\nfollowing conduct:\n\n(i) enters into a scheme;\n\n(ii) begins to carry out a scheme;\n\n(iii) carries out a scheme; and\n\n(b) having regard to any matters as required under\nsubsection 53ZR(1), it would be reasonable to conclude that\nthe purpose of the person engaging in that conduct was to\navoid the application of a civil penalty provision of a gas\nmarket instrument.\nNote 1:\nFor enforcement, see section 53ZK and Part VI.\nNote 2:\nSee section 4F (references to purpose).\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nGas market  Part IVBB\nCompliance with gas market instruments  Division 3\n\nSection 53ZQ\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nConstitutional corporations\n\n(2) A constitutional corporation contravenes this subsection if:\n\n(a) the corporation, either alone or with other persons, engages\nin any of the following conduct:\n\n(i) enters into a scheme;\n\n(ii) begins to carry out a scheme;\n\n(iii) carries out a scheme; and\n\n(b) having regard to any matters as required under\nsubsection 53ZR(1), it would be reasonable to conclude that\nthe purpose of the corporation engaging in that conduct was\nto avoid the application of a civil penalty provision of a gas\nmarket instrument.\nNote:\nFor enforcement, see section 53ZK and Part VI.\nConstitutional trade and commerce\n\n(3) A person contravenes this subsection if:\n\n(a) in the course of constitutional trade or commerce, the person,\neither alone or with others, engages in any of the following\nconduct:\n\n(i) enters into a scheme;\n\n(ii) begins to carry out a scheme;\n\n(iii) carries out a scheme; and\n\n(b) having regard to any matters as required under\nsubsection 53ZR(1), it would be reasonable to conclude that\nthe purpose of the person engaging in that conduct was to\navoid the application of a civil penalty provision of a gas\nmarket instrument.\nNote:",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53zq-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53zq-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53zq-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53zq-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3b7266a5d1ce7c131b1cd2dd7234e516803b75b32ef8f007e8d505515e7948a4"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-53zq",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "53ZQ Schemes for avoidance purposes",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 542,
      "values:originalText": "General prohibition\n\n(1) A person contravenes this subsection if:\n\n(a) the person, either alone or with others, engages in any of the\nfollowing conduct:\n\n(i) enters into a scheme;\n\n(ii) begins to carry out a scheme;\n\n(iii) carries out a scheme; and\n\n(b) having regard to any matters as required under\nsubsection 53ZR(1), it would be reasonable to conclude that\nthe purpose of the person engaging in that conduct was to\navoid the application of a civil penalty provision of a gas\nmarket instrument.\nNote 1:\nFor enforcement, see section 53ZK and Part VI.\nNote 2:\nSee section 4F (references to purpose).\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nGas market  Part IVBB\nCompliance with gas market instruments  Division 3\n\nSection 53ZQ\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nConstitutional corporations\n\n(2) A constitutional corporation contravenes this subsection if:\n\n(a) the corporation, either alone or with other persons, engages\nin any of the following conduct:\n\n(i) enters into a scheme;\n\n(ii) begins to carry out a scheme;\n\n(iii) carries out a scheme; and\n\n(b) having regard to any matters as required under\nsubsection 53ZR(1), it would be reasonable to conclude that\nthe purpose of the corporation engaging in that conduct was\nto avoid the application of a civil penalty provision of a gas\nmarket instrument.\nNote:\nFor enforcement, see section 53ZK and Part VI.\nConstitutional trade and commerce\n\n(3) A person contravenes this subsection if:\n\n(a) in the course of constitutional trade or commerce, the person,\neither alone or with others, engages in any of the following\nconduct:\n\n(i) enters into a scheme;\n\n(ii) begins to carry out a scheme;\n\n(iii) carries out a scheme; and\n\n(b) having regard to any matters as required under\nsubsection 53ZR(1), it would be reasonable to conclude that\nthe purpose of the person engaging in that conduct was to\navoid the application of a civil penalty provision of a gas\nmarket instrument.\nNote:\nFor enforcement, see section 53ZK and Part VI.\nProhibitions independent of each other\n\n(4) To avoid doubt, subsections (1), (2) and (3) are independent from\nand do not limit each other.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.\nPart IVBB  Gas market"
    },
