    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53zr",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "53ZR Whether it is reasonable to draw conclusion as to purpose",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-53zr"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.544",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Regard must be had to any matters prescribed by the regulations\nfor the purposes of this subsection in determining, for the purposes\nof section 53ZQ, whether it would be reasonable to conclude that\nthe purpose of a person entering into or carrying out (to any extent)\na scheme was to avoid the application of a civil penalty provision\nof a gas market instrument.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not limit the matters to which regard may be\nhad in making a determination described in that subsection.\n53ZS  This Subdivision does not limit Division 2\n\nThis Subdivision does not limit a provision of Division 2.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nGas market  Part IVBB\nInvestigation powers  Division 4\n\nSection 53ZT\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Regard must be had to any matters prescribed by the regulations\nfor the purposes of this subsection in determining, for the purposes\nof section 53ZQ, whether it would be reasonable to conclude that\nthe purpose of a person entering into or carrying out (to any extent)\na scheme was to avoid the application of a civil penalty provision\nof a gas market instrument.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not limit the matters to which regard may be\nhad in making a determination described in that subsection.\n53ZS  This Subdivision does not limit Division 2\n\nThis Subdivision does not limit a provision of Division 2.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nGas market  Part IVBB\nInvestigation powers  Division 4\n\nSection 53ZT\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53zr-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53zr-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "014a102d7f27428e84b2a6ae469a4bf8ca4723d1dd6bcac9d07eb07b2cafe651"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-53zr",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "53ZR Whether it is reasonable to draw conclusion as to purpose",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 544,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Regard must be had to any matters prescribed by the regulations\nfor the purposes of this subsection in determining, for the purposes\nof section 53ZQ, whether it would be reasonable to conclude that\nthe purpose of a person entering into or carrying out (to any extent)\na scheme was to avoid the application of a civil penalty provision\nof a gas market instrument.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not limit the matters to which regard may be\nhad in making a determination described in that subsection.\n53ZS  This Subdivision does not limit Division 2\n\nThis Subdivision does not limit a provision of Division 2.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nGas market  Part IVBB\nInvestigation powers  Division 4\n\nSection 53ZT\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026"
    },
