        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53zz-ss-2-logic-deontic-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "03368f274183cfd4d923278e8a5ef98fba438023fe5f9c4f5493a7531bfe9640",
      "skos:note": "Excludes or limits the operation of a law of a State or Territory Legislation Act 2003 override Prevents acquisition of property without just terms."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-53zz-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "53ZZ(2) Concurrent operation of State and Territory laws",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 548,
      "values:originalText": "(2) Section 6 (about the application of this Act to persons who are not\ncorporations) does not apply in relation to the gas market\nprovisions.\n53ZZB  Constitution—acquisition of property\n\nThe gas market provisions have no effect to the extent (if any) to\nwhich their operation would result in the acquisition of property\n(within the meaning of paragraph 51(xxxi) of the Constitution)\notherwise than on just terms (within the meaning of that\nparagraph).\n53ZZC  Regulations referring to other instruments"
    },
